cw_polite_basics	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:05.440\nHello everyone, welcome to today's Dutch lesson!\n\n2\n00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:11.140\nToday we are going to learn essential polite response words in Dutch.\n\n3\n00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:16.221\nThese short words will help you respond politely in everyday conversations.\n\n4\n00:00:16.241 --> 00:00:23.501\nWe will cover words like yes, no, please, thank you, and excuse me.\n\n5\n00:00:23.621 --> 00:00:27.961\nListen carefully to the pronunciation and practice along with me.\n\n6\n00:00:28.101 --> 00:00:31.301\nLaten we samen beginnen!\n\n7\n00:00:31.361 --> 00:00:36.301\nOur first word is JA, which means YES.\n\n8\n00:00:36.361 --> 00:00:39.921\nJa, ik wil koffie drinken.\n\n9\n00:00:40.001 --> 00:00:43.462\nJa, dat is heel goed.\n\n10\n00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:48.742\nOur second word is NEE, which means NO.\n\n11\n00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:52.482\nNee, ik drink geen thee.\n\n12\n00:00:52.522 --> 00:00:55.662\nNee, dat wil ik niet.\n\n13\n00:00:55.702 --> 00:01:00.462\nNext, we have OKÉ, which means OKAY.\n\n14\n00:01:00.602 --> 00:01:03.902\nOké, dat is helemaal prima.\n\n15\n00:01:03.962 --> 00:01:07.882\nOké, wij gaan nu beginnen.\n\n16\n00:01:07.922 --> 00:01:15.083\nNow let's learn GOED, which means GOOD or WELL.\n\n17\n00:01:15.123 --> 00:01:20.163\nHet gaat heel goed vandaag.\n\n18\n00:01:20.203 --> 00:01:24.363\nDat is een goed idee.\n\n19\n00:01:24.403 --> 00:01:33.823\nNext is ALSJEBLIEFT, which means PLEASE or HERE YOU GO when speaking informally.\n\n20\n00:01:33.883 --> 00:01:37.964\nEen kopje koffie, alsjeblieft.\n\n21\n00:01:38.024 --> 00:01:42.384\nHier is jouw water, alsjeblieft.\n\n22\n00:01:42.424 --> 00:01:49.024\nTo answer, we say DANK JE, which means THANK YOU.\n\n23\n00:01:49.064 --> 00:01:52.604\nDank je voor jouw hulp.\n\n24\n00:01:52.664 --> 00:01:56.384\nDank je wel voor alles.\n\n25\n00:01:56.464 --> 00:02:04.645\nIn formal situations, we use ALSTUBLIEFT for PLEASE or HERE YOU GO.\n\n26\n00:02:04.745 --> 00:02:09.025\nEen moment geduld, alstublieft.\n\n27\n00:02:09.105 --> 00:02:12.405\nAlstublieft, uw sleutel is hier.\n\n28\n00:02:12.485 --> 00:02:18.145\nThe formal way to say THANK YOU is DANK U.\n\n29\n00:02:18.345 --> 00:02:20.985\nDank u wel, meneer.\n\n30\n00:02:21.025 --> 00:02:23.765\nDank u voor de informatie.\n\n31\n00:02:23.925 --> 00:02:30.886\nNext, we have GRAAG, which means GLADLY or WITH PLEASURE.\n\n32\n00:02:30.966 --> 00:02:34.186\nIk help jou heel graag.\n\n33\n00:02:34.206 --> 00:02:37.266\nJa, heel graag een koffie.\n\n34\n00:02:37.306 --> 00:02:44.326\nTo get someone's attention politely, use PARDON, which means EXCUSE ME.\n\n35\n00:02:44.366 --> 00:02:47.386\nPardon, waar is het station?\n\n36\n00:02:47.426 --> 00:02:50.126\nPardon, ik zoek de winkel.\n\n37\n00:02:50.166 --> 00:02:55.546\nTo apologize, use SORRY, which means SORRY.\n\n38\n00:02:55.706 --> 00:02:58.327\nSorry, ik ben te laat.\n\n39\n00:02:58.407 --> 00:03:01.127\nSorry, dat is mijn fout.\n\n40\n00:03:01.207 --> 00:03:08.387\nA slightly more sincere apology is HET SPIJT ME, which means I AM SORRY.\n\n41\n00:03:08.447 --> 00:03:12.467\nHet spijt me heel erg.\n\n42\n00:03:12.507 --> 00:03:16.967\nHet spijt me, ik weet het niet.\n\n43\n00:03:17.007 --> 00:03:25.128\nNow let's look at basic greetings. First, HALLO, which means HELLO.\n\n44\n00:03:25.168 --> 00:03:29.388\nHallo, hoe gaat het vandaag?\n\n45\n00:03:29.448 --> 00:03:33.448\nHallo, fijn je te zien.\n\n46\n00:03:33.488 --> 00:03:39.708\nNext is DAG, which can mean HELLO or BYE.\n\n47\n00:03:39.748 --> 00:03:43.588\nDag, ik ga nu weg.\n\n48\n00:03:43.628 --> 00:03:48.048\nDag, ik wens jou een fijne dag!\n\n49\n00:03:48.128 --> 00:03:53.429\nAnd finally, TOT ZIENS, which means GOODBYE.\n\n50\n00:03:53.469 --> 00:03:57.429\nTot ziens en fijne dag!\n\n51\n00:03:57.469 --> 00:04:01.529\nTot ziens, tot de volgende keer!\n\n52\n00:04:01.569 --> 00:04:08.149\nGreat job today! Let's do a quick spoken recap of the main words.\n\n53\n00:04:08.209 --> 00:04:13.189\nVandaag leren we: ja, nee, oké.\n\n54\n00:04:13.289 --> 00:04:22.850\nEn ook: alsjeblieft, graag, pardon, tot ziens.\n\n55\n00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:28.790\nKeep practicing these essential polite response words every day!\n\n56\n00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:30.210\nSee you in the next Dutch lesson!\n
cw_polite_basics	en	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:05.440\nHello everyone, welcome to today's Dutch lesson!\n\n2\n00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:11.140\nToday we are going to learn essential polite response words in Dutch.\n\n3\n00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:16.221\nThese short words will help you respond politely in everyday conversations.\n\n4\n00:00:16.241 --> 00:00:23.501\nWe will cover words like yes, no, please, thank you, and excuse me.\n\n5\n00:00:23.621 --> 00:00:27.961\nListen carefully to the pronunciation and practice along with me.\n\n6\n00:00:28.101 --> 00:00:31.301\nLet's start together!\n\n7\n00:00:31.361 --> 00:00:36.301\nOur first word is JA, which means YES.\n\n8\n00:00:36.361 --> 00:00:39.921\nYes, I want to drink coffee.\n\n9\n00:00:40.001 --> 00:00:43.462\nYes, that is very good.\n\n10\n00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:48.742\nOur second word is NEE, which means NO.\n\n11\n00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:52.482\nNo, I do not drink tea.\n\n12\n00:00:52.522 --> 00:00:55.662\nNo, I do not want that.\n\n13\n00:00:55.702 --> 00:01:00.462\nNext, we have OKÉ, which means OKAY.\n\n14\n00:01:00.602 --> 00:01:03.902\nOkay, that is completely fine.\n\n15\n00:01:03.962 --> 00:01:07.882\nOkay, we are going to start now.\n\n16\n00:01:07.922 --> 00:01:15.083\nNow let's learn GOED, which means GOOD or WELL.\n\n17\n00:01:15.123 --> 00:01:20.163\nIt goes very well today.\n\n18\n00:01:20.203 --> 00:01:24.363\nThat is a good idea.\n\n19\n00:01:24.403 --> 00:01:33.823\nNext is ALSJEBLIEFT, which means PLEASE or HERE YOU GO when speaking informally.\n\n20\n00:01:33.883 --> 00:01:37.964\nA cup of coffee, please.\n\n21\n00:01:38.024 --> 00:01:42.384\nHere is your water, here you go.\n\n22\n00:01:42.424 --> 00:01:49.024\nTo answer, we say DANK JE, which means THANK YOU.\n\n23\n00:01:49.064 --> 00:01:52.604\nThank you for your help.\n\n24\n00:01:52.664 --> 00:01:56.384\nThank you very much for everything.\n\n25\n00:01:56.464 --> 00:02:04.645\nIn formal situations, we use ALSTUBLIEFT for PLEASE or HERE YOU GO.\n\n26\n00:02:04.745 --> 00:02:09.025\nA moment of patience, please.\n\n27\n00:02:09.105 --> 00:02:12.405\nHere you go, your key is here.\n\n28\n00:02:12.485 --> 00:02:18.145\nThe formal way to say THANK YOU is DANK U.\n\n29\n00:02:18.345 --> 00:02:20.985\nThank you very much, sir.\n\n30\n00:02:21.025 --> 00:02:23.765\nThank you for the information.\n\n31\n00:02:23.925 --> 00:02:30.886\nNext, we have GRAAG, which means GLADLY or WITH PLEASURE.\n\n32\n00:02:30.966 --> 00:02:34.186\nI help you very gladly.\n\n33\n00:02:34.206 --> 00:02:37.266\nYes, gladly a coffee.\n\n34\n00:02:37.306 --> 00:02:44.326\nTo get someone's attention politely, use PARDON, which means EXCUSE ME.\n\n35\n00:02:44.366 --> 00:02:47.386\nExcuse me, where is the station?\n\n36\n00:02:47.426 --> 00:02:50.126\nExcuse me, I am looking for the store.\n\n37\n00:02:50.166 --> 00:02:55.546\nTo apologize, use SORRY, which means SORRY.\n\n38\n00:02:55.706 --> 00:02:58.327\nSorry, I am late.\n\n39\n00:02:58.407 --> 00:03:01.127\nSorry, that is my mistake.\n\n40\n00:03:01.207 --> 00:03:08.387\nA slightly more sincere apology is HET SPIJT ME, which means I AM SORRY.\n\n41\n00:03:08.447 --> 00:03:12.467\nI am very sorry.\n\n42\n00:03:12.507 --> 00:03:16.967\nI am sorry, I do not know.\n\n43\n00:03:17.007 --> 00:03:25.128\nNow let's look at basic greetings. First, HALLO, which means HELLO.\n\n44\n00:03:25.168 --> 00:03:29.388\nHello, how are you today?\n\n45\n00:03:29.448 --> 00:03:33.448\nHello, nice to see you.\n\n46\n00:03:33.488 --> 00:03:39.708\nNext is DAG, which can mean HELLO or BYE.\n\n47\n00:03:39.748 --> 00:03:43.588\nBye, I am leaving now.\n\n48\n00:03:43.628 --> 00:03:48.048\nBye, I wish you a nice day!\n\n49\n00:03:48.128 --> 00:03:53.429\nAnd finally, TOT ZIENS, which means GOODBYE.\n\n50\n00:03:53.469 --> 00:03:57.429\nGoodbye and have a nice day!\n\n51\n00:03:57.469 --> 00:04:01.529\nGoodbye, until next time!\n\n52\n00:04:01.569 --> 00:04:08.149\nGreat job today! Let's do a quick spoken recap of the main words.\n\n53\n00:04:08.209 --> 00:04:13.189\nToday we learn: yes, no, okay.\n\n54\n00:04:13.289 --> 00:04:22.850\nAnd also: please, gladly, excuse me, goodbye.\n\n55\n00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:28.790\nKeep practicing these essential polite response words every day!\n\n56\n00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:30.210\nSee you in the next Dutch lesson!\n
cw_professions_basic	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:07.240\nHello everyone! Welcome to today's Dutch vocabulary lesson.\n\n2\n00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:12.081\nToday, we are going to learn common professions in Dutch.\n\n3\n00:00:12.141 --> 00:00:17.001\nLearning names of jobs will help you talk about work and daily life.\n\n4\n00:00:17.061 --> 00:00:19.001\nAre you ready to begin?\n\n5\n00:00:19.201 --> 00:00:22.921\nLaten we beginnen!\n\n6\n00:00:23.001 --> 00:00:24.622\nLet's begin!\n\n7\n00:00:24.682 --> 00:00:31.202\nOur first profession is teacher, which in Dutch is leraar.\n\n8\n00:00:31.262 --> 00:00:35.162\nHij is een leraar.\n\n9\n00:00:35.202 --> 00:00:37.702\nHe is a teacher.\n\n10\n00:00:37.742 --> 00:00:43.263\nDe leraar helpt de kinderen.\n\n11\n00:00:43.283 --> 00:00:46.343\nThe teacher helps the children.\n\n12\n00:00:46.383 --> 00:00:52.083\nNext, we have doctor, which is dokter in Dutch.\n\n13\n00:00:52.163 --> 00:00:57.444\nZij is een dokter.\n\n14\n00:00:57.524 --> 00:01:00.324\nShe is a doctor.\n\n15\n00:01:00.364 --> 00:01:09.504\nDe dokter werkt in het ziekenhuis.\n\n16\n00:01:09.944 --> 00:01:14.885\nThe doctor works in the hospital.\n\n17\n00:01:14.965 --> 00:01:21.225\nOur third word is cook, which is kok in Dutch.\n\n18\n00:01:21.305 --> 00:01:25.565\nHij is een goede kok.\n\n19\n00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:29.046\nHe is a good cook.\n\n20\n00:01:29.086 --> 00:01:33.926\nDe kok maakt lekker eten.\n\n21\n00:01:33.966 --> 00:01:38.106\nThe cook makes delicious food.\n\n22\n00:01:38.166 --> 00:01:45.027\nNext is police officer, called politieagent in Dutch.\n\n23\n00:01:45.107 --> 00:01:50.327\nZij is een vriendelijke politieagent.\n\n24\n00:01:50.407 --> 00:01:54.467\nShe is a friendly police officer.\n\n25\n00:01:54.507 --> 00:02:00.248\nDe politieagent helpt mensen op straat.\n\n26\n00:02:00.268 --> 00:02:04.928\nThe police officer helps people on the street.\n\n27\n00:02:04.948 --> 00:02:11.208\nNow, let's learn nurse, which is verpleegkundige.\n\n28\n00:02:11.268 --> 00:02:15.669\nIk ben een verpleegkundige.\n\n29\n00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:17.409\nI am a nurse.\n\n30\n00:02:17.449 --> 00:02:21.609\nDe verpleegkundige zorgt voor zieke mensen.\n\n31\n00:02:21.649 --> 00:02:24.389\nThe nurse takes care of sick people.\n\n32\n00:02:24.429 --> 00:02:29.630\nOur next profession is engineer, which is ingenieur in Dutch.\n\n33\n00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:32.570\nHij is een slimme ingenieur.\n\n34\n00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:35.170\nHe is a smart engineer.\n\n35\n00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:38.890\nDe ingenieur ontwerpt een mooie brug.\n\n36\n00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:42.170\nThe engineer designs a beautiful bridge.\n\n37\n00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:45.511\nNext, we have baker, which is bakker.\n\n38\n00:02:45.571 --> 00:02:47.991\nZij is een vriendelijke bakker.\n\n39\n00:02:48.071 --> 00:02:50.411\nShe is a friendly baker.\n\n40\n00:02:50.451 --> 00:02:53.491\nDe bakker bakt elke dag brood.\n\n41\n00:02:53.511 --> 00:02:56.171\nThe baker bakes bread every day.\n\n42\n00:02:56.231 --> 00:03:00.552\nOur eighth word is driver, which is chauffeur in Dutch.\n\n43\n00:03:00.612 --> 00:03:02.892\nHij is een fijne chauffeur.\n\n44\n00:03:02.932 --> 00:03:05.792\nHe is a nice driver.\n\n45\n00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:10.532\nDe chauffeur rijdt met de bus.\n\n46\n00:03:10.572 --> 00:03:14.893\nThe driver drives the bus.\n\n47\n00:03:14.953 --> 00:03:21.813\nNow let's learn salesperson, which is verkoper.\n\n48\n00:03:21.893 --> 00:03:26.273\nZij is een actieve verkoper.\n\n49\n00:03:26.373 --> 00:03:30.414\nShe is an active salesperson.\n\n50\n00:03:30.454 --> 00:03:35.694\nDe verkoper werkt in een winkel.\n\n51\n00:03:35.714 --> 00:03:40.154\nThe salesperson works in a shop.\n\n52\n00:03:40.194 --> 00:03:47.575\nAnd finally, student, which is student in Dutch.\n\n53\n00:03:47.635 --> 00:03:52.135\nIk ben een ijverige student.\n\n54\n00:03:52.355 --> 00:03:55.795\nI am a diligent student.\n\n55\n00:03:55.835 --> 00:04:01.616\nDe student studeert aan de school.\n\n56\n00:04:01.636 --> 00:04:06.196\nThe student studies at the school.\n\n57\n00:04:06.236 --> 00:04:10.996\nGreat job today! Let's do a quick recap of the words we learned.\n\n58\n00:04:11.036 --> 00:04:19.897\nVandaag leerden we: leraar, dokter, kok.\n\n59\n00:04:19.937 --> 00:04:27.637\nToday we learned: teacher, doctor, cook.\n\n60\n00:04:27.697 --> 00:04:36.697\nOok politieagent, verpleegkundige en ingenieur.\n\n61\n00:04:37.858 --> 00:04:45.498\nAlso police officer, nurse, and engineer.\n\n62\n00:04:45.558 --> 00:04:54.799\nEn ten slotte bakker, chauffeur en verkoper.\n\n63\n00:04:54.919 --> 00:05:02.579\nAnd finally baker, driver, and salesperson.\n\n64\n00:05:02.619 --> 00:05:06.760\nKeep practicing these profession names!\n\n65\n00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:08.320\nBedankt voor het kijken en tot ziens!\n\n66\n00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:10.440\nThanks for watching and see you soon!\n
