now.\n\n32\n00:02:31.505 --> 00:02:36.566\nHe is tired after work.\n\n33\n00:02:36.586 --> 00:02:40.706\nHe is tired after work.\n\n34\n00:02:40.806 --> 00:02:46.586\nOur sixth word is for sick: ziek.\n\n35\n00:02:46.606 --> 00:02:51.546\nMy sister is sick today.\n\n36\n00:02:51.586 --> 00:02:55.326\nMy sister is sick today.\n\n37\n00:02:55.406 --> 00:02:59.806\nI feel very sick.\n\n38\n00:03:00.006 --> 00:03:03.647\nI feel very sick.\n\n39\n00:03:03.667 --> 00:03:10.207\nNext, we have happy or fortunate: gelukkig.\n\n40\n00:03:10.247 --> 00:03:15.367\nWe are very happy together.\n\n41\n00:03:15.387 --> 00:03:19.287\nWe are very happy together.\n\n42\n00:03:19.347 --> 00:03:23.667\nShe is a happy person.\n\n43\n00:03:23.727 --> 00:03:27.267\nShe is a happy person.\n\n44\n00:03:27.307 --> 00:03:33.448\nFinally, our word for nervous is: nerveus.\n\n45\n00:03:33.548 --> 00:03:37.908\nI am nervous for the test.\n\n46\n00:03:38.088 --> 00:03:41.208\nI am nervous for the test.\n\n47\n00:03:41.268 --> 00:03:46.148\nWhy are you so nervous?\n\n48\n00:03:46.188 --> 00:03:50.308\nWhy are you so nervous?\n\n49\n00:03:50.348 --> 00:03:54.668\nNow let's do a recap of all the words!\n\n50\n00:03:54.708 --> 00:04:06.569\nToday we learned: happy, sad, angry, afraid.\n\n51\n00:04:06.609 --> 00:04:15.889\nToday we learned: happy, sad, angry, afraid.\n\n52\n00:04:15.969 --> 00:04:26.610\nAnd also: tired, sick, happy, nervous.\n\n53\n00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:35.330\nAnd also: tired, sick, happy, nervous.\n\n54\n00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:38.170\nExcellent work today! Keep practicing!\n
cw_health_words	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:06.500\nHello everyone, welcome back to Dutch with Gemini!\n\n2\n00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:11.580\nToday we are learning essential health words in Dutch.\n\n3\n00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:17.481\nThese words will help you explain how you feel or ask for help.\n\n4\n00:00:17.701 --> 00:00:20.581\nLaten we beginnen!\n\n5\n00:00:20.641 --> 00:00:26.161\nOur first word is ZIEK, which means sick.\n\n6\n00:00:26.241 --> 00:00:30.261\nIk ben vandaag een beetje ziek.\n\n7\n00:00:30.281 --> 00:00:34.182\nMijn broer is ook ziek.\n\n8\n00:00:34.222 --> 00:00:39.582\nNext, we have PIJN, which means pain.\n\n9\n00:00:39.682 --> 00:00:43.242\nIk heb hier veel pijn.\n\n10\n00:00:43.302 --> 00:00:46.862\nWaar doet het precies pijn?\n\n11\n00:00:46.922 --> 00:00:53.382\nNow let's look at body parts. HOOFD means head.\n\n12\n00:00:53.402 --> 00:00:57.403\nMijn hoofd doet een beetje pijn.\n\n13\n00:00:57.483 --> 00:01:01.543\nIk heb pijn in mijn hoofd.\n\n14\n00:01:01.583 --> 00:01:05.883\nThe word for belly or stomach is BUIK.\n\n15\n00:01:05.943 --> 00:01:10.703\nHet kind heeft pijn in de buik.\n\n16\n00:01:10.723 --> 00:01:15.524\nMijn buik is heel erg gevoelig.\n\n17\n00:01:15.564 --> 00:01:19.904\nThe word for throat is KEEL.\n\n18\n00:01:19.984 --> 00:01:23.824\nIk heb last van mijn keel.\n\n19\n00:01:23.864 --> 00:01:27.884\nDrink warme thee voor je keel.\n\n20\n00:01:27.904 --> 00:01:33.984\nWhen you are sick, you see a DOKTER, which means doctor.\n\n21\n00:01:34.084 --> 00:01:38.045\nIk ga morgen naar de dokter.\n\n22\n00:01:38.105 --> 00:01:42.425\nDe dokter helpt de zieke mensen.\n\n23\n00:01:42.465 --> 00:01:47.465\nThe word for medicine is MEDICIJN.\n\n24\n00:01:47.505 --> 00:01:51.845\nNeem dit medicijn met water in.\n\n25\n00:01:51.885 --> 00:01:56.145\nDit medicijn werkt heel snel.\n\n26\n00:01:56.165 --> 00:02:01.946\nTo heal, you need RUST, which means rest.\n\n27\n00:02:01.986 --> 00:02:05.146\nJe hebt nu veel rust nodig.\n\n28\n00:02:05.166 --> 00:02:08.066\nNeem een dagje rust.\n\n29\n00:02:08.106 --> 00:02:14.226\nWhen you recover, you feel BETER, which means better.\n\n30\n00:02:14.306 --> 00:02:17.426\nIk voel mij al veel beter.\n\n31\n00:02:17.506 --> 00:02:21.187\nBeterschap en word snel beter!\n\n32\n00:02:21.287 --> 00:02:27.087\nAnother useful word is KOORTS, which means fever.\n\n33\n00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:30.507\nHij heeft vandaag hoge koorts.\n\n34\n00:02:30.547 --> 00:02:32.767\nHeb je ook koorts?\n\n35\n00:02:32.827 --> 00:02:38.487\nYou buy your medicine at the APOTHEEK, or pharmacy.\n\n36\n00:02:38.567 --> 00:02:42.128\nIk koop medicijnen bij de apotheek.\n\n37\n00:02:42.188 --> 00:02:45.608\nWaar is de dichtstbijzijnde apotheek?\n\n38\n00:02:45.668 --> 00:02:52.068\nFinally, don't forget WATER, which means water.\n\n39\n00:02:52.128 --> 00:02:55.248\nDrink veel water als je ziek bent.\n\n40\n00:02:55.288 --> 00:02:58.948\nEen glas koud water helpt altijd.\n\n41\n00:02:58.988 --> 00:03:01.749\nYou did a fantastic job today!\n\n42\n00:03:01.809 --> 00:03:06.349\nLet's review all our health vocabulary.\n\n43\n00:03:06.409 --> 00:03:09.909\nNu kennen we belangrijke woorden.\n\n44\n00:03:09.949 --> 00:03:15.049\nWe kennen ziek, pijn en dokter.\n\n45\n00:03:15.089 --> 00:03:20.549\nWe kennen hoofd, buik en keel.\n\n46\n00:03:20.609 --> 00:03:26.490\nEn ook medicijn, rust en beter.\n\n47\n00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:30.610\nKeep practicing these sentences every day!\n\n48\n00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:32.670\nTot de volgende keer!\n
cw_health_words	en	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:06.500\nHello everyone, welcome back to Dutch with Gemini!\n\n2\n00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:11.580\nToday we are learning essential health words in Dutch.\n\n3\n00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:17.481\nThese words will help you explain how you feel or ask for help.\n\n4\n00:00:17.701 --> 00:00:20.581\nLet's begin!\n\n5\n00:00:20.641 --> 00:00:26.161\nOur first word is ZIEK, which means sick.\n\n6\n00:00:26.241 --> 00:00:30.261\nI am a little sick today.\n\n7\n00:00:30.281 --> 00:00:34.182\nMy brother is also sick.\n\n8\n00:00:34.222 --> 00:00:39.582\nNext, we have PIJN, which means pain.\n\n9\n00:00:39.682 --> 00:00:43.242\nI have a lot of pain here.\n\n10\n00:00:43.302 --> 00:00:46.862\nWhere does it hurt exactly?\n\n11\n00:00:46.922 --> 00:00:53.382\nNow let's look at body parts. HOOFD means head.\n\n12\n00:00:53.402 --> 00:00:57.403\nMy head hurts a little.\n\n13\n00:00:57.483 --> 00:01:01.543\nI have pain in my head.\n\n14\n00:01:01.583 --> 00:01:05.883\nThe word for belly or stomach is BUIK.\n\n15\n00:01:05.943 --> 00:01:10.703\nThe child has pain in the belly.\n\n16\n00:01:10.723 --> 00:01:15.524\nMy belly is very sensitive.\n\n17\n00:01:15.564 --> 00:01:19.904\nThe word for throat is KEEL.\n\n18\n00:01:19.984 --> 00:01:23.824\nMy throat is bothering me.\n\n19\n00:01:23.864 --> 00:01:27.884\nDrink warm tea for your throat.\n\n20\n00:01:27.904 --> 00:01:33.984\nWhen you are sick, you see a DOKTER, which means doctor.\n\n21\n00:01:34.084 --> 00:01:38.045\nI am going to the doctor tomorrow.\n\n22\n00:01:38.105 --> 00:01:42.425\nThe doctor helps the sick people.\n\n23\n00:01:42.465 --> 00:01:47.465\nThe word for medicine is MEDICIJN.\n\n24\n00:01:47.505 --> 00:01:51.845\nTake this medicine with water.\n\n25\n00:01:51.885 --> 00:01:56.145\nThis medicine works very fast.\n\n26\n00:01:56.165 --> 00:02:01.946\nTo heal, you need RUST, which means rest.\n\n27\n00:02:01.986 --> 00:02:05.146\nYou need a lot of rest now.\n\n28\n00:02:05.166 --> 00:02:08.066\nTake a day of rest.\n\n29\n00:02:08.106 --> 00:02:14.226\nWhen you recover, you feel BETER, which means better.\n\n30\n00:02:14.306 --> 00:02:17.426\nI feel much better already.\n\n31\n00:02:17.506 --> 00:02:21.187\nGet well soon and get better fast!\n\n32\n00:02:21.287 --> 00:02:27.087\nAnother useful word is KOORTS, which means fever.\n\n33\n00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:30.507\nHe has a high fever today.\n\n34\n00:02:30.547 --> 00:02:32.767\nDo you also have a fever?\n\n35\n00:02:32.827 --> 00:02:38.487\nYou buy your medicine at the APOTHEEK, or pharmacy.\n\n36\n00:02:38.567 --> 00:02:42.128\nI buy medicines at the pharmacy.\n\n37\n00:02:42.188 --> 00:02:45.608\nWhere is the nearest pharmacy?\n\n38\n00:02:45.668 --> 00:02:52.068\nFinally, don't forget WATER, which means water.\n\n39\n00:02:52.128 --> 00:02:55.248\nDrink a lot of water when you are sick.\n\n40\n00:02:55.288 --> 00:02:58.948\nA glass of cold water always helps.\n\n41\n00:02:58.988 --> 00:03:01.749\nYou did a fantastic job today!\n\n42\n00:03:01.809 --> 00:03:06.349\nLet's review all our health vocabulary.\n\n43\n00:03:06.409 --> 00:03:09.909\nNow we know important words.\n\n44\n00:03:09.949 --> 00:03:15.049\nWe know sick, pain, and doctor.\n\n45\n00:03:15.089 --> 00:03:20.549\nWe know head, belly, and throat.\n\n46\n00:03:20.609 --> 00:03:26.490\nAnd also medicine, rest, and better.\n\n47\n00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:30.610\nKeep practicing these sentences every day!\n\n48\n00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:32.670\nUntil next time!\n
cw_house_objects	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:02.020\nHello everyone!\n\n2\n00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:04.440\nWelcome to our Dutch lesson.\n\n3\n00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:08.680\nToday we learn household objects.\n\n4\n00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:11.620\nWelkom bij deze les!\n\n5\n00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:13.420\nAre you ready?\n\n6\n00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:16.141\nLaten we nu beginnen!\n\n7\n00:00:16.221 --> 00:00:20.221\nOur first word is sleutel.\n\n8\n00:00:20.321 --> 00:00:23.861\nSleutel means key in English.\n\n9\n00:00:23.921 --> 00:00:27.781\nLet's listen to two example sentences.\n\n10\n00:00:27.841 --> 00:00:31.461\nDit is een oude sleutel.\n\n11\n00:00:31.501 --> 00:00:35.041\nDe sleutel ligt op tafel.\n\n12\n00:00:35.061 --> 00:00:36.721\nGreat job!\n\n13\n00:00:36.841 --> 00:00:41.222\nRemember: sleutel means key.\n\n14\n00:00:41.302 --> 00:00:45.082\nOur next word is telefoon.\n\n15\n00:00:45.102 --> 00:00:48.782\nTelefoon means phone in English.\n\n16\n00:00:48.862 --> 00:00:51.782\nHere are two examples.\n\n17\n00:00:51.842 --> 00:00:55.702\nDit is mijn nieuwe telefoon.\n\n18\n00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:59.622\nDe telefoon ringt erg luid.\n\n19\n00:00:59.722 --> 00:01:01.162\nExcellent!\n\n20\n00:01:01.242 --> 00:01:05.982\nRemember: telefoon means phone.\n\n21\n00:01:06.042 --> 00:01:09.863\nNext, we have the word deur.\n\n22\n00:01:09.923 --> 00:01:13.543\nDeur means door in English.\n\n23\n00:01:13.583 --> 00:01:16.463\nLet's practice with two sentences.\n\n24\n00:01:16.523 --> 00:01:20.523\nDe deur is nu open.\n\n25\n00:01:20.603 --> 00:01:25.963\nIk sluit de zware deur.\n\n26\n00:01:26.043 --> 00:01:28.403\nWonderful practice!\n\n27\n00:01:28.443 --> 00:01:33.503\nRemember: deur means door.\n\n28\n00:01:33.543 --> 00:01:36.564\nNow let me teach you raam.\n\n29\n00:01:36.644 --> 00:01:41.304\nRaam means window in English.\n\n30\n00:01:41.344 --> 00:01:44.424\nLook at these simple sentences.\n\n31\n00:01:44.484 --> 00:01:49.124\nHet raam is heel schoon.\n\n32\n00:01:49.204 --> 00:01:53.684\nIk kijk door het raam.\n\n33\n00:01:53.744 --> 00:01:55.444\nVery well done!\n\n34\n00:01:55.484 --> 00:02:00.564\nRemember: raam means window.\n\n35\n00:02:00.644 --> 00:02:04.065\nOur fifth word is lamp.\n\n36\n00:02:04.205 --> 00:02:08.305\nLamp means lamp in English.\n\n37\n00:02:08.385 --> 00:02:11.185\nHere are clear examples.\n\n38\n00:02:11.225 --> 00:02:16.365\nDe lamp staat in de kamer.\n\n39\n00:02:16.465 --> 00:02:21.005\nIk doe de lamp aan.\n\n40\n00:02:21.045 --> 00:02:22.645\nGreat effort!\n\n41\n00:02:22.685 --> 00:02:27.605\nRemember: lamp means lamp.\n\n42\n00:02:27.645 --> 00:02:31.186\nNext up is the word tafel.\n\n43\n00:02:31.246 --> 00:02:35.366\nTafel means table in English.\n\n44\n00:02:35.426 --> 00:02:38.446\nLet me give you two examples.\n\n45\n00:02:38.486 --> 00:02:43.526\nDe tafel is erg groot.\n\n46\n00:02:43.586 --> 00:02:48.466\nWij eten aan de tafel.\n\n47\n00:02:48.486 --> 00:02:50.406\nAwesome job!\n\n48\n00:02:50.446 --> 00:02:55.026\nRemember: tafel means table.\n\n49\n00:02:55.086 --> 00:02:58.687\nLet's learn the word stoel.\n\n50\n00:02:58.787 --> 00:03:03.227\nStoel means chair in English.\n\n51\n00:03:03.287 --> 00:03:06.527\nListen to these Dutch sentences.\n\n52\n00:03:06.587 --> 00:03:11.827\nDit is een fijne stoel.\n\n53\n00:03:11.907 --> 00:03:17.307\nIk zit op de stoel.\n\n54\n00:03:17.347 --> 00:03:19.567\nFantastic work!\n\n55\n00:03:19.607 --> 00:03:24.227\nRemember: stoel means chair.\n\n56\n00:03:24.327 --> 00:03:29.008\nOur final word today is spiegel.\n\n57\n00:03:29.068 --> 00:03:33.748\nSpiegel means mirror in English.\n\n58\n00:03:33.768 --> 00:03:37.348\nLet me show you two sentences.\n\n59\n00:03:37.368 --> 00:03:44.748\nDe spiegel hangt aan de muur.\n\n60\n00:03:44.828 --> 00:03:50.268\nIk kijk in de spiegel.\n\n61\n00:03:50.308 --> 00:03:52.028\nPerfect!\n\n62\n00:03:52.089 --> 00:03:57.009\nRemember: spiegel means mirror.\n\n63\n00:03:57.069 --> 00:04:00.149\nYou did an amazing job today!\n\n64\n00:04:00.189 --> 00:04:03.929\nLet's do a quick spoken review.\n\n65\n00:04:03.989 --> 00:04:09.429\nVandaag leerden we deze woorden:\n\n66\n00:04:09.489 --> 00:04:23.889\nSleutel, telefoon, deur, raam, lamp, tafel, stoel, spiegel.\n\n67\n00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.990\nPractice these words at home!\n\n68\n00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:32.990\nTot de volgende keer!\n
cw_house_objects	en	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:03.020\nHello everyone!\n\n2\n00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:05.440\nWelcome to our Dutch lesson.\n\n3\n00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:09.680\nToday we learn household objects.\n\n4\n00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:12.620\nWelcome to this lesson!\n\n5\n00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.420\nAre you ready?\n\n6\n00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.141\nLet us start now!\n\n7\n00:00:17.221 --> 00:00:21.221\nOur first word is sleutel.\n\n8\n00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:24.861\nSleutel means key in English.\n\n9\n00:00:24.921 --> 00:00:28.781\nLet's listen to two example sentences.\n\n10\n00:00:28.841 --> 00:00:32.461\nThis is an old key.\n\n11\n00:00:32.501 --> 00:00:36.041\nThe key lies on the table.\n\n12\n00:00:36.061 --> 00:00:37.721\nGreat job!\n\n13\n00:00:37.841 --> 00:00:42.222\nRemember: sleutel means key.\n\n14\n00:00:42.302 --> 00:00:46.082\nOur next word is telefoon.\n\n15\n00:00:46.102 --> 00:00:49.782\nTelefoon means phone in English.\n\n16\n00:00:49.862 --> 00:00:52.782\nHere are two examples.\n\n17\n00:00:52.842 --> 00:00:56.702\nThis is my new phone.\n\n18\n00:00:56.722 --> 00:01:00.622\nThe phone rings very loudly.\n\n19\n00:01:00.722 --> 00:01:02.162\nExcellent!\n\n20\n00:01:02.242 --> 00:01:06.982\nRemember: telefoon means phone.\n\n21\n00:01:07.042 --> 00:01:10.863\nNext, we have the word deur.\n\n22\n00:01:10.923 --> 00:01:14.543\nDeur means door in English.\n\n23\n00:01:14.583 --> 00:01:17.463\nLet's practice with two sentences.\n\n24\n00:01:17.523 --> 00:01:21.523\nThe door is open now.\n\n25\n00:01:21.603 --> 00:01:26.963\nI close the heavy door.\n\n26\n00:01:27.043 --> 00:01:29.403\nWonderful practice!\n\n27\n00:01:29.443 --> 00:01:34.503\nRemember: deur means door.\n\n28\n00:01:34.543 --> 00:01:37.564\nNow let me teach you raam.\n\n29\n00:01:37.644 --> 00:01:42.304\nRaam means window in English.\n\n30\n00:01:42.344 --> 00:01:45.424\nLook at these simple sentences.\n\n31\n00:01:45.484 --> 00:01:50.124\nThe window is very clean.\n\n32\n00:01:50.204 --> 00:01:54.684\nI look through the window.\n\n33\n00:01:54.744 --> 00:01:56.444\nVery well done!\n\n34\n00:01:56.484 --> 00:02:01.564\nRemember: raam means window.\n\n35\n00:02:01.644 --> 00:02:05.065\nOur fifth word is lamp.\n\n36\n00:02:05.205 --> 00:02:09.305\nLamp means lamp in English.\n\n37\n00:02:09.385 --> 00:02:12.185\nHere are clear examples.\n\n38\n00:02:12.225 --> 00:02:17.365\nThe lamp stands in the room.\n\n39\n00:02:17.465 --> 00:02:22.005\nI turn on the lamp.\n\n40\n00:02:22.045 --> 00:02:23.645\nGreat effort!\n\n41\n00:02:23.685 --> 00:02:28.605\nRemember: lamp means lamp.\n\n42\n00:02:28.645 --> 00:02:32.186\nNext up is the word tafel.\n\n43\n00:02:32.246 --> 00:02:36.366\nTafel means table in English.\n\n44\n00:02:36.426 --> 00:02:39.446\nLet me give you two examples.\n\n45\n00:02:39.486 --> 00:02:44.526\nThe table is very big.\n\n46\n00:02:44.586 --> 00:02:49.466\nWe eat at the table.\n\n47\n00:02:49.486 --> 00:02:51.406\nAwesome job!\n\n48\n00:02:51.446 --> 00:02:56.026\nRemember: tafel means table.\n\n49\n00:02:56.086 --> 00:02:59.687\nLet's learn the word stoel.\n\n50\n00:02:59.787 --> 00:03:04.227\nStoel means chair in English.\n\n51\n00:03:04.287 --> 00:03:07.527\nListen to these Dutch sentences.\n\n52\n00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:12.827\nThis is a nice chair.\n\n53\n00:03:12.907 --> 00:03:18.307\nI sit on the chair.\n\n54\n00:03:18.347 --> 00:03:20.567\nFantastic work!\n\n55\n00:03:20.607 --> 00:03:25.227\nRemember: stoel means chair.\n\n56\n00:03:25.327 --> 00:03:30.008\nOur final word today is spiegel.\n\n57\n00:03:30.068 --> 00:03:34.748\nSpiegel means mirror in English.\n\n58\n00:03:34.768 --> 00:03:38.348\nLet me show you two sentences.\n\n59\n00:03:38.368 --> 00:03:45.748\nThe mirror hangs on the wall.\n\n60\n00:03:45.828 --> 00:03:51.268\nI look in the mirror.\n\n61\n00:03:51.308 --> 00:03:53.028\nPerfect!\n\n62\n00:03:53.089 --> 00:03:58.009\nRemember: spiegel means mirror.\n\n63\n00:03:58.069 --> 00:04:01.149\nYou did an amazing job today!\n\n64\n00:04:01.189 --> 00:04:04.929\nLet's do a quick spoken review.\n\n65\n00:04:04.989 --> 00:04:10.429\nToday we learned these words:\n\n66\n00:04:10.489 --> 00:04:24.889\nSleutel, telefoon, deur, raam, lamp, tafel, stoel, spiegel.\n\n67\n00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:27.990\nPractice these words at home!\n\n68\n00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:33.990\nUntil next time!\n
cw_linking_words	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:05.720\nHello everyone, welcome back to your Dutch lesson!\n\n2\n00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:09.720\nToday, we are learning common linking words.\n\n3\n00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:14.920\nLinking words connect your ideas and make your Dutch sound natural.\n\n4\n00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:19.180\nWe will practice eight essential words step by step.\n\n5\n00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.641\nAre you ready?\n\n6\n00:00:21.861 --> 00:00:25.561\nLaten we beginnen!\n\n7\n00:00:25.641 --> 00:00:28.961\nOur first word is 'eerst'.\n\n8\n00:00:29.041 --> 00:00:32.401\n'Eerst' means 'first' in English.\n\n9\n00:00:32.501 --> 00:00:35.181\nListen to this example sentence:\n\n10\n00:00:35.261 --> 00:00:40.141\nEerst drink ik warm water.\n\n11\n00:00:40.201 --> 00:00:43.501\nFirst I drink warm water.\n\n12\n00:00:43.541 --> 00:00:47.401\nYou use 'eerst' at the start of a sequence.\n\n13\n00:00:47.441 --> 00:00:49.941\nLet's hear another example:\n\n14\n00:00:50.041 --> 00:00:54.101\nEerst lees ik een boek.\n\n15\n00:00:54.161 --> 00:00:56.641\nFirst I read a book.\n\n16\n00:00:56.701 --> 00:01:00.822\nRemember: 'eerst' means 'first'.\n\n17\n00:01:00.882 --> 00:01:04.282\nNext, we have the word 'dan'.\n\n18\n00:01:04.322 --> 00:01:06.882\n'Dan' means 'then'.\n\n19\n00:01:06.922 --> 00:01:09.142\nHere is our first example:\n\n20\n00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:12.362\nDan eet ik een appel.\n\n21\n00:01:12.402 --> 00:01:15.542\nThen I eat an apple.\n\n22\n00:01:15.562 --> 00:01:20.482\n'Dan' helps move to the next action.\n\n23\n00:01:20.602 --> 00:01:23.262\nLet's try another sentence:\n\n24\n00:01:23.322 --> 00:01:26.742\nDan ga ik naar school.\n\n25\n00:01:26.782 --> 00:01:30.622\nThen I go to school.\n\n26\n00:01:30.642 --> 00:01:36.382\nGreat work! 'Dan' means 'then'.\n\n27\n00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:40.303\nOur third word is 'daarna'.\n\n28\n00:01:40.323 --> 00:01:45.383\n'Daarna' means 'after that'.\n\n29\n00:01:45.483 --> 00:01:48.443\nListen carefully to this sentence:\n\n30\n00:01:48.503 --> 00:01:52.783\nDaarna speel ik een spel.\n\n31\n00:01:52.943 --> 00:01:56.663\nAfter that I play a game.\n\n32\n00:01:56.703 --> 00:02:00.943\nIt shows what happens after an action.\n\n33\n00:02:01.003 --> 00:02:03.323\nHere is one more example:\n\n34\n00:02:03.383 --> 00:02:07.183\nDaarna kook ik het eten.\n\n35\n00:02:07.343 --> 00:02:10.963\nAfter that I cook the dinner.\n\n36\n00:02:11.043 --> 00:02:16.663\nSo, 'daarna' means 'after that'.\n\n37\n00:02:16.783 --> 00:02:20.164\nNow let's look at 'tot slot'.\n\n38\n00:02:20.184 --> 00:02:26.524\n'Tot slot' means 'finally' or 'in conclusion'.\n\n39\n00:02:26.564 --> 00:02:28.864\nHere is an example:\n\n40\n00:02:28.904 --> 00:02:33.004\nTot slot drink ik thee.\n\n41\n00:02:33.064 --> 00:02:36.224\nFinally I drink tea.\n\n42\n00:02:36.464 --> 00:02:41.284\nUse 'tot slot' at the end of a series.\n\n43\n00:02:41.364 --> 00:02:44.644\nLet's practice with another sentence:\n\n44\n00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:48.664\nTot slot ga ik slapen.\n\n45\n00:02:48.704 --> 00:02:51.964\nFinally I go to sleep.\n\n46\n00:02:52.024 --> 00:02:57.204\nRemember: 'tot slot' means 'finally'.\n\n47\n00:02:57.324 --> 00:03:02.265\nMoving on, our fifth word is 'ook'.\n\n48\n00:03:02.285 --> 00:03:07.525\n'Ook' means 'also' or 'too'.\n\n49\n00:03:07.565 --> 00:03:10.765\nListen to this simple example:\n\n50\n00:03:10.845 --> 00:03:14.125\nIk wil ook een koekje.\n\n51\n00:03:14.285 --> 00:03:17.325\nI also want a cookie.\n\n52\n00:03:17.385 --> 00:03:20.685\nIt adds extra information.\n\n53\n00:03:20.725 --> 00:03:23.525\nHere is another sentence:\n\n54\n00:03:23.585 --> 00:03:26.985\nHij komt ook naar school.\n\n55\n00:03:27.045 --> 00:03:30.185\nHe is also coming to school.\n\n56\n00:03:30.265 --> 00:03:33.865\nSo, 'ook' means 'also'.\n\n57\n00:03:33.945 --> 00:03:37.725\nOur sixth word is 'wel'.\n\n58\n00:03:37.745 --> 00:03:43.206\n'Wel' is used to express agreement or positive emphasis.\n\n59\n00:03:43.346 --> 00:03:46.546\nLet's hear an example sentence:\n\n60\n00:03:46.606 --> 00:03:51.126\nIk spreek wel Nederlands.\n\n61\n00:03:51.286 --> 00:03:53.766\nI do speak Dutch.\n\n62\n00:03:53.846 --> 00:03:57.966\nIt gives a warm or affirmative tone.\n\n63\n00:03:58.026 --> 00:04:01.106\nHere is another example:\n\n64\n00:04:01.166 --> 00:04:05.666\nHet is wel een mooi huis.\n\n65\n00:04:05.726 --> 00:04:09.766\nIt is indeed a nice house.\n\n66\n00:04:09.826 --> 00:04:15.546\nRemember: 'wel' adds positive emphasis.\n\n67\n00:04:15.566 --> 00:04:19.927\nThe seventh word is 'toch'.\n\n68\n00:04:19.947 --> 00:04:26.767\n'Toch' means 'still', 'anyway', or 'after all'.\n\n69\n00:04:26.887 --> 00:04:29.927\nListen to this sentence:\n\n70\n00:04:29.987 --> 00:04:35.487\nIk ga toch naar buiten.\n\n71\n00:04:35.667 --> 00:04:39.407\nI am going outside anyway.\n\n72\n00:04:39.467 --> 00:04:44.667\nIt often expresses an action despite something else.\n\n73\n00:04:44.787 --> 00:04:48.167\nLet me give you another example:\n\n74\n00:04:48.227 --> 00:04:52.247\nHet is toch heel warm.\n\n75\n00:04:52.307 --> 00:04:55.547\nIt is still very warm.\n\n76\n00:04:55.687 --> 00:05:02.148\nSo, 'toch' means 'still' or 'anyway'.\n\n77\n00:05:02.228 --> 00:05:07.028\nOur eighth word is 'eigenlijk'.\n\n78\n00:05:07.048 --> 00:05:12.968\n'Eigenlijk' means 'actually' or 'in fact'.\n\n79\n00:05:13.008 --> 00:05:15.268\nHere is an example:\n\n80\n00:05:15.328 --> 00:05:20.108\nIk ben eigenlijk heel moe.\n\n81\n00:05:20.288 --> 00:05:24.068\nI am actually very tired.\n\n82\n00:05:24.148 --> 00:05:29.168\nIt helps share a genuine feeling or fact.\n\n83\n00:05:29.248 --> 00:05:32.588\nLet's listen to another sentence:\n\n84\n00:05:32.608 --> 00:05:37.588\nDat is eigenlijk erg goed.\n\n85\n00:05:37.628 --> 00:05:41.629\nThat is actually very good.\n\n86\n00:05:41.769 --> 00:05:47.249\nRemember: 'eigenlijk' means 'actually'.\n\n87\n00:05:47.329 --> 00:05:50.749\nYou did a fantastic job today!\n\n88\n00:05:50.829 --> 00:05:56.229\nLet's do a quick spoken recap of all eight words.\n\n89\n00:05:56.289 --> 00:06:02.169\nVandaag leerden we deze handige woorden.\n\n90\n00:06:02.209 --> 00:06:06.489\nToday we learned these useful words.\n\n91\n00:06:06.669 --> 00:06:12.009\nEerst, dan, daarna en tot slot.\n\n92\n00:06:12.109 --> 00:06:17.790\nFirst, then, after that, and finally.\n\n93\n00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:24.050\nOok, wel, toch en eigenlijk.\n\n94\n00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:30.010\nAlso, indeed, anyway, and actually.\n\n95\n00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:34.910\nKeep practicing these linking words in your daily Dutch conversations.\n\n96\n00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:37.070\nSee you next time! Goodbye!\n
cw_linking_words	en	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:05.720\nHello everyone, welcome back to your Dutch lesson!\n\n2\n00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:09.720\nToday, we are learning common linking words.\n\n3\n00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:14.920\nLinking words connect your ideas and make your Dutch sound natural.\n\n4\n00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:19.180\nWe will practice eight essential words step by step.\n\n5\n00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.641\nAre you ready?\n\n6\n00:00:21.861 --> 00:00:25.561\nLet's begin!\n\n7\n00:00:25.641 --> 00:00:28.961\nOur first word is 'eerst'.\n\n8\n00:00:29.041 --> 00:00:32.401\n'Eerst' means 'first' in English.\n\n9\n00:00:32.501 --> 00:00:35.181\nListen to this example sentence:\n\n10\n00:00:35.261 --> 00:00:40.141\nFirst I drink warm water.\n\n11\n00:00:40.201 --> 00:00:43.501\nFirst I drink warm water.\n\n12\n00:00:43.541 --> 00:00:47.401\nYou use 'eerst' at the start of a sequence.\n\n13\n00:00:47.441 --> 00:00:49.941\nLet's hear another example:\n\n14\n00:00:50.041 --> 00:00:54.101\nFirst I read a book.\n\n15\n00:00:54.161 --> 00:00:56.641\nFirst I read a book.\n\n16\n00:00:56.701 --> 00:01:00.822\nRemember: 'eerst' means 'first'.\n\n17\n00:01:00.882 --> 00:01:04.282\nNext, we have the word 'dan'.\n\n18\n00:01:04.322 --> 00:01:06.882\n'Dan' means 'then'.\n\n19\n00:01:06.922 --> 00:01:09.142\nHere is our first example:\n\n20\n00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:12.362\nThen I eat an apple.\n\n21\n00:01:12.402 --> 00:01:15.542\nThen I eat an apple.\n\n22\n00:01:15.562 --> 00:01:20.482\n'Dan' helps move to the next action.\n\n23\n00:01:20.602 --> 00:01:23.262\nLet's try another sentence:\n\n24\n00:01:23.322 --> 00:01:26.742\nThen I go to school.\n\n25\n00:01:26.782 --> 00:01:30.622\nThen I go to school.\n\n26\n00:01:30.642 --> 00:01:36.382\nGreat work! 'Dan' means 'then'.\n\n27\n00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:40.303\nOur third word is 'daarna'.\n\n28\n00:01:40.323 --> 00:01:45.383\n'Daarna' means 'after that'.\n\n29\n00:01:45.483 --> 00:01:48.443\nListen carefully to this sentence:\n\n30\n00:01:48.503 --> 00:01:52.783\nAfter that I play a game.\n\n31\n00:01:52.943 --> 00:01:56.663\nAfter that I play a game.\n\n32\n00:01:56.703 --> 00:02:00.943\nIt shows what happens after an action.\n\n33\n00:02:01.003 --> 00:02:03.323\nHere is one more example:\n\n34\n00:02:03.383 --> 00:02:07.183\nAfter that I cook the dinner.\n\n35\n00:02:07.343 --> 00:02:10.963\nAfter that I cook the dinner.\n\n36\n00:02:11.043 --> 00:02:16.663\nSo, 'daarna' means 'after that'.\n\n37\n00:02:16.783 --> 00:02:20.164\nNow let's look at 'tot slot'.\n\n38\n00:02:20.184 --> 00:02:26.524\n'Tot slot' means 'finally' or 'in conclusion'.\n\n39\n00:02:26.564 --> 00:02:28.864\nHere is an example:\n\n40\n00:02:28.904 --> 00:02:33.004\nFinally I drink tea.\n\n41\n00:02:33.064 --> 00:02:36.224\nFinally I drink tea.\n\n42\n00:02:36.464 --> 00:02:41.284\nUse 'tot slot' at the end of a series.\n\n43\n00:02:41.364 --> 00:02:44.644\nLet's practice with another sentence:\n\n44\n00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:48.664\nFinally I go to sleep.\n\n45\n00:02:48.704 --> 00:02:51.964\nFinally I go to sleep.\n\n46\n00:02:52.024 --> 00:02:57.204\nRemember: 'tot slot' means 'finally'.\n\n47\n00:02:57.324 --> 00:03:02.265\nMoving on, our fifth word is 'ook'.\n\n48\n00:03:02.285 --> 00:03:07.525\n'Ook' means 'also' or 'too'.\n\n49\n00:03:07.565 --> 00:03:10.765\nListen to this simple example:\n\n50\n00:03:10.845 --> 00:03:14.125\nI also want a cookie.\n\n51\n00:03:14.285 --> 00:03:17.325\nI also want a cookie.\n\n52\n00:03:17.385 --> 00:03:20.685\nIt adds extra information.\n\n53\n00:03:20.725 --> 00:03:23.525\nHere is another sentence:\n\n54\n00:03:23.585 --> 00:03:26.985\nHe is also coming to school.\n\n55\n00:03:27.045 --> 00:03:30.185\nHe is also coming to school.\n\n56\n00:03:30.265 --> 00:03:33.865\nSo, 'ook' means 'also'.\n\n57\n00:03:33.945 --> 00:03:37.725\nOur sixth word is 'wel'.\n\n58\n00:03:37.745 --> 00:03:43.206\n'Wel' is used to express agreement or positive emphasis.\n\n59\n00:03:43.346 --> 00:03:46.546\nLet's hear an example sentence:\n\n60\n00:03:46.606 --> 00:03:51.126\nI do speak Dutch.\n\n61\n00:03:51.286 --> 00:03:53.766\nI do speak Dutch.\n\n62\n00:03:53.846 --> 00:03:57.966\nIt gives a warm or affirmative tone.\n\n63\n00:03:58.026 --> 00:04:01.106\nHere is another example:\n\n64\n00:04:01.166 --> 00:04:05.666\nIt is indeed a nice house.\n\n65\n00:04:05.726 --> 00:04:09.766\nIt is indeed a nice house.\n\n66\n00:04:09.826 --> 00:04:15.546\nRemember: 'wel' adds positive emphasis.\n\n67\n00:04:15.566 --> 00:04:19.927\nThe seventh word is 'toch'.\n\n68\n00:04:19.947 --> 00:04:26.767\n'Toch' means 'still', 'anyway', or 'after all'.\n\n69\n00:04:26.887 --> 00:04:29.927\nListen to this sentence:\n\n70\n00:04:29.987 --> 00:04:35.487\nI am going outside anyway.\n\n71\n00:04:35.667 --> 00:04:39.407\nI am going outside anyway.\n\n72\n00:04:39.467 --> 00:04:44.667\nIt often expresses an action despite something else.\n\n73\n00:04:44.787 --> 00:04:48.167\nLet me give you another example:\n\n74\n00:04:48.227 --> 00:04:52.247\nIt is still very warm.\n\n75\n00:04:52.307 --> 00:04:55.547\nIt is still very warm.\n\n76\n00:04:55.687 --> 00:05:02.148\nSo, 'toch' means 'still' or 'anyway'.\n\n77\n00:05:02.228 --> 00:05:07.028\nOur eighth word is 'eigenlijk'.\n\n78\n00:05:07.048 --> 00:05:12.968\n'Eigenlijk' means 'actually' or 'in fact'.\n\n79\n00:05:13.008 --> 00:05:15.268\nHere is an example:\n\n80\n00:05:15.328 --> 00:05:20.108\nI am actually very tired.\n\n81\n00:05:20.288 --> 00:05:24.068\nI am actually very tired.\n\n82\n00:05:24.148 --> 00:05:29.168\nIt helps share a genuine feeling or fact.\n\n83\n00:05:29.248 --> 00:05:32.588\nLet's listen to another sentence:\n\n84\n00:05:32.608 --> 00:05:37.588\nThat is actually very good.\n\n85\n00:05:37.628 --> 00:05:41.629\nThat is actually very good.\n\n86\n00:05:41.769 --> 00:05:47.249\nRemember: 'eigenlijk' means 'actually'.\n\n87\n00:05:47.329 --> 00:05:50.749\nYou did a fantastic job today!\n\n88\n00:05:50.829 --> 00:05:56.229\nLet's do a quick spoken recap of all eight words.\n\n89\n00:05:56.289 --> 00:06:02.169\nToday we learned these useful words.\n\n90\n00:06:02.209 --> 00:06:06.489\nToday we learned these useful words.\n\n91\n00:06:06.669 --> 00:06:12.009\nFirst, then, after that, and finally.\n\n92\n00:06:12.109 --> 00:06:17.790\nFirst, then, after that, and finally.\n\n93\n00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:24.050\nAlso, indeed, anyway, and actually.\n\n94\n00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:30.010\nAlso, indeed, anyway, and actually.\n\n95\n00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:34.910\nKeep practicing these linking words in your daily Dutch conversations.\n\n96\n00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:37.070\nSee you next time! Goodbye!\n
cw_nature	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:03.480\nWelcome to today's Dutch lesson!\n\n2\n00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:07.100\nToday we learn nature words.\n\n3\n00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.980\nNature is very beautiful.\n\n4\n00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:13.620\nLet's start with our lesson!\n\n5\n00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.461\nLaten we beginnen!\n\n6\n00:00:17.561 --> 00:00:20.301\nLet's begin!\n\n7\n00:00:20.401 --> 00:00:23.881\nOur first word is boom.\n\n8\n00:00:23.921 --> 00:00:28.801\nBoom means tree in English.\n\n9\n00:00:28.881 --> 00:00:33.741\nIk zie een grote boom.\n\n10\n00:00:33.901 --> 00:00:37.861\nI see a big tree.\n\n11\n00:00:37.901 --> 00:00:41.981\nDe boom is groen.\n\n12\n00:00:42.001 --> 00:00:45.681\nThe tree is green.\n\n13\n00:00:45.741 --> 00:00:49.501\nBoom means tree.\n\n14\n00:00:49.601 --> 00:00:52.922\nOur second word is bloem.\n\n15\n00:00:52.982 --> 00:00:57.182\nBloem means flower.\n\n16\n00:00:57.242 --> 00:01:01.882\nDe bloem is erg mooi.\n\n17\n00:01:01.902 --> 00:01:06.122\nThe flower is very pretty.\n\n18\n00:01:06.182 --> 00:01:10.742\nZij koopt een rode bloem.\n\n19\n00:01:10.802 --> 00:01:14.662\nShe buys a red flower.\n\n20\n00:01:14.722 --> 00:01:17.782\nBloem means flower.\n\n21\n00:01:17.882 --> 00:01:22.262\nOur third word is gras.\n\n22\n00:01:22.342 --> 00:01:26.783\nGras means grass.\n\n23\n00:01:26.843 --> 00:01:31.863\nHet gras is groen.\n\n24\n00:01:31.903 --> 00:01:36.183\nThe grass is green.\n\n25\n00:01:36.203 --> 00:01:41.583\nWij zitten in het gras.\n\n26\n00:01:41.623 --> 00:01:45.543\nWe sit in the grass.\n\n27\n00:01:45.643 --> 00:01:50.103\nGras means grass.\n\n28\n00:01:50.123 --> 00:01:53.083\nGreat progress so far!\n\n29\n00:01:53.143 --> 00:01:56.443\nNow let's look at the sky.\n\n30\n00:01:56.503 --> 00:02:01.004\nOur fourth word is zon.\n\n31\n00:02:01.084 --> 00:02:04.944\nZon means sun.\n\n32\n00:02:04.984 --> 00:02:10.304\nDe zon schijnt vandaag.\n\n33\n00:02:10.324 --> 00:02:14.244\nThe sun shines today.\n\n34\n00:02:14.324 --> 00:02:18.924\nIk hou van de zon.\n\n35\n00:02:18.944 --> 00:02:22.044\nI love the sun.\n\n36\n00:02:22.104 --> 00:02:26.104\nZon means sun.\n\n37\n00:02:26.184 --> 00:02:30.664\nOur fifth word is maan.\n\n38\n00:02:30.704 --> 00:02:34.585\nMaan means moon.\n\n39\n00:02:34.625 --> 00:02:36.825\nDe maan schijnt 's nachts.\n\n40\n00:02:36.885 --> 00:02:39.745\nThe moon shines at night.\n\n41\n00:02:39.765 --> 00:02:43.165\nIk zie de witte maan.\n\n42\n00:02:43.265 --> 00:02:46.845\nI see the white moon.\n\n43\n00:02:46.885 --> 00:02:49.725\nMaan means moon.\n\n44\n00:02:49.805 --> 00:02:53.505\nOur sixth word is lucht.\n\n45\n00:02:53.565 --> 00:02:57.745\nLucht means sky or air.\n\n46\n00:02:57.785 --> 00:03:01.425\nDe lucht is heel blauw.\n\n47\n00:03:01.465 --> 00:03:04.745\nThe sky is very blue.\n\n48\n00:03:04.825 --> 00:03:08.626\nVogels vliegen in de lucht.\n\n49\n00:03:08.666 --> 00:03:12.146\nBirds fly in the sky.\n\n50\n00:03:12.206 --> 00:03:15.066\nLucht means sky.\n\n51\n00:03:15.126 --> 00:03:16.526\nExcellent!\n\n52\n00:03:16.566 --> 00:03:20.986\nNext, let's learn about water and land.\n\n53\n00:03:21.066 --> 00:03:24.546\nOur seventh word is zee.\n\n54\n00:03:24.626 --> 00:03:27.646\nZee means sea.\n\n55\n00:03:27.686 --> 00:03:31.246\nDe zee is erg koud.\n\n56\n00:03:31.266 --> 00:03:34.406\nThe sea is very cold.\n\n57\n00:03:34.446 --> 00:03:37.286\nWij zwemmen in de zee.\n\n58\n00:03:37.306 --> 00:03:40.087\nWe swim in the sea.\n\n59\n00:03:40.147 --> 00:03:42.927\nZee means sea.\n\n60\n00:03:43.007 --> 00:03:47.127\nOur eighth word is rivier.\n\n61\n00:03:47.187 --> 00:03:51.267\nRivier means river.\n\n62\n00:03:51.327 --> 00:03:55.567\nDe rivier is heel lang.\n\n63\n00:03:55.587 --> 00:03:59.547\nThe river is very long.\n\n64\n00:03:59.627 --> 00:04:04.087\nVissen zwemmen in de rivier.\n\n65\n00:04:04.187 --> 00:04:08.027\nFish swim in the river.\n\n66\n00:04:08.087 --> 00:04:12.067\nRivier means river.\n\n67\n00:04:12.147 --> 00:04:16.328\nOur ninth word is berg.\n\n68\n00:04:16.388 --> 00:04:20.428\nBerg means mountain.\n\n69\n00:04:20.468 --> 00:04:24.708\nDe berg is heel hoog.\n\n70\n00:04:24.728 --> 00:04:28.748\nThe mountain is very high.\n\n71\n00:04:28.788 --> 00:04:33.188\nWij klimmen op de berg.\n\n72\n00:04:33.208 --> 00:04:36.848\nWe climb on the mountain.\n\n73\n00:04:36.908 --> 00:04:41.048\nBerg means mountain.\n\n74\n00:04:41.088 --> 00:04:44.528\nTime for a quick recap!\n\n75\n00:04:44.588 --> 00:04:49.329\nVandaag leerden we nieuwe woorden.\n\n76\n00:04:49.369 --> 00:04:53.729\nToday we learned new words.\n\n77\n00:04:53.789 --> 00:04:59.609\nBoom, bloem, gras, zon en maan.\n\n78\n00:04:59.649 --> 00:05:08.269\nTree, flower, grass, sun and moon.\n\n79\n00:05:08.389 --> 00:05:17.909\nEn ook lucht, zee, rivier, berg.\n\n80\n00:05:18.009 --> 00:05:27.290\nAnd also sky, sea, river, mountain.\n\n81\n00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:31.850\nYou did a fantastic job today!\n\n82\n00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:35.990\nPractice these words often.\n\n83\n00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:37.710\nSee you in the next lesson!\n
