s look at NOOIT, which means never.\n\n30\n00:02:21.325 --> 00:02:25.865\nIk kom nooit te laat.\n\n31\n00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:29.026\nI never arrive late.\n\n32\n00:02:29.106 --> 00:02:34.286\nZij drinkt nooit koffie 's morgens.\n\n33\n00:02:34.386 --> 00:02:37.586\nShe never drinks coffee in the morning.\n\n34\n00:02:37.626 --> 00:02:42.386\nHij eet nooit vlees.\n\n35\n00:02:42.426 --> 00:02:45.366\nHe never eats meat.\n\n36\n00:02:45.406 --> 00:02:51.226\nNext we have BIJNA, which means almost.\n\n37\n00:02:51.286 --> 00:02:56.007\nHet is bijna acht uur.\n\n38\n00:02:56.087 --> 00:02:59.307\nIt is almost eight o'clock.\n\n39\n00:02:59.367 --> 00:03:04.287\nIk ben bijna klaar met werken.\n\n40\n00:03:04.447 --> 00:03:07.787\nI am almost done with work.\n\n41\n00:03:07.827 --> 00:03:13.107\nDe trein komt bijna aan.\n\n42\n00:03:13.127 --> 00:03:16.547\nThe train is almost arriving.\n\n43\n00:03:16.627 --> 00:03:24.888\nOur final word is NAUWELIJK S, which means hardly or barely.\n\n44\n00:03:24.928 --> 00:03:29.428\nIk kan het nauwelijks horen.\n\n45\n00:03:29.548 --> 00:03:32.008\nI can hardly hear it.\n\n46\n00:03:32.068 --> 00:03:37.148\nHij spreekt nauwelijks Nederlands.\n\n47\n00:03:37.188 --> 00:03:40.068\nHe barely speaks Dutch.\n\n48\n00:03:40.148 --> 00:03:45.008\nEr is nauwelijks tijd over.\n\n49\n00:03:45.048 --> 00:03:48.169\nThere is hardly any time left.\n\n50\n00:03:48.209 --> 00:03:50.249\nGreat job today!\n\n51\n00:03:50.289 --> 00:03:53.649\nLet's do a quick recap of today's words.\n\n52\n00:03:53.689 --> 00:04:01.349\nVandaag leerden we: niemand, niets, nergens.\n\n53\n00:04:01.389 --> 00:04:07.729\nToday we learned: nobody, nothing, nowhere.\n\n54\n00:04:07.789 --> 00:04:14.490\nEn ook: nooit, bijna, nauwelijks.\n\n55\n00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:20.690\nAnd also: never, almost, hardly.\n\n56\n00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:24.090\nPractice these words in your daily conversation!\n\n57\n00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:26.430\nTot de volgende keer!\n\n58\n00:04:26.490 