cw_numbers_large	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:04.620\nWelcome to today's Dutch lesson!\n\n2\n00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:09.200\nToday we will learn large numbers in Dutch.\n\n3\n00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:15.561\nWe will learn words like hundred, thousand, and million.\n\n4\n00:00:15.601 --> 00:00:19.741\nWe will also talk about prices and years.\n\n5\n00:00:19.801 --> 00:00:21.961\nAre you ready to begin?\n\n6\n00:00:22.161 --> 00:00:25.421\nLaten we beginnen!\n\n7\n00:00:25.561 --> 00:00:27.361\nLet's start!\n\n8\n00:00:27.441 --> 00:00:31.401\nOur first key word is HONDERD.\n\n9\n00:00:31.441 --> 00:00:34.081\nHonderd means hundred.\n\n10\n00:00:34.141 --> 00:00:38.261\nHet boek kost honderd euro.\n\n11\n00:00:38.281 --> 00:00:41.902\nThe book costs one hundred euros.\n\n12\n00:00:41.982 --> 00:00:45.542\nIk zie honderd mensen hier.\n\n13\n00:00:45.662 --> 00:00:49.002\nI see one hundred people here.\n\n14\n00:00:49.022 --> 00:00:52.222\nNext is TWEEHONDERD.\n\n15\n00:00:52.262 --> 00:00:55.622\nTweehonderd means two hundred.\n\n16\n00:00:55.682 --> 00:00:59.862\nHij heeft tweehonderd boeken thuis.\n\n17\n00:00:59.922 --> 00:01:03.182\nHe has two hundred books at home.\n\n18\n00:01:03.222 --> 00:01:07.303\nDit hotel heeft tweehonderd kamers.\n\n19\n00:01:07.323 --> 00:01:11.303\nThis hotel has two hundred rooms.\n\n20\n00:01:11.403 --> 00:01:15.783\nNow let's look at DRIEHONDERD.\n\n21\n00:01:15.823 --> 00:01:20.323\nDriehonderd means three hundred.\n\n22\n00:01:20.363 --> 00:01:26.063\nDe fiets kost driehonderd euro.\n\n23\n00:01:26.083 --> 00:01:30.963\nThe bicycle costs three hundred euros.\n\n24\n00:01:31.003 --> 00:01:35.464\nGreat! Now let's move to thousands.\n\n25\n00:01:35.484 --> 00:01:41.004\nThe word for thousand is DUIZEND.\n\n26\n00:01:41.084 --> 00:01:46.304\nEr wonen duizend mensen hier.\n\n27\n00:01:46.404 --> 00:01:49.784\nOne thousand people live here.\n\n28\n00:01:49.844 --> 00:01:55.084\nDe auto kost duizend euro.\n\n29\n00:01:55.104 --> 00:02:00.045\nThe car costs one thousand euros.\n\n30\n00:02:00.085 --> 00:02:04.305\nNext is VIJFDUIZEND.\n\n31\n00:02:04.345 --> 00:02:09.265\nVijfduizend means five thousand.\n\n32\n00:02:09.345 --> 00:02:14.945\nHij verdient vijfduizend euro.\n\n33\n00:02:14.985 --> 00:02:19.145\nHe earns five thousand euros.\n\n34\n00:02:19.165 --> 00:02:22.065\nNow for even bigger numbers!\n\n35\n00:02:22.085 --> 00:02:27.906\nThe word for million is MILJOEN.\n\n36\n00:02:28.066 --> 00:02:33.246\nAmsterdam heeft een miljoen inwoners.\n\n37\n00:02:33.406 --> 00:02:37.806\nAmsterdam has one million inhabitants.\n\n38\n00:02:37.866 --> 00:02:40.206\nNow let's practice prices.\n\n39\n00:02:40.266 --> 00:02:45.386\nIn Dutch, we use EURO and CENT.\n\n40\n00:02:45.426 --> 00:02:50.986\nDe koffie kost twee euro vijftig.\n\n41\n00:02:51.006 --> 00:02:55.047\nThe coffee costs two euros fifty.\n\n42\n00:02:55.107 --> 00:02:59.647\nDe broek kost vijftig euro.\n\n43\n00:02:59.667 --> 00:03:03.707\nThe pants cost fifty euros.\n\n44\n00:03:03.747 --> 00:03:08.547\nEen appel kost tachtig cent.\n\n45\n00:03:08.587 --> 00:03:12.167\nAn apple costs eighty cents.\n\n46\n00:03:12.187 --> 00:03:15.847\nNow let's learn how to express years.\n\n47\n00:03:15.887 --> 00:03:23.868\nFor years in the 1900s, we say nineteen hundred followed by the number.\n\n48\n00:03:23.948 --> 00:03:29.648\nIk ben geboren in negentienennegentig.\n\n49\n00:03:29.808 --> 00:03:34.468\nI was born in nineteen ninety-nine.\n\n50\n00:03:34.528 --> 00:03:41.088\nFor years in the 2000s, we say tweeduizend followed by the number.\n\n51\n00:03:41.148 --> 00:03:45.348\nHet is nu tweeduizendvierentwintig.\n\n52\n00:03:45.449 --> 00:03:49.709\nIt is now two thousand twenty-four.\n\n53\n00:03:49.809 --> 00:03:55.009\nMijn vriend woont hier sinds tweeduizendtien.\n\n54\n00:03:55.049 --> 00:04:00.369\nMy friend lives here since two thousand ten.\n\n55\n00:04:00.449 --> 00:04:03.049\nFantastic practice today!\n\n56\n00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:11.609\nVandaag leerden we: honderd, duizend, en miljoen.\n\n57\n00:04:11.649 --> 00:04:19.090\nToday we learned: hundred, thousand, and million.\n\n58\n00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:22.590\nDank je wel en tot ziens!\n\n59\n00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.990\nThank you and see you soon!\n
