:55.104 --> 00:02:00.045\nThe car costs one thousand euros.\n\n30\n00:02:00.085 --> 00:02:04.305\nNext is VIJFDUIZEND.\n\n31\n00:02:04.345 --> 00:02:09.265\nVijfduizend means five thousand.\n\n32\n00:02:09.345 --> 00:02:14.945\nHe earns five thousand euros.\n\n33\n00:02:14.985 --> 00:02:19.145\nHe earns five thousand euros.\n\n34\n00:02:19.165 --> 00:02:22.065\nNow for even bigger numbers!\n\n35\n00:02:22.085 --> 00:02:27.906\nThe word for million is MILJOEN.\n\n36\n00:02:28.066 --> 00:02:33.246\nAmsterdam has one million inhabitants.\n\n37\n00:02:33.406 --> 00:02:37.806\nAmsterdam has one million inhabitants.\n\n38\n00:02:37.866 --> 00:02:40.206\nNow let's practice prices.\n\n39\n00:02:40.266 --> 00:02:45.386\nIn Dutch, we use EURO and CENT.\n\n40\n00:02:45.426 --> 00:02:50.986\nThe coffee costs two euros fifty.\n\n41\n00:02:51.006 --> 00:02:55.047\nThe coffee costs two euros fifty.\n\n42\n00:02:55.107 --> 00:02:59.647\nThe pants cost fifty euros.\n\n43\n00:02:59.667 --> 00:03:03.707\nThe pants cost fifty euros.\n\n44\n00:03:03.747 --> 00:03:08.547\nAn apple costs eighty cents.\n\n45\n00:03:08.587 --> 00:03:12.167\nAn apple costs eighty cents.\n\n46\n00:03:12.187 --> 00:03:15.847\nNow let's learn how to express years.\n\n47\n00:03:15.887 --> 00:03:23.868\nFor years in the 1900s, we say nineteen hundred followed by the number.\n\n48\n00:03:23.948 --> 00:03:29.648\nI was born in nineteen ninety-nine.\n\n49\n00:03:29.808 --> 00:03:34.468\nI was born in nineteen ninety-nine.\n\n50\n00:03:34.528 --> 00:03:41.088\nFor years in the 2000s, we say tweeduizend followed by the number.\n\n51\n00:03:41.148 --> 00:03:45.348\nIt is now two thousand twenty-four.\n\n52\n00:03:45.449 --> 00:03:49.709\nIt is now two thousand twenty-four.\n\n53\n00:03:49.809 --> 00:03:55.009\nMy friend lives here since two thousand ten.\n\n54\n00:03:55.049 --> 00:04:00.369\nMy friend lives here since two thousand ten.\n\n55\n00:04:00.449 --> 00:04:03.049\nFantastic practice today!\n\n56\n00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:11.609\nToday we learned: hundred, thousand, and million.\n\n57\n00:04:11.649 --> 00:04:19.090\nToday we learned: hundred, thousand, and million.\n\n58\n00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:22.590\nThank you and see you soon!\n\n59\n00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.990\nThank you and see you soon!\n
cw_opposites	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:06.080\nHello everyone! Welcome to today's Dutch vocabulary lesson.\n\n2\n00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:11.481\nToday we are going to learn common opposite words in Dutch.\n\n3\n00:00:11.541 --> 00:00:18.001\nLearning opposites helps us describe things easily in everyday conversations.\n\n4\n00:00:18.041 --> 00:00:22.021\nTegenstellingen in het Nederlands.\n\n5\n00:00:22.101 --> 00:00:24.741\nOpposites in Dutch.\n\n6\n00:00:24.861 --> 00:00:27.861\nAre you ready to practice together?\n\n7\n00:00:27.981 --> 00:00:30.581\nLaten we beginnen!\n\n8\n00:00:30.621 --> 00:00:32.661\nLet's begin!\n\n9\n00:00:32.761 --> 00:00:38.462\nOur first pair of words is GROOT and KLEIN.\n\n10\n00:00:38.542 --> 00:00:42.702\nGroot means big or large.\n\n11\n00:00:42.782 --> 00:00:46.602\nHet huis is heel groot.\n\n12\n00:00:46.622 --> 00:00:49.922\nThe house is very big.\n\n13\n00:00:49.962 --> 00:00:54.302\nKlein means small or little.\n\n14\n00:00:54.322 --> 00:00:58.003\nDe muis is erg klein.\n\n15\n00:00:58.023 --> 00:01:01.363\nThe mouse is very small.\n\n16\n00:01:01.383 --> 00:01:06.123\nNext, we have WARM and KOUD.\n\n17\n00:01:06.163 --> 00:01:09.523\nWarm means warm or hot.\n\n18\n00:01:09.543 --> 00:01:13.803\nDe soep is erg warm.\n\n19\n00:01:13.823 --> 00:01:18.263\nThe soup is very warm.\n\n20\n00:01:18.303 --> 00:01:22.044\nKoud means cold.\n\n21\n00:01:22.104 --> 00:01:26.364\nHet ijs is heel koud.\n\n22\n00:01:26.384 --> 00:01:30.464\nThe ice is very cold.\n\n23\n00:01:30.484 --> 00:01:35.604\nNow let's practice SNEL and LANGZAAM.\n\n24\n00:01:35.664 --> 00:01:40.184\nSnel means fast or quick.\n\n25\n00:01:40.224 --> 00:01:44.565\nDe auto rijdt heel snel.\n\n26\n00:01:44.585 --> 00:01:49.045\nThe car drives very fast.\n\n27\n00:01:49.105 --> 00:01:52.865\nLangzaam means slow.\n\n28\n00:01:52.905 --> 00:01:57.805\nDe schildpad loopt erg langzaam.\n\n29\n00:01:57.825 --> 00:02:02.165\nThe turtle walks very slowly.\n\n30\n00:02:02.245 --> 00:02:07.246\nOur next pair is OUD and JONG.\n\n31\n00:02:07.326 --> 00:02:10.806\nOud means old.\n\n32\n00:02:10.846 --> 00:02:15.066\nDe opa is erg oud.\n\n33\n00:02:15.086 --> 00:02:19.446\nThe grandfather is very old.\n\n34\n00:02:19.526 --> 00:02:23.246\nJong means young.\n\n35\n00:02:23.306 --> 00:02:26.666\nHet kind is nog jong.\n\n36\n00:02:26.686 --> 00:02:31.467\nThe child is still young.\n\n37\n00:02:31.487 --> 00:02:36.787\nNext, we have DUUR and GOEDKOOP.\n\n38\n00:02:36.847 --> 00:02:40.847\nDuur means expensive.\n\n39\n00:02:40.887 --> 00:02:45.967\nDie fiets is erg duur.\n\n40\n00:02:45.987 --> 00:02:51.248\nThat bicycle is very expensive.\n\n41\n00:02:51.288 --> 00:02:55.548\nGoedkoop means cheap.\n\n42\n00:02:55.588 --> 00:03:01.028\nDeze appel is heel goedkoop.\n\n43\n00:03:01.068 --> 00:03:06.168\nThis apple is very cheap.\n\n44\n00:03:06.268 --> 00:03:11.648\nNow let's look at LICHT and DONKER.\n\n45\n00:03:11.748 --> 00:03:16.689\nLicht means light or bright.\n\n46\n00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:21.809\nDe kamer is heel licht.\n\n47\n00:03:21.829 --> 00:03:27.009\nThe room is very light.\n\n48\n00:03:27.069 --> 00:03:31.069\nDonker means dark.\n\n49\n00:03:31.109 --> 00:03:36.049\nDe nacht is erg donker.\n\n50\n00:03:36.069 --> 00:03:41.290\nThe night is very dark.\n\n51\n00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:46.410\nNext up are HOOG and LAAG.\n\n52\n00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:51.430\nHoog means high or tall.\n\n53\n00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:57.570\nDe berg is erg hoog.\n\n54\n00:03:57.730 --> 00:04:04.311\nThe mountain is very high.\n\n55\n00:04:04.391 --> 00:04:08.631\nLaag means low.\n\n56\n00:04:08.671 --> 00:04:13.631\nDe stoel is vrij laag.\n\n57\n00:04:13.651 --> 00:04:17.611\nThe chair is quite low.\n\n58\n00:04:17.671 --> 00:04:22.852\nLet's continue with OPEN and DICHT.\n\n59\n00:04:22.932 --> 00:04:27.072\nOpen means open.\n\n60\n00:04:27.112 --> 00:04:31.592\nDe deur is nu open.\n\n61\n00:04:31.632 --> 00:04:35.512\nThe door is open now.\n\n62\n00:04:35.552 --> 00:04:39.692\nDicht means closed.\n\n63\n00:04:39.752 --> 00:04:44.232\nHet raam is nu dicht.\n\n64\n00:04:44.252 --> 00:04:48.213\nThe window is closed now.\n\n65\n00:04:48.233 --> 00:04:53.873\nNow we have BLIJ and VERDRIETIG.\n\n66\n00:04:53.933 --> 00:04:57.913\nBlij means happy.\n\n67\n00:04:57.953 --> 00:05:02.753\nDe jongen is erg blij.\n\n68\n00:05:02.773 --> 00:05:06.853\nThe boy is very happy.\n\n69\n00:05:06.913 --> 00:05:11.494\nVerdrietig means sad.\n\n70\n00:05:11.554 --> 00:05:16.634\nHet meisje is soms verdrietig.\n\n71\n00:05:16.654 --> 00:05:20.434\nThe girl is sometimes sad.\n\n72\n00:05:20.514 --> 00:05:26.554\nOur last pair is MOOI and LELIJK.\n\n73\n00:05:26.614 --> 00:05:32.315\nMooi means beautiful or pretty.\n\n74\n00:05:32.355 --> 00:05:38.835\nDie bloem is erg mooi.\n\n75\n00:05:38.875 --> 00:05:42.995\nThat flower is very beautiful.\n\n76\n00:05:43.075 --> 00:05:47.435\nLelijk means ugly.\n\n77\n00:05:47.495 --> 00:05:53.036\nHet oude schilderij is lelijk.\n\n78\n00:05:53.056 --> 00:05:59.156\nThe old painting is ugly.\n\n79\n00:05:59.176 --> 00:06:04.916\nGreat job today! Let's do a quick spoken recap.\n\n80\n00:06:04.976 --> 00:06:08.996\nVandaag leerden we:\n\n81\n00:06:09.016 --> 00:06:11.856\nToday we learned:\n\n82\n00:06:11.996 --> 00:06:19.177\ngroot, klein, warm, koud,\n\n83\n00:06:19.237 --> 00:06:26.397\nbig, small, warm, cold,\n\n84\n00:06:26.477 --> 00:06:33.677\nsnel, langzaam, oud, jong,\n\n85\n00:06:34.457 --> 00:06:41.657\nfast, slow, old, young,\n\n86\n00:06:42.278 --> 00:06:49.478\nduur, goedkoop, licht, donker,\n\n87\n00:06:50.138 --> 00:06:57.338\nexpensive, cheap, light, dark,\n\n88\n00:06:57.698 --> 00:07:04.219\nhoog, laag, open, dicht,\n\n89\n00:07:04.279 --> 00:07:11.479\nhigh, low, open, closed,\n\n90\n00:07:12.199 --> 00:07:20.599\nblij, verdrietig, mooi, en lelijk.\n\n91\n00:07:20.659 --> 00:07:28.820\nhappy, sad, beautiful, and ugly.\n\n92\n00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:33.500\nFantastic work! Keep practicing these words every day.\n\n93\n00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:34.680\nSee you in the next lesson!\n
