n62\n00:04:36.552 --> 00:04:40.692\nDicht means closed.\n\n63\n00:04:40.752 --> 00:04:45.232\nThe window is closed now.\n\n64\n00:04:45.252 --> 00:04:49.213\nThe window is closed now.\n\n65\n00:04:49.233 --> 00:04:54.873\nNow we have BLIJ and VERDRIETIG.\n\n66\n00:04:54.933 --> 00:04:58.913\nBlij means happy.\n\n67\n00:04:58.953 --> 00:05:03.753\nThe boy is very happy.\n\n68\n00:05:03.773 --> 00:05:07.853\nThe boy is very happy.\n\n69\n00:05:07.913 --> 00:05:12.494\nVerdrietig means sad.\n\n70\n00:05:12.554 --> 00:05:17.634\nThe girl is sometimes sad.\n\n71\n00:05:17.654 --> 00:05:21.434\nThe girl is sometimes sad.\n\n72\n00:05:21.514 --> 00:05:27.554\nOur last pair is MOOI and LELIJK.\n\n73\n00:05:27.614 --> 00:05:33.315\nMooi means beautiful or pretty.\n\n74\n00:05:33.355 --> 00:05:39.835\nThat flower is very beautiful.\n\n75\n00:05:39.875 --> 00:05:43.995\nThat flower is very beautiful.\n\n76\n00:05:44.075 --> 00:05:48.435\nLelijk means ugly.\n\n77\n00:05:48.495 --> 00:05:54.036\nThe old painting is ugly.\n\n78\n00:05:54.056 --> 00:06:00.156\nThe old painting is ugly.\n\n79\n00:06:00.176 --> 00:06:05.916\nGreat job today! Let's do a quick spoken recap.\n\n80\n00:06:05.976 --> 00:06:09.996\nToday we learned:\n\n81\n00:06:10.016 --> 00:06:12.856\nToday we learned:\n\n82\n00:06:12.996 --> 00:06:20.177\nbig, small, warm, cold,\n\n83\n00:06:20.237 --> 00:06:27.397\nbig, small, warm, cold,\n\n84\n00:06:27.477 --> 00:06:34.677\nfast, slow, old, young,\n\n85\n00:06:35.457 --> 00:06:42.657\nfast, slow, old, young,\n\n86\n00:06:43.278 --> 00:06:50.478\nexpensive, cheap, light, dark,\n\n87\n00:06:51.138 --> 00:06:58.338\nexpensive, cheap, light, dark,\n\n88\n00:06:58.698 --> 00:07:05.219\nhigh, low, open, closed,\n\n89\n00:07:05.279 --> 00:07:12.479\nhigh, low, open, closed,\n\n90\n00:07:13.199 --> 00:07:21.599\nhappy, sad, beautiful, and ugly.\n\n91\n00:07:21.659 --> 00:07:29.820\nhappy, sad, beautiful, and ugly.\n\n92\n00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:34.500\nFantastic work! Keep practicing these words every day.\n\n93\n00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:35.680\nSee you in the next lesson!\n
cw_quantities	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:02.980\nWelcome to our Dutch lesson!\n\n2\n00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.101\nToday we learn quantity words.\n\n3\n00:00:07.161 --> 00:00:10.501\nLaten we beginnen!\n\n4\n00:00:10.581 --> 00:00:14.682\nOur first word is VEEL.\n\n5\n00:00:14.742 --> 00:00:19.563\nVEEL means a lot or many.\n\n6\n00:00:19.623 --> 00:00:24.163\nIk drink veel water.\n\n7\n00:00:24.243 --> 00:00:28.604\nZij heeft veel boeken.\n\n8\n00:00:28.644 --> 00:00:33.024\nNext, we have WEINIG.\n\n9\n00:00:33.104 --> 00:00:38.105\nWEINIG means little or few.\n\n10\n00:00:38.165 --> 00:00:43.086\nHij slaapt weinig uren.\n\n11\n00:00:43.146 --> 00:00:47.626\nWij hebben weinig tijd.\n\n12\n00:00:47.666 --> 00:00:51.787\nNow we learn MEER.\n\n13\n00:00:51.827 --> 00:00:56.368\nMEER means more in English.\n\n14\n00:00:56.448 --> 00:01:00.848\nIk wil meer koffie.\n\n15\n00:01:00.908 --> 00:01:05.509\nJij koopt meer appels.\n\n16\n00:01:05.629 --> 00:01:09.609\nThe opposite is MINDER.\n\n17\n00:01:09.649 --> 00:01:14.470\nMINDER means less or fewer.\n\n18\n00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:19.031\nHij eet minder suiker.\n\n19\n00:01:19.111 --> 00:01:23.651\nZij werkt minder uren.\n\n20\n00:01:23.751 --> 00:01:27.112\nOur next word is GENOEG.\n\n21\n00:01:27.152 --> 00:01:30.652\nGENOEG means enough.\n\n22\n00:01:30.712 --> 00:01:34.653\nIk heb genoeg geld.\n\n23\n00:01:34.733 --> 00:01:38.693\nEr is genoeg eten.\n\n24\n00:01:38.713 --> 00:01:41.554\nNow let's practice HEEL.\n\n25\n00:01:41.654 --> 00:01:44.954\nHEEL means very.\n\n26\n00:01:44.994 --> 00:01:48.415\nDit is heel goed.\n\n27\n00:01:48.455 --> 00:01:52.055\nHet is heel warm.\n\n28\n00:01:52.095 --> 00:01:55.156\nAnother word is ERG.\n\n29\n00:01:55.256 --> 00:01:58.736\nERG also means very.\n\n30\n00:01:58.776 --> 00:02:02.136\nHet is erg koud.\n\n31\n00:02:02.156 --> 00:02:05.717\nDat is erg leuk.\n\n32\n00:02:05.737 --> 00:02:08.877\nLet's review our new words.\n\n33\n00:02:08.917 --> 00:02:16.758\nVandaag leerden we: veel, weinig, meer.\n\n34\n00:02:16.818 --> 00:02:24.840\nEn ook minder, genoeg, heel, erg.\n\n35\n00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:27.160\nGreat job today!\n\n36\n00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:28.500\nSee you next time!\n
cw_quantities	en	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:03.980\nWelcome to our Dutch lesson!\n\n2\n00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.101\nToday we learn quantity words.\n\n3\n00:00:08.161 --> 00:00:11.501\nLet's begin!\n\n4\n00:00:11.581 --> 00:00:15.682\nOur first word is VEEL.\n\n5\n00:00:15.742 --> 00:00:20.563\nVEEL means a lot or many.\n\n6\n00:00:20.623 --> 00:00:25.163\nI drink a lot of water.\n\n7\n00:00:25.243 --> 00:00:29.604\nShe has many books.\n\n8\n00:00:29.644 --> 00:00:34.024\nNext, we have WEINIG.\n\n9\n00:00:34.104 --> 00:00:39.105\nWEINIG means little or few.\n\n10\n00:00:39.165 --> 00:00:44.086\nHe sleeps few hours.\n\n11\n00:00:44.146 --> 00:00:48.626\nWe have little time.\n\n12\n00:00:48.666 --> 00:00:52.787\nNow we learn MEER.\n\n13\n00:00:52.827 --> 00:00:57.368\nMEER means more in English.\n\n14\n00:00:57.448 --> 00:01:01.848\nI want more coffee.\n\n15\n00:01:01.908 --> 00:01:06.509\nYou buy more apples.\n\n16\n00:01:06.629 --> 00:01:10.609\nThe opposite is MINDER.\n\n17\n00:01:10.649 --> 00:01:15.470\nMINDER means less or fewer.\n\n18\n00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:20.031\nHe eats less sugar.\n\n19\n00:01:20.111 --> 00:01:24.651\nShe works fewer hours.\n\n20\n00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:28.112\nOur next word is GENOEG.\n\n21\n00:01:28.152 --> 00:01:31.652\nGENOEG means enough.\n\n22\n00:01:31.712 --> 00:01:35.653\nI have enough money.\n\n23\n00:01:35.733 --> 00:01:39.693\nThere is enough food.\n\n24\n00:01:39.713 --> 00:01:42.554\nNow let's practice HEEL.\n\n25\n00:01:42.654 --> 00:01:45.954\nHEEL means very.\n\n26\n00:01:45.994 --> 00:01:49.415\nThis is very good.\n\n27\n00:01:49.455 --> 00:01:53.055\nIt is very warm.\n\n28\n00:01:53.095 --> 00:01:56.156\nAnother word is ERG.\n\n29\n00:01:56.256 --> 00:01:59.736\nERG also means very.\n\n30\n00:01:59.776 --> 00:02:03.136\nIt is very cold.\n\n31\n00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:06.717\nThat is very nice.\n\n32\n00:02:06.737 --> 00:02:09.877\nLet's review our new words.\n\n33\n00:02:09.917 --> 00:02:17.758\nToday we learned: much, little, more.\n\n34\n00:02:17.818 --> 00:02:25.840\nAnd also less, enough, very, very.\n\n35\n00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:28.160\nGreat job today!\n\n36\n00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:29.500\nSee you next time!\n
cw_seasons	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.200\nHello everyone! Welcome to today's Dutch lesson.\n\n2\n00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:10.881\nToday we are going to learn about the seasons and weather in Dutch.\n\n3\n00:00:10.961 --> 00:00:16.081\nLearning weather words will help you talk about daily life easily.\n\n4\n00:00:16.141 --> 00:00:19.361\nAre you ready to practice?\n\n5\n00:00:19.441 --> 00:00:23.021\nLaten we beginnen!\n\n6\n00:00:23.081 --> 00:00:27.202\nFirst, let's learn the four main seasons.\n\n7\n00:00:27.242 --> 00:00:33.462\nOur first word is de lente, which means spring.\n\n8\n00:00:33.522 --> 00:00:38.342\nHet is lente in Nederland.\n\n9\n00:00:38.382 --> 00:00:43.623\nDe bloemen bloeien in de lente.\n\n10\n00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:49.543\nNext is de zomer, which means summer.\n\n11\n00:00:49.603 --> 00:00:54.423\nDe zomer is heel mooi.\n\n12\n00:00:54.483 --> 00:00:58.804\nIk ga zwemmen in de zomer.\n\n13\n00:00:58.884 --> 00:01:06.164\nOur third season is de herfst, which means autumn or fall.\n\n14\n00:01:06.204 --> 00:01:10.184\nDe herfst is erg nat.\n\n15\n00:01:10.224 --> 00:01:13.985\nHet waait hard in de herfst.\n\n16\n00:01:14.005 --> 00:01:19.745\nThe fourth season is de winter, which means winter.\n\n17\n00:01:19.785 --> 00:01:22.985\nDe winter is koud.\n\n18\n00:01:23.025 --> 00:01:26.625\nHet sneeuwt in de winter.\n\n19\n00:01:26.665 --> 00:01:30.706\nNow, let's learn general weather vocabulary.\n\n20\n00:01:30.726 --> 00:01:35.766\nThe word het weer means the weather.\n\n21\n00:01:35.806 --> 00:01:39.686\nHet weer is vandaag goed.\n\n22\n00:01:39.726 --> 00:01:43.006\nWat is het weer vandaag?\n\n23\n00:01:43.046 --> 00:01:47.727\nNext, de zon means the sun.\n\n24\n00:01:47.747 --> 00:01:51.467\nDe zon schijnt vandaag fel.\n\n25\n00:01:51.527 --> 00:01:55.247\nIk zie de zon opkomen.\n\n26\n00:01:55.267 --> 00:02:00.047\nThe word de regen means the rain.\n\n27\n00:02:00.067 --> 00:02:03.608\nDe regen valt op de straat.\n\n28\n00:02:03.688 --> 00:02:07.188\nIk loop door de regen.\n\n29\n00:02:07.228 --> 00:02:11.948\nNext is de wind, which means the wind.\n\n30\n00:02:11.988 --> 00:02:16.348\nDe wind is heel sterk.\n\n31\n00:02:16.428 --> 00:02:20.629\nIk voel de koude wind.\n\n32\n00:02:20.649 --> 00:02:26.369\nThe word de sneeuw means the snow.\n\n33\n00:02:26.389 --> 00:02:30.729\nDe sneeuw is erg koud.\n\n34\n00:02:30.769 --> 00:02:35.449\nDe kinderen spelen in de sneeuw.\n\n35\n00:02:35.489 --> 00:02:41.210\nNext, de wolk means the cloud.\n\n36\n00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:45.350\nIk zie een grote wolk.\n\n37\n00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:49.730\nDe wolk is heel grijs.\n\n38\n00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:55.371\nNow let's practice adjectives used to describe weather.\n\n39\n00:02:55.391 --> 00:03:01.331\nThe word warm means warm or hot.\n\n40\n00:03:01.351 --> 00:03:05.571\nHet is vandaag erg warm.\n\n41\n00:03:05.591 --> 00:03:09.912\nDe thee is lekker warm.\n\n42\n00:03:09.932 --> 00:03:15.132\nThe word koud means cold.\n\n43\n00:03:15.152 --> 00:03:19.372\nDe wind is erg koud.\n\n44\n00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:21.912\nIk vind het ijs koud.\n\n45\n00:03:21.932 --> 00:03:26.153\nThe word nat means wet.\n\n46\n00:03:26.193 --> 00:03:29.893\nMijn jas is erg nat.\n\n47\n00:03:29.933 --> 00:03:33.673\nDe straat is vandaag nat.\n\n48\n00:03:33.693 --> 00:03:38.333\nThe word droog means dry.\n\n49\n00:03:38.353 --> 00:03:41.934\nDe grond is weer droog.\n\n50\n00:03:41.974 --> 00:03:45.514\nBinnen blijven wij droog.\n\n51\n00:03:45.634 --> 00:03:51.394\nLet's learn a few useful items for different weather conditions.\n\n52\n00:03:51.414 --> 00:03:57.274\nThe word de paraplu means the umbrella.\n\n53\n00:03:57.334 --> 00:04:00.535\nIk neem een paraplu mee.\n\n54\n00:04:00.575 --> 00:04:04.815\nDe paraplu is erg groot.\n\n55\n00:04:04.835 --> 00:04:11.235\nThe word de jas means the coat or jacket.\n\n56\n00:04:11.295 --> 00:04:14.175\nIk trek een jas aan.\n\n57\n00:04:14.215 --> 00:04:17.916\nDeze jas is heel warm.\n\n58\n00:04:17.936 --> 00:04:23.576\nThe word de storm means the storm.\n\n59\n00:04:23.656 --> 00:04:26.576\nEr komt een grote storm.\n\n60\n00:04:26.616 --> 00:04:30.696\nDe storm maakt veel lawaai.\n\n61\n00:04:30.756 --> 00:04:36.597\nFinally, de schaduw means the shade or shadow.\n\n62\n00:04:36.637 --> 00:04:39.737\nWe zitten in de schaduw.\n\n63\n00:04:39.757 --> 00:04:43.317\nDe schaduw geeft wat koelte.\n\n64\n00:04:43.337 --> 00:04:49.118\nGreat job! Let's do a quick spoken recap of what we learned today.\n\n65\n00:04:49.158 --> 00:05:22.500\nToday we learned: de lente, de zomer, de herfst, de winter, het weer, de zon, de regen, de wind, de sneeuw, de wolk, warm, koud, nat, droog, de paraplu, de jas, de storm, and de schaduw.\n\n66\n00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:25.880\nKeep practicing these weather words every day!\n\n67\n00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:28.600\nSee you in the next Dutch lesson. Goodbye!\n
cw_seasons	en	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:06.200\nHello everyone! Welcome to today's Dutch lesson.\n\n2\n00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:11.881\nToday we are going to learn about the seasons and weather in Dutch.\n\n3\n00:00:11.961 --> 00:00:17.081\nLearning weather words will help you talk about daily life easily.\n\n4\n00:00:17.141 --> 00:00:20.361\nAre you ready to practice?\n\n5\n00:00:20.441 --> 00:00:24.021\nLet's get started!\n\n6\n00:00:24.081 --> 00:00:28.202\nFirst, let's learn the four main seasons.\n\n7\n00:00:28.242 --> 00:00:34.462\nOur first word is de lente, which means spring.\n\n8\n00:00:34.522 --> 00:00:39.342\nIt is spring in the Netherlands.\n\n9\n00:00:39.382 --> 00:00:44.623\nThe flowers bloom in the spring.\n\n10\n00:00:44.643 --> 00:00:50.543\nNext is de zomer, which means summer.\n\n11\n00:00:50.603 --> 00:00:55.423\nSummer is very beautiful.\n\n12\n00:00:55.483 --> 00:00:59.804\nI go swimming in the summer.\n\n13\n00:00:59.884 --> 00:01:07.164\nOur third season is de herfst, which means autumn or fall.\n\n14\n00:01:07.204 --> 00:01:11.184\nAutumn is very wet.\n\n15\n00:01:11.224 --> 00:01:14.985\nIt is very windy in autumn.\n\n16\n00:01:15.005 --> 00:01:20.745\nThe fourth season is de winter, which means winter.\n\n17\n00:01:20.785 --> 00:01:23.985\nWinter is cold.\n\n18\n00:01:24.025 --> 00:01:27.625\nIt snows in the winter.\n\n19\n00:01:27.665 --> 00:01:31.706\nNow, let's learn general weather vocabulary.\n\n20\n00:01:31.726 --> 00:01:36.766\nThe word het weer means the weather.\n\n21\n00:01:36.806 --> 00:01:40.686\nThe weather is good today.\n\n22\n00:01:40.726 --> 00:01:44.006\nWhat is the weather today?\n\n23\n00:01:44.046 --> 00:01:48.727\nNext, de zon means the sun.\n\n24\n00:01:48.747 --> 00:01:52.467\nThe sun shines brightly today.\n\n25\n00:01:52.527 --> 00:01:56.247\nI see the sun rising.\n\n26\n00:01:56.267 --> 00:02:01.047\nThe word de regen means the rain.\n\n27\n00:02:01.067 --> 00:02:04.608\nThe rain falls on the street.\n\n28\n00:02:04.688 --> 00:02:08.188\nI walk through the rain.\n\n29\n00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:12.948\nNext is de wind, which means the wind.\n\n30\n00:02:12.988 --> 00:02:17.348\nThe wind is very strong.\n\n31\n00:02:17.428 --> 00:02:21.629\nI feel the cold wind.\n\n32\n00:02:21.649 --> 00:02:27.369\nThe word de sneeuw means the snow.\n\n33\n00:02:27.389 --> 00:02:31.729\nThe snow is very cold.\n\n34\n00:02:31.769 --> 00:02:36.449\nThe children play in the snow.\n\n35\n00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:42.210\nNext, de wolk means the cloud.\n\n36\n00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:46.350\nI see a big cloud.\n\n37\n00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:50.730\nThe cloud is very grey.\n\n38\n00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:56.371\nNow let's practice adjectives used to describe weather.\n\n39\n00:02:56.391 --> 00:03:02.331\nThe word warm means warm or hot.\n\n40\n00:03:02.351 --> 00:03:06.571\nIt is very warm today.\n\n41\n00:03:06.591 --> 00:03:10.912\nThe tea is nice and warm.\n\n42\n00:03:10.932 --> 00:03:16.132\nThe word koud means cold.\n\n43\n00:03:16.152 --> 00:03:20.372\nThe wind is very cold.\n\n44\n00:03:20.432 --> 00:03:22.912\nI find the ice cold.\n\n45\n00:03:22.932 --> 00:03:27.153\nThe word nat means wet.\n\n46\n00:03:27.193 --> 00:03:30.893\nMy coat is very wet.\n\n47\n00:03:30.933 --> 00:03:34.673\nThe street is wet today.\n\n48\n00:03:34.693 --> 00:03:39.333\nThe word droog means dry.\n\n49\n00:03:39.353 --> 00:03:42.934\nThe ground is dry again.\n\n50\n00:03:42.974 --> 00:03:46.514\nInside we stay dry.\n\n51\n00:03:46.634 --> 00:03:52.394\nLet's learn a few useful items for different weather conditions.\n\n52\n00:03:52.414 --> 00:03:58.274\nThe word de paraplu means the umbrella.\n\n53\n00:03:58.334 --> 00:04:01.535\nI take an umbrella with me.\n\n54\n00:04:01.575 --> 00:04:05.815\nThe umbrella is very big.\n\n55\n00:04:05.835 --> 00:04:12.235\nThe word de jas means the coat or jacket.\n\n56\n00:04:12.295 --> 00:04:15.175\nI put on a coat.\n\n57\n00:04:15.215 --> 00:04:18.916\nThis coat is very warm.\n\n58\n00:04:18.936 --> 00:04:24.576\nThe word de storm means the storm.\n\n59\n00:04:24.656 --> 00:04:27.576\nA big storm is coming.\n\n60\n00:04:27.616 --> 00:04:31.696\nThe storm makes a lot of noise.\n\n61\n00:04:31.756 --> 00:04:37.597\nFinally, de schaduw means the shade or shadow.\n\n62\n00:04:37.637 --> 00:04:40.737\nWe are sitting in the shade.\n\n63\n00:04:40.757 --> 00:04:44.317\nThe shade gives some coolness.\n\n64\n00:04:44.337 --> 00:04:50.118\nGreat job! Let's do a quick spoken recap of what we learned today.\n\n65\n00:04:50.158 --> 00:05:23.500\nToday we learned: de lente, de zomer, de herfst, de winter, het weer, de zon, de regen, de wind, de sneeuw, de wolk, warm, koud, nat, droog, de paraplu, de jas, de storm, and de schaduw.\n\n66\n00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:26.880\nKeep practicing these weather words every day!\n\n67\n00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:29.600\nSee you in the next Dutch lesson. Goodbye!\n
cw_shopping_words	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:04.660\nWelcome to Dutch language practice.\n\n2\n00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:09.520\nToday we will learn common shopping words.\n\n3\n00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:13.961\nAre you ready to practice?\n\n4\n00:00:14.001 --> 00:00:17.321\nLaten we beginnen!\n\n5\n00:00:17.461 --> 00:00:19.921\nLet us begin!\n\n6\n00:00:20.001 --> 00:00:27.321\nOur first word is winkel, which means shop.\n\n7\n00:00:27.381 --> 00:00:31.821\nIk ga naar de winkel.\n\n8\n00:00:32.001 --> 00:00:35.261\nI go to the shop.\n\n9\n00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:40.022\nDe winkel is vandaag open.\n\n10\n00:00:40.042 --> 00:00:43.942\nThe shop is open today.\n\n11\n00:00:43.982 --> 00:00:51.122\nNext, we have kopen, which means to buy.\n\n12\n00:00:51.182 --> 00:00:55.162\nIk koop een nieuw boek.\n\n13\n00:00:55.322 --> 00:00:58.522\nI buy a new book.\n\n14\n00:00:58.562 --> 00:01:02.762\nWij kopen lekker eten.\n\n15\n00:01:02.822 --> 00:01:06.263\nWe buy delicious food.\n\n16\n00:01:06.283 --> 00:01:09.803\nNow let us talk about prices.\n\n17\n00:01:09.823 --> 00:01:14.163\nThe word prijs means price.\n\n18\n00:01:14.203 --> 00:01:17.583\nWat is de prijs?\n\n19\n00:01:17.623 --> 00:01:20.803\nWhat is the price?\n\n20\n00:01:20.843 --> 00:01:25.503\nDe prijs is vijf euro.\n\n21\n00:01:25.543 --> 00:01:29.623\nThe price is five euros.\n\n22\n00:01:29.683 --> 00:01:35.824\nIf something costs a lot, it is duur.\n\n23\n00:01:35.864 --> 00:01:39.804\nDuur means expensive.\n\n24\n00:01:39.864 --> 00:01:44.944\nDie grote tas is duur.\n\n25\n00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:49.304\nThat big bag is expensive.\n\n26\n00:01:49.364 --> 00:01:54.224\nHet brood is niet duur.\n\n27\n00:01:54.244 --> 00:01:58.424\nThe bread is not expensive.\n\n28\n00:01:58.444 --> 00:02:03.545\nThe opposite of expensive is goedkoop.\n\n29\n00:02:03.585 --> 00:02:07.765\nGoedkoop means cheap.\n\n30\n00:02:07.805 --> 00:02:12.685\nDeze appels zijn goedkoop.\n\n31\n00:02:12.705 --> 00:02:16.005\nThese apples are cheap.\n\n32\n00:02:16.065 --> 00:02:20.865\nHet water is heel goedkoop.\n\n33\n00:02:20.885 --> 00:02:23.105\nThe water is very cheap.\n\n34\n00:02:23.125 --> 00:02:27.826\nWhen you get a deal, look for korting.\n\n35\n00:02:27.866 --> 00:02:31.986\nKorting means discount.\n\n36\n00:02:32.086 --> 00:02:36.266\nEr is nu veel korting.\n\n37\n00:02:36.286 --> 00:02:39.806\nThere is much discount now.\n\n38\n00:02:39.866 --> 00:02:43.606\nKrijg ik een korting?\n\n39\n00:02:43.646 --> 00:02:45.466\nDo I get a discount?\n\n40\n00:02:45.506 --> 00:02:50.706\nWhen you are done shopping, head to the kassa.\n\n41\n00:02:50.746 --> 00:02:56.467\nKassa means cash register or checkout.\n\n42\n00:02:56.507 --> 00:03:00.567\nDe kassa is daar.\n\n43\n00:03:00.587 --> 00:03:04.427\nThe cash register is over there.\n\n44\n00:03:04.487 --> 00:03:08.647\nIk sta bij de kassa.\n\n45\n00:03:08.787 --> 00:03:11.147\nI am standing at the cash register.\n\n46\n00:03:11.227 --> 00:03:16.427\nAt the checkout, you need to betalen.\n\n47\n00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:20.608\nBetalen means to pay.\n\n48\n00:03:20.688 --> 00:03:25.168\nIk betaal met een kaart.\n\n49\n00:03:25.308 --> 00:03:27.388\nI pay with a card.\n\n50\n00:03:27.428 --> 00:03:31.568\nWij betalen in de winkel.\n\n51\n00:03:31.608 --> 00:03:33.868\nWe pay in the store.\n\n52\n00:03:33.908 --> 00:03:38.928\nGreat job! Let us recap what we learned.\n\n53\n00:03:38.988 --> 00:03:43.168\nVandaag leerden we deze woorden.\n\n54\n00:03:43.208 --> 00:03:46.689\nToday we learned these words.\n\n55\n00:03:46.729 --> 00:03:50.069\nIk koop in de winkel.\n\n56\n00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:53.129\nI buy in the shop.\n\n57\n00:03:53.149 --> 00:03:56.849\nDe prijs is niet duur.\n\n58\n00:03:56.869 --> 00:04:00.369\nThe price is not expensive.\n\n59\n00:04:00.429 --> 00:04:03.649\nHet is heel goedkoop.\n\n60\n00:04:03.709 --> 00:04:06.589\nIt is very cheap.\n\n61\n00:04:06.649 --> 00:04:10.089\nIk krijg ook korting.\n\n62\n00:04:10.209 --> 00:04:1