together early.\n\n59\n00:03:39.967 --> 00:03:44.287\nListen to this incorrect Dutch sentence.\n\n60\n00:03:44.347 --> 00:03:48.107\nIk ga werken morgen.\n\n61\n00:03:48.147 --> 00:03:52.147\nThat sentence is incorrect in Dutch!\n\n62\n00:03:52.207 --> 00:03:55.247\nWhy is that sentence wrong?\n\n63\n00:03:55.307 --> 00:03:59.648\nWerken must go to the end!\n\n64\n00:03:59.708 --> 00:04:03.648\nHere is the correct sentence again.\n\n65\n00:04:03.728 --> 00:04:08.008\nIk ga morgen werken.\n\n66\n00:04:08.188 --> 00:04:12.528\nI am going to work tomorrow.\n\n67\n00:04:12.588 --> 00:04:16.788\nSecond mistake: forgetting the full infinitive.\n\n68\n00:04:16.888 --> 00:04:21.088\nListen to another incorrect sentence.\n\n69\n00:04:21.148 --> 00:04:24.908\nWij gaan eten kook.\n\n70\n00:04:24.948 --> 00:04:29.989\nThat is wrong because kook is conjugated.\n\n71\n00:04:30.029 --> 00:04:35.329\nYou must always use the infinitive koken!\n\n72\n00:04:35.429 --> 00:04:38.209\nLet's fix that sentence now.\n\n73\n00:04:38.269 --> 00:04:42.329\nWij gaan eten koken.\n\n74\n00:04:42.369 --> 00:04:45.629\nWe are going to cook food.\n\n75\n00:04:45.689 --> 00:04:49.569\nHere is your handy memory anchor tip.\n\n76\n00:04:49.729 --> 00:04:54.729\nGaan is second, action verb is last!\n\n77\n00:04:54.749 --> 00:04:58.609\nKeep the infinitive at the very end!\n\n78\n00:04:58.669 --> 00:05:02.130\nLet's do a fast final review.\n\n79\n00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:06.210\nVandaag leerden we de toekomst.\n\n80\n00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:10.390\nToday we learned the future tense.\n\n81\n00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:15.810\nUse conjugated gaan plus full infinitive.\n\n82\n00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:16.490\nTot de volgende keer!\n\n83\n00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:17.070\nUntil next time!\n
grammar_future_zullen	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:08.041\nImagine promising a friend: I will help you tomorrow!\n\n2\n00:00:08.101 --> 00:00:12.841\nHow do you express the future in Dutch?\n\n3\n00:00:12.881 --> 00:00:17.761\nWe use the auxiliary verb zullen.\n\n4\n00:00:17.801 --> 00:00:22.982\nIt works just like the English word will.\n\n5\n00:00:23.042 --> 00:00:26.282\nLet's see how it works!\n\n6\n00:00:26.422 --> 00:00:30.702\nLaten we beginnen!\n\n7\n00:00:30.822 --> 00:00:33.543\nLet's start!\n\n8\n00:00:33.603 --> 00:00:38.123\nFirst, let's look at the forms.\n\n9\n00:00:38.183 --> 00:00:44.524\nFor I, we use ik zal.\n\n10\n00:00:44.624 --> 00:00:48.644\nIk zal je helpen.\n\n11\n00:00:48.824 --> 00:00:51.724\nI will help you.\n\n12\n00:00:51.804 --> 00:00:58.225\nFor you, we say jij zult.\n\n13\n00:00:58.305 --> 00:01:03.165\nJij zult snel leren.\n\n14\n00:01:03.245 --> 00:01:07.085\nYou will learn quickly.\n\n15\n00:01:07.125 --> 00:01:14.666\nFor he, she, or it, we use zal.\n\n16\n00:01:14.726 --> 00:01:19.566\nHij zal morgen komen.\n\n17\n00:01:19.626 --> 00:01:23.367\nHe will come tomorrow.\n\n18\n00:01:23.427 --> 00:01:27.087\nHet zal morgen regenen.\n\n19\n00:01:27.147 --> 00:01:29.647\nIt will rain tomorrow.\n\n20\n00:01:29.687 --> 00:01:34.068\nFor plural forms, we use zullen.\n\n21\n00:01:34.128 --> 00:01:37.948\nWij zullen samen eten.\n\n22\n00:01:37.988 --> 00:01:40.408\nWe will eat together.\n\n23\n00:01:40.428 --> 00:01:44.028\nNow, let's try a quick prompt!\n\n24\n00:01:44.089 --> 00:01:47.549\nHow would you say: I will call?\n\n25\n00:01:47.569 --> 00:01:49.809\nTake a moment to think.\n\n26\n00:01:49.849 --> 00:01:51.989\nHere is the answer.\n\n27\n00:01:52.049 --> 00:01:54.629\nIk zal bellen.\n\n28\n00:01:54.889 --> 00:01:56.750\nI will call.\n\n29\n00:01:56.770 --> 00:02:00.150\nGreat job! Let's try another one.\n\n30\n00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:04.090\nHow would you say: They will arrive?\n\n31\n00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:07.530\nZij zullen aankomen.\n\n32\n00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:09.691\nThey will arrive.\n\n33\n00:02:09.731 --> 00:02:13.351\nNotice the sentence structure in Dutch.\n\n34\n00:02:13.431 --> 00:02:16.771\nZullen comes in second position.\n\n35\n00:02:16.791 --> 00:02:20.632\nThe main action verb goes to the end.\n\n36\n00:02:20.692 --> 00:02:23.632\nLet's practice this pattern together!\n\n37\n00:02:23.692 --> 00:02:26.972\nIk zal een boek lezen.\n\n38\n00:02:27.252 --> 00:02:30.032\nI will read a book.\n\n39\n00:02:30.132 --> 00:02:34.013\nJij zult de auto wassen.\n\n40\n00:02:34.093 --> 00:02:37.473\nYou will wash the car.\n\n41\n00:02:37.533 --> 00:02:41.513\nWij zullen een taart maken.\n\n42\n00:02:41.553 --> 00:02:44.954\nWe will make a cake.\n\n43\n00:02:44.994 --> 00:02:48.694\nNow let's visit our Error Clinic!\n\n44\n00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:53.614\nMistake number one: conjugating the end verb.\n\n45\n00:02:53.654 --> 00:02:56.834\nBeginners often say: Ik zal leest.\n\n46\n00:02:56.855 --> 00:03:02.615\nThat is wrong because leest is conjugated.\n\n47\n00:03:02.655 --> 00:03:06.595\nThe verb at the end must be infinitive!\n\n48\n00:03:06.635 --> 00:03:09.096\nThe correct sentence is:\n\n49\n00:03:09.156 --> 00:03:11.956\nIk zal lezen.\n\n50\n00:03:12.216 --> 00:03:14.776\nI will read.\n\n51\n00:03:14.796 --> 00:03:18.396\nMistake number two: word order.\n\n52\n00:03:18.436 --> 00:03:22.197\nDon't say: Ik zal helpen jou.\n\n53\n00:03:22.277 --> 00:03:25.957\nAlways put the second verb at the end!\n\n54\n00:03:26.037 --> 00:03:28.937\nIk zal jou helpen.\n\n55\n00:03:29.197 --> 00:03:30.957\nI will help you.\n\n56\n00:03:30.997 --> 00:03:34.298\nHere is your memory anchor:\n\n57\n00:03:34.398 --> 00:03:41.338\nZullen second, main verb at the end!\n\n58\n00:03:41.378 --> 00:03:44.758\nLet's finish with a quick summary.\n\n59\n00:03:44.818 --> 00:03:50.559\nVandaag leerden we de toekomst.\n\n60\n00:03:50.579 --> 00:03:54.639\nToday we learned the future.\n\n61\n00:03:54.659 --> 00:04:03.540\nUse zal or zullen plus infinitive. Excellent work!\n
grammar_future_zullen	en	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:08.041\nImagine promising a friend: I will help you tomorrow!\n\n2\n00:00:08.101 --> 00:00:12.841\nHow do you express the future in Dutch?\n\n3\n00:00:12.881 --> 00:00:17.761\nWe use the auxiliary verb zullen.\n\n4\n00:00:17.801 --> 00:00:22.982\nIt works just like the English word will.\n\n5\n00:00:23.042 --> 00:00:26.282\nLet's see how it works!\n\n6\n00:00:26.422 --> 00:00:30.702\nLet's start!\n\n7\n00:00:30.822 --> 00:00:33.543\nLet's start!\n\n8\n00:00:33.603 --> 00:00:38.123\nFirst, let's look at the forms.\n\n9\n00:00:38.183 --> 00:00:44.524\nFor I, we use ik zal.\n\n10\n00:00:44.624 --> 00:00:48.644\nI will help you.\n\n11\n00:00:48.824 --> 00:00:51.724\nI will help you.\n\n12\n00:00:51.804 --> 00:00:58.225\nFor you, we say jij zult.\n\n13\n00:00:58.305 --> 00:01:03.165\nYou will learn quickly.\n\n14\n00:01:03.245 --> 00:01:07.085\nYou will learn quickly.\n\n15\n00:01:07.125 --> 00:01:14.666\nFor he, she, or it, we use zal.\n\n16\n00:01:14.726 --> 00:01:19.566\nHe will come tomorrow.\n\n17\n00:01:19.626 --> 00:01:23.367\nHe will come tomorrow.\n\n18\n00:01:23.427 --> 00:01:27.087\nIt will rain tomorrow.\n\n19\n00:01:27.147 --> 00:01:29.647\nIt will rain tomorrow.\n\n20\n00:01:29.687 --> 00:01:34.068\nFor plural forms, we use zullen.\n\n21\n00:01:34.128 --> 00:01:37.948\nWe will eat together.\n\n22\n00:01:37.988 --> 00:01:40.408\nWe will eat together.\n\n23\n00:01:40.428 --> 00:01:44.028\nNow, let's try a quick prompt!\n\n24\n00:01:44.089 --> 00:01:47.549\nHow would you say: I will call?\n\n25\n00:01:47.569 --> 00:01:49.809\nTake a moment to think.\n\n26\n00:01:49.849 --> 00:01:51.989\nHere is the answer.\n\n27\n00:01:52.049 --> 00:01:54.629\nI will call.\n\n28\n00:01:54.889 --> 00:01:56.750\nI will call.\n\n29\n00:01:56.770 --> 00:02:00.150\nGreat job! Let's try another one.\n\n30\n00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:04.090\nHow would you say: They will arrive?\n\n31\n00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:07.530\nThey will arrive.\n\n32\n00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:09.691\nThey will arrive.\n\n33\n00:02:09.731 --> 00:02:13.351\nNotice the sentence structure in Dutch.\n\n34\n00:02:13.431 --> 00:02:16.771\nZullen comes in second position.\n\n35\n00:02:16.791 --> 00:02:20.632\nThe main action verb goes to the end.\n\n36\n00:02:20.692 --> 00:02:23.632\nLet's practice this pattern together!\n\n37\n00:02:23.692 --> 00:02:26.972\nI will read a book.\n\n38\n00:02:27.252 --> 00:02:30.032\nI will read a book.\n\n39\n00:02:30.132 --> 00:02:34.013\nYou will wash the car.\n\n40\n00:02:34.093 --> 00:02:37.473\nYou will wash the car.\n\n41\n00:02:37.533 --> 00:02:41.513\nWe will make a cake.\n\n42\n00:02:41.553 --> 00:02:44.954\nWe will make a cake.\n\n43\n00:02:44.994 --> 00:02:48.694\nNow let's visit our Error Clinic!\n\n44\n00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:53.614\nMistake number one: conjugating the end verb.\n\n45\n00:02:53.654 --> 00:02:56.834\nBeginners often say: Ik zal leest.\n\n46\n00:02:56.855 --> 00:03:02.615\nThat is wrong because leest is conjugated.\n\n47\n00:03:02.655 --> 00:03:06.595\nThe verb at the end must be infinitive!\n\n48\n00:03:06.635 --> 00:03:09.096\nThe correct sentence is:\n\n49\n00:03:09.156 --> 00:03:11.956\nI will read.\n\n50\n00:03:12.216 --> 00:03:14.776\nI will read.\n\n51\n00:03:14.796 --> 00:03:18.396\nMistake number two: word order.\n\n52\n00:03:18.436 --> 00:03:22.197\nDon't say: Ik zal helpen jou.\n\n53\n00:03:22.277 --> 00:03:25.957\nAlways put the second verb at the end!\n\n54\n00:03:26.037 --> 00:03:28.937\nI will help you.\n\n55\n00:03:29.197 --> 00:03:30.957\nI will help you.\n\n56\n00:03:30.997 --> 00:03:34.298\nHere is your memory anchor:\n\n57\n00:03:34.398 --> 00:03:41.338\nZullen second, main verb at the end!\n\n58\n00:03:41.378 --> 00:03:44.758\nLet's finish with a quick summary.\n\n59\n00:03:44.818 --> 00:03:50.559\nToday we learned the future.\n\n60\n00:03:50.579 --> 00:03:54.639\nToday we learned the future.\n\n61\n00:03:54.659 --> 00:04:03.540\nUse zal or zullen plus infinitive. Excellent work!\n
grammar_imperative	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:03.840\nImagine ordering coffee in Amsterdam!\n\n2\n00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.661\nOr asking someone to stop!\n\n3\n00:00:06.721 --> 00:00:09.941\nYou need the imperative form.\n\n4\n00:00:10.021 --> 00:00:14.942\nIn English, you say 'Listen!' or 'Stop!'.\n\n5\n00:00:14.982 --> 00:00:18.062\nDutch works almost the same way!\n\n6\n00:00:18.082 --> 00:00:20.922\nYou just use the verb stem.\n\n7\n00:00:20.962 --> 00:00:23.522\nNo subject pronoun is needed.\n\n8\n00:00:23.602 --> 00:00:25.623\nLaten we beginnen!\n\n9\n00:00:25.723 --> 00:00:27.103\nLet's begin!\n\n10\n00:00:27.223 --> 00:00:29.023\nLuister naar mij!\n\n11\n00:00:29.203 --> 00:00:30.683\nListen to me!\n\n12\n00:00:30.823 --> 00:00:34.323\nNotice there is no 'jij' or 'u'.\n\n13\n00:00:34.403 --> 00:00:37.224\nJust the stem word: luister.\n\n14\n00:00:37.384 --> 00:00:40.224\nLet's make simple command sentences.\n\n15\n00:00:40.264 --> 00:00:41.624\nKom hier!\n\n16\n00:00:41.684 --> 00:00:43.084\nCome here!\n\n17\n00:00:43.104 --> 00:00:45.865\nThe infinitive verb is 'komen'.\n\n18\n00:00:45.885 --> 00:00:48.125\nThe verb stem is 'kom'.\n\n19\n00:00:48.205 --> 00:00:49.665\nEet je soep!\n\n20\n00:00:49.745 --> 00:00:51.165\nEat your soup!\n\n21\n00:00:51.185 --> 00:00:54.045\nCan you guess the command for 'kijken'?\n\n22\n00:00:54.085 --> 00:00:57.186\nKijk naar buiten!\n\n23\n00:00:57.266 --> 00:01:00.106\nLook outside!\n\n24\n00:01:00.246 --> 00:01:01.926\nExcellent!\n\n25\n00:01:02.006 --> 00:01:05.087\nLet's practice with another verb.\n\n26\n00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:08.207\nHow do you tell someone to stop?\n\n27\n00:01:08.227 --> 00:01:11.487\nThe infinitive is 'stoppen'.\n\n28\n00:01:11.587 --> 00:01:14.868\nStop nu direct!\n\n29\n00:01:14.948 --> 00:01:17.748\nStop right now!\n\n30\n00:01:17.788 --> 00:01:19.628\nGreat job!\n\n31\n00:01:19.668 --> 00:01:23.028\nNow let's try polite commands.\n\n32\n00:01:23.088 --> 00:01:26.689\nSometimes you want to add 'alstublieft'.\n\n33\n00:01:26.729 --> 00:01:30.169\nKom binnen, alstublieft.\n\n34\n00:01:30.209 --> 00:01:32.269\nCome in, please.\n\n35\n00:01:32.349 --> 00:01:35.830\nGa zitten, alstublieft.\n\n36\n00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:38.170\nSit down, please.\n\n37\n00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:41.570\nPattern drill! Let's practice more.\n\n38\n00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:44.411\nLees dit boek!\n\n39\n00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:46.311\nRead this book!\n\n40\n00:01:46.391 --> 00:01:49.131\nSchrijf je naam!\n\n41\n00:01:49.211 --> 00:01:51.131\nWrite your name!\n\n42\n00:01:51.191 --> 00:01:53.532\nDrink je water!\n\n43\n00:01:53.572 --> 00:01:55.952\nDrink your water!\n\n44\n00:01:55.992 --> 00:02:00.052\nMaak de deur dicht!\n\n45\n00:02:00.092 --> 00:02:01.732\nClose the door!\n\n46\n00:02:01.792 --> 00:02:04.533\nHow would you say 'Open the door'?\n\n47\n00:02:04.553 --> 00:02:08.053\nThe verb is 'openmaken'.\n\n48\n00:02:08.093 --> 00:02:12.073\nMaak de deur open!\n\n49\n00:02:12.153 --> 00:02:13.634\nOpen the door!\n\n50\n00:02:13.674 --> 00:02:16.814\nNow, time for the error clinic!\n\n51\n00:02:16.854 --> 00:02:20.774\nMistake one: adding pronouns to commands.\n\n52\n00:02:20.794 --> 00:02:24.775\nBeginners say: Jij luister!\n\n53\n00:02:24.795 --> 00:02:26.575\nThat is incorrect.\n\n54\n00:02:26.635 --> 00:02:28.995\nLuister goed!\n\n55\n00:02:29.135 --> 00:02:30.695\nListen carefully!\n\n56\n00:02:30.735 --> 00:02:32.635\nDrop the pronoun!\n\n57\n00:02:32.655 --> 00:02:36.456\nMistake two: using full infinitives.\n\n58\n00:02:36.496 --> 00:02:40.036\nBeginners say: Komen hier!\n\n59\n00:02:40.056 --> 00:02:41.616\nThat is wrong too.\n\n60\n00:02:41.776 --> 00:02:44.297\nUse only the verb stem!\n\n61\n00:02:44.337 --> 00:02:47.397\nKom snel hier!\n\n62\n00:02:47.437 --> 00:02:49.097\nCome here quickly!\n\n63\n00:02:49.157 --> 00:02:51.417\nHere is your memory tip!\n\n64\n00:02:51.457 --> 00:02:56.038\nCommand equals stem without pronoun.\n\n65\n00:02:56.158 --> 00:02:58.718\nLet's do a quick spoken recap.\n\n66\n00:02:58.738 --> 00:03:02.258\nToday we learned the imperative form.\n\n67\n00:03:02.318 --> 00:03:06.539\nVandaag leerden we de gebiedende wijs.\n\n68\n00:03:06.579 --> 00:03:09.059\nToday we learned the imperative.\n\n69\n00:03:09.119 --> 00:03:12.319\nGebruik gewoon de werkwoordsstam!\n\n70\n00:03:12.359 --> 00:03:14.980\nJust use the verb stem!\n\n71\n00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:16.880\nWell done and see you next time!\n
