oken recap.\n\n66\n00:02:59.738 --> 00:03:03.258\nToday we learned the imperative form.\n\n67\n00:03:03.318 --> 00:03:07.539\nToday we learned the imperative.\n\n68\n00:03:07.579 --> 00:03:10.059\nToday we learned the imperative.\n\n69\n00:03:10.119 --> 00:03:13.319\nJust use the verb stem!\n\n70\n00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:15.980\nJust use the verb stem!\n\n71\n00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:17.880\nWell done and see you next time!\n
grammar_imperfect_irregular	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:05.340\nImagine telling a friend about yesterday.\n\n2\n00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:08.820\nYou need the simple past tense.\n\n3\n00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:13.160\nToday we learn irregular past verbs.\n\n4\n00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:17.480\nIn English: is becomes was.\n\n5\n00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:20.801\nIn Dutch, it is very similar!\n\n6\n00:00:20.861 --> 00:00:22.961\nLaten we beginnen!\n\n7\n00:00:23.041 --> 00:00:25.161\nLet's get started!\n\n8\n00:00:25.281 --> 00:00:28.121\nLet's look at the verb ZIJN.\n\n9\n00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:32.361\nIn the past, ZIJN becomes WAS.\n\n10\n00:00:32.421 --> 00:00:35.521\nIk was gisteren thuis.\n\n11\n00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:37.721\nI was home yesterday.\n\n12\n00:00:37.741 --> 00:00:41.461\nSimple, right? Just like English!\n\n13\n00:00:41.501 --> 00:00:44.901\nNow look at HEBBEN, to have.\n\n14\n00:00:44.941 --> 00:00:49.021\nIn the past, HEBBEN becomes HAD.\n\n15\n00:00:49.121 --> 00:00:51.662\nZij had een goede dag.\n\n16\n00:00:51.722 --> 00:00:54.502\nShe had a good day.\n\n17\n00:00:54.542 --> 00:00:58.482\nNext is GAAN, which means to go.\n\n18\n00:00:58.622 --> 00:01:02.522\nGAAN becomes GING in the past.\n\n19\n00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:05.122\nHij ging naar de winkel.\n\n20\n00:01:05.162 --> 00:01:07.782\nHe went to the shop.\n\n21\n00:01:07.842 --> 00:01:11.962\nNotice how the vowel changes completely!\n\n22\n00:01:12.002 --> 00:01:16.022\nNext is ZIEN, to see.\n\n23\n00:01:16.102 --> 00:01:20.522\nZIEN becomes ZAG in past tense.\n\n24\n00:01:20.602 --> 00:01:24.523\nIk zag een mooie vogel.\n\n25\n00:01:24.743 --> 00:01:27.863\nI saw a beautiful bird.\n\n26\n00:01:27.883 --> 00:01:30.023\nTime for a quick check!\n\n27\n00:01:30.083 --> 00:01:33.983\nHow do you say: I was home?\n\n28\n00:01:34.003 --> 00:01:36.703\nCan you guess the Dutch sentence?\n\n29\n00:01:36.723 --> 00:01:38.363\nThe answer is:\n\n30\n00:01:38.423 --> 00:01:41.763\nIk was gisteren thuis.\n\n31\n00:01:41.983 --> 00:01:44.363\nI was home yesterday.\n\n32\n00:01:44.383 --> 00:01:47.343\nGreat job! Let's continue.\n\n33\n00:01:47.383 --> 00:01:51.563\nNow look at DOEN, to do.\n\n34\n00:01:51.643 --> 00:01:55.523\nDOEN becomes DEED in the past.\n\n35\n00:01:55.563 --> 00:01:59.004\nWij deden ons werk.\n\n36\n00:01:59.044 --> 00:02:01.584\nWe did our work.\n\n37\n00:02:01.644 --> 00:02:05.324\nNote: plural forms take -en!\n\n38\n00:02:05.344 --> 00:02:09.724\nSo DEED becomes DEDEN for plural.\n\n39\n00:02:09.804 --> 00:02:13.064\nLet's look at KUNNEN, can.\n\n40\n00:02:13.104 --> 00:02:18.304\nKUNNEN becomes KON in past tense.\n\n41\n00:02:18.364 --> 00:02:24.684\nIk kon niet komen.\n\n42\n00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:26.904\nI could not come.\n\n43\n00:02:26.944 --> 00:02:33.305\nFor plural, KON becomes KONNEN.\n\n44\n00:02:33.385 --> 00:02:40.585\nWij konnen het zien.\n\n45\n00:02:41.525 --> 00:02:44.205\nWe could see it.\n\n46\n00:02:44.245 --> 00:02:49.265\nNow look at WETEN, to know.\n\n47\n00:02:49.305 --> 00:02:55.425\nWETEN becomes WIST in the past.\n\n48\n00:02:55.465 --> 00:03:02.665\nHij wist het antwoord.\n\n49\n00:03:03.305 --> 00:03:06.126\nHe knew the answer.\n\n50\n00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:09.406\nLet's try another quick prompt!\n\n51\n00:03:09.446 --> 00:03:12.946\nHow would you say: He went?\n\n52\n00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:16.266\nRemember the verb GAAN!\n\n53\n00:03:16.306 --> 00:03:18.466\nThe answer is:\n\n54\n00:03:18.526 --> 00:03:25.326\nHij ging naar huis.\n\n55\n00:03:25.366 --> 00:03:27.886\nHe went home.\n\n56\n00:03:27.926 --> 00:03:32.166\nNow, let's practice the pattern together!\n\n57\n00:03:32.226 --> 00:03:36.326\nIk was daar.\n\n58\n00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:39.187\nI was there.\n\n59\n00:03:39.247 --> 00:03:43.467\nIk had tijd.\n\n60\n00:03:43.707 --> 00:03:45.587\nI had time.\n\n61\n00:03:45.667 --> 00:03:47.967\nIk ging weg.\n\n62\n00:03:48.107 --> 00:03:50.347\nI went away.\n\n63\n00:03:50.427 --> 00:03:52.787\nIk zag jou.\n\n64\n00:03:52.907 --> 00:03:55.287\nI saw you.\n\n65\n00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:57.547\nIk deed het.\n\n66\n00:03:57.687 --> 00:03:59.827\nI did it.\n\n67\n00:03:59.867 --> 00:04:04.047\nNow, let's look at common errors!\n\n68\n00:04:04.107 --> 00:04:10.408\nError 1: adding regular endings to irregulars.\n\n69\n00:04:10.448 --> 00:04:12.608\nBeginners often say:\n\n70\n00:04:12.688 --> 00:04:15.768\nHij gaande naar school.\n\n71\n00:04:15.808 --> 00:04:19.788\nWrong: He went to school.\n\n72\n00:04:19.808 --> 00:04:25.068\nThat is incorrect! Do not add -de.\n\n73\n00:04:25.188 --> 00:04:29.848\nGAAN changes completely to GING.\n\n74\n00:04:29.888 --> 00:04:31.888\nCorrect sentence:\n\n75\n00:04:31.928 --> 00:04:34.828\nHij ging naar school.\n\n76\n00:04:34.868 --> 00:04:37.648\nHe went to school.\n\n77\n00:04:37.728 --> 00:04:42.188\nError 2: forgetting plural forms.\n\n78\n00:04:42.208 --> 00:04:46.249\nFor plural subjects, add -en.\n\n79\n00:04:46.289 --> 00:04:51.389\nDon't say: wij was. Say: wij waren.\n\n80\n00:04:51.429 --> 00:04:54.469\nWij waren erg blij.\n\n81\n00:04:54.509 --> 00:04:58.249\nWe were very happy.\n\n82\n00:04:58.289 --> 00:05:00.069\nMemory anchor:\n\n83\n00:05:00.129 --> 00:05:05.829\nIrregular past verbs usually change their vowel!\n\n84\n00:05:05.869 --> 00:05:09.269\nVandaag leerden we:\n\n85\n00:05:09.329 --> 00:05:17.710\nIk was, ik had, ik ging.\n\n86\n00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:25.850\nI was, I had, I went.\n\n87\n00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:30.970\nKeep practicing these core irregular verbs!\n\n88\n00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:32.470\nSee you in the next lesson!\n
