grammar_imperfect_regular	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:05.320\nImagine talking about yesterday with a friend.\n\n2\n00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:09.260\nYou need the Dutch simple past tense!\n\n3\n00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:12.820\nIn English, you usually add E-D.\n\n4\n00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:18.001\nIn Dutch, we add T-E or D-E.\n\n5\n00:00:18.061 --> 00:00:20.681\nLet's look at an easy example.\n\n6\n00:00:20.741 --> 00:00:23.581\nIk werk vandaag.\n\n7\n00:00:23.741 --> 00:00:25.121\nI work today.\n\n8\n00:00:25.201 --> 00:00:28.361\nIk werkte gisteren.\n\n9\n00:00:28.521 --> 00:00:30.781\nI worked yesterday.\n\n10\n00:00:30.861 --> 00:00:32.401\nLaten we beginnen!\n\n11\n00:00:32.501 --> 00:00:33.861\nLet's begin!\n\n12\n00:00:33.921 --> 00:00:38.381\nHow do we choose T-E or D-E?\n\n13\n00:00:38.421 --> 00:00:42.321\nWe use the rule of 't Kofschip!\n\n14\n00:00:42.381 --> 00:00:44.901\nLook at the stem of the verb.\n\n15\n00:00:44.961 --> 00:00:48.902\nIs the last letter in 't Kofschip?\n\n16\n00:00:48.922 --> 00:00:58.882\nThe letters are T, K, F, S, C, H, P.\n\n17\n00:00:58.962 --> 00:01:02.082\nIf yes, add T-E!\n\n18\n00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:04.982\nOtherwise, add D-E!\n\n19\n00:01:05.042 --> 00:01:07.902\nLet's test the verb 'werken'.\n\n20\n00:01:07.942 --> 00:01:10.602\nThe stem is 'werk'.\n\n21\n00:01:10.662 --> 00:01:14.082\nIt ends with K.\n\n22\n00:01:14.122 --> 00:01:17.002\nK is in 't Kofschip!\n\n23\n00:01:17.062 --> 00:01:21.343\nSo we add T-E: werkte.\n\n24\n00:01:21.403 --> 00:01:24.003\nHij werkte heel hard.\n\n25\n00:01:24.043 --> 00:01:26.323\nHe worked very hard.\n\n26\n00:01:26.363 --> 00:01:29.603\nFor plural subjects, add T-E-N.\n\n27\n00:01:31.103 --> 00:01:34.083\nWij werkten gisteren samen.\n\n28\n00:01:34.123 --> 00:01:36.923\nWe worked together yesterday.\n\n29\n00:01:36.983 --> 00:01:40.423\nNow, let's try 'maken'.\n\n30\n00:01:40.463 --> 00:01:43.123\nThe stem is 'maak'.\n\n31\n00:01:43.163 --> 00:01:46.783\nDoes K belong in 't Kofschip?\n\n32\n00:01:46.843 --> 00:01:49.044\nYes! So add T-E.\n\n33\n00:01:50.404 --> 00:01:52.824\nZij maakte een taart.\n\n34\n00:01:52.884 --> 00:01:54.864\nShe made a cake.\n\n35\n00:01:54.904 --> 00:01:57.184\nCan you guess the plural form?\n\n36\n00:01:57.224 --> 00:01:59.964\nZij maakten een taart.\n\n37\n00:02:00.004 --> 00:02:02.184\nThey made a cake.\n\n38\n00:02:02.204 --> 00:02:06.064\nNow let's look at D-E verbs.\n\n39\n00:02:06.104 --> 00:02:08.804\nTake the verb 'wonen'.\n\n40\n00:02:08.844 --> 00:02:11.544\nThe stem is 'woon'.\n\n41\n00:02:11.584 --> 00:02:14.604\nDoes N belong in 't Kofschip?\n\n42\n00:02:14.644 --> 00:02:19.665\nNo! N is not in 't Kofschip.\n\n43\n00:02:19.705 --> 00:02:23.465\nSo we add D-E!\n\n44\n00:02:23.525 --> 00:02:27.685\nIk woonde in Amsterdam.\n\n45\n00:02:27.805 --> 00:02:30.965\nI lived in Amsterdam.\n\n46\n00:02:31.005 --> 00:02:35.545\nHow would you say 'We lived in Utrecht'?\n\n47\n00:02:35.605 --> 00:02:38.865\nThink about the plural ending!\n\n48\n00:02:38.905 --> 00:02:42.925\nWij woonden in Utrecht.\n\n49\n00:02:42.965 --> 00:02:45.865\nWe lived in Utrecht.\n\n50\n00:02:45.905 --> 00:02:49.646\nLet's practice with 'spelen'.\n\n51\n00:02:49.666 --> 00:02:53.046\nThe stem is 'speel'.\n\n52\n00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:56.986\nL is not in 't Kofschip.\n\n53\n00:02:57.006 --> 00:03:00.766\nSo we add D-E!\n\n54\n00:03:00.806 --> 00:03:05.066\nHet kind speelde buiten.\n\n55\n00:03:05.086 --> 00:03:08.446\nThe child played outside.\n\n56\n00:03:08.466 --> 00:03:12.946\nDe kinderen speelden buiten.\n\n57\n00:03:12.966 --> 00:03:16.626\nThe children played outside.\n\n58\n00:03:16.646 --> 00:03:20.107\nNow time for our Error Clinic!\n\n59\n00:03:20.127 --> 00:03:24.067\nHere is a common beginner mistake:\n\n60\n00:03:24.127 --> 00:03:26.887\nHij woonte in Rotterdam.\n\n61\n00:03:26.927 --> 00:03:30.027\nHe lived in Rotterdam.\n\n62\n00:03:30.087 --> 00:03:34.007\nWhy is 'woonte' wrong?\n\n63\n00:03:34.027 --> 00:03:38.587\nBecause 'woon' ends in N!\n\n64\n00:03:38.827 --> 00:03:42.047\nN is not in 't Kofschip.\n\n65\n00:03:42.067 --> 00:03:44.607\nThe correct version is:\n\n66\n00:03:44.687 --> 00:03:48.767\nHij woonde in Rotterdam.\n\n67\n00:03:48.807 --> 00:03:52.168\nHe lived in Rotterdam.\n\n68\n00:03:52.208 --> 00:03:55.808\nHere is another common mistake:\n\n69\n00:03:55.848 --> 00:04:00.248\nWij werkte gisteren samen.\n\n70\n00:04:00.268 --> 00:04:03.728\nWe worked together yesterday.\n\n71\n00:04:03.768 --> 00:04:07.768\nWhy is 'werkte' wrong here?\n\n72\n00:04:07.788 --> 00:04:11.708\nBecause 'wij' is plural!\n\n73\n00:04:11.728 --> 00:04:16.548\nPlural always needs -TEN or -DEN.\n\n74\n00:04:16.568 --> 00:04:19.088\nThe correct version is:\n\n75\n00:04:19.128 --> 00:04:23.809\nWij werkten gisteren samen.\n\n76\n00:04:23.829 --> 00:04:27.489\nWe worked together yesterday.\n\n77\n00:04:27.509 --> 00:04:29.729\nMemory anchor time!\n\n78\n00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:33.189\nCheck the stem in 't Kofschip!\n\n79\n00:04:33.229 --> 00:04:39.069\nT-E for Kofschip, D-E for rest!\n\n80\n00:04:39.209 --> 00:04:42.449\nAdd -N for plural!\n\n81\n00:04:42.489 --> 00:04:46.009\nLet's recap what we learned today.\n\n82\n00:04:46.049 --> 00:04:49.929\nVandaag leerden we de verleden tijd.\n\n83\n00:04:49.969 --> 00:04:54.030\nToday we learned the past tense.\n\n84\n00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:59.590\nIk werkte en ik woonde.\n\n85\n00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:03.990\nI worked and I lived.\n\n86\n00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:06.690\nGreat job today! See you next time!\n
grammar_imperfect_regular	en	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:05.320\nImagine talking about yesterday with a friend.\n\n2\n00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:09.260\nYou need the Dutch simple past tense!\n\n3\n00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:12.820\nIn English, you usually add E-D.\n\n4\n00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:18.001\nIn Dutch, we add T-E or D-E.\n\n5\n00:00:18.061 --> 00:00:20.681\nLet's look at an easy example.\n\n6\n00:00:20.741 --> 00:00:23.581\nI work today.\n\n7\n00:00:23.741 --> 00:00:25.121\nI work today.\n\n8\n00:00:25.201 --> 00:00:28.361\nI worked yesterday.\n\n9\n00:00:28.521 --> 00:00:30.781\nI worked yesterday.\n\n10\n00:00:30.861 --> 00:00:32.401\nLet's begin!\n\n11\n00:00:32.501 --> 00:00:33.861\nLet's begin!\n\n12\n00:00:33.921 --> 00:00:38.381\nHow do we choose T-E or D-E?\n\n13\n00:00:38.421 --> 00:00:42.321\nWe use the rule of 't Kofschip!\n\n14\n00:00:42.381 --> 00:00:44.901\nLook at the stem of the verb.\n\n15\n00:00:44.961 --> 00:00:48.902\nIs the last letter in 't Kofschip?\n\n16\n00:00:48.922 --> 00:00:58.882\nThe letters are T, K, F, S, C, H, P.\n\n17\n00:00:58.962 --> 00:01:02.082\nIf yes, add T-E!\n\n18\n00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:04.982\nOtherwise, add D-E!\n\n19\n00:01:05.042 --> 00:01:07.902\nLet's test the verb 'werken'.\n\n20\n00:01:07.942 --> 00:01:10.602\nThe stem is 'werk'.\n\n21\n00:01:10.662 --> 00:01:14.082\nIt ends with K.\n\n22\n00:01:14.122 --> 00:01:17.002\nK is in 't Kofschip!\n\n23\n00:01:17.062 --> 00:01:21.343\nSo we add T-E: werkte.\n\n24\n00:01:21.403 --> 00:01:24.003\nHe worked very hard.\n\n25\n00:01:24.043 --> 00:01:26.323\nHe worked very hard.\n\n26\n00:01:26.363 --> 00:01:29.603\nFor plural subjects, add T-E-N.\n\n27\n00:01:31.103 --> 00:01:34.083\nWe worked together yesterday.\n\n28\n00:01:34.123 --> 00:01:36.923\nWe worked together yesterday.\n\n29\n00:01:36.983 --> 00:01:40.423\nNow, let's try 'maken'.\n\n30\n00:01:40.463 --> 00:01:43.123\nThe stem is 'maak'.\n\n31\n00:01:43.163 --> 00:01:46.783\nDoes K belong in 't Kofschip?\n\n32\n00:01:46.843 --> 00:01:49.044\nYes! So add T-E.\n\n33\n00:01:50.404 --> 00:01:52.824\nShe made a cake.\n\n34\n00:01:52.884 --> 00:01:54.864\nShe made a cake.\n\n35\n00:01:54.904 --> 00:01:57.184\nCan you guess the plural form?\n\n36\n00:01:57.224 --> 00:01:59.964\nThey made a cake.\n\n37\n00:02:00.004 --> 00:02:02.184\nThey made a cake.\n\n38\n00:02:02.204 --> 00:02:06.064\nNow let's look at D-E verbs.\n\n39\n00:02:06.104 --> 00:02:08.804\nTake the verb 'wonen'.\n\n40\n00:02:08.844 --> 00:02:11.544\nThe stem is 'woon'.\n\n41\n00:02:11.584 --> 00:02:14.604\nDoes N belong in 't Kofschip?\n\n42\n00:02:14.644 --> 00:02:19.665\nNo! N is not in 't Kofschip.\n\n43\n00:02:19.705 --> 00:02:23.465\nSo we add D-E!\n\n44\n00:02:23.525 --> 00:02:27.685\nI lived in Amsterdam.\n\n45\n00:02:27.805 --> 00:02:30.965\nI lived in Amsterdam.\n\n46\n00:02:31.005 --> 00:02:35.545\nHow would you say 'We lived in Utrecht'?\n\n47\n00:02:35.605 --> 00:02:38.865\nThink about the plural ending!\n\n48\n00:02:38.905 --> 00:02:42.925\nWe lived in Utrecht.\n\n49\n00:02:42.965 --> 00:02:45.865\nWe lived in Utrecht.\n\n50\n00:02:45.905 --> 00:02:49.646\nLet's practice with 'spelen'.\n\n51\n00:02:49.666 --> 00:02:53.046\nThe stem is 'speel'.\n\n52\n00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:56.986\nL is not in 't Kofschip.\n\n53\n00:02:57.006 --> 00:03:00.766\nSo we add D-E!\n\n54\n00:03:00.806 --> 00:03:05.066\nThe child played outside.\n\n55\n00:03:05.086 --> 00:03:08.446\nThe child played outside.\n\n56\n00:03:08.466 --> 00:03:12.946\nThe children played outside.\n\n57\n00:03:12.966 --> 00:03:16.626\nThe children played outside.\n\n58\n00:03:16.646 --> 00:03:20.107\nNow time for our Error Clinic!\n\n59\n00:03:20.127 --> 00:03:24.067\nHere is a common beginner mistake:\n\n60\n00:03:24.127 --> 00:03:26.887\nHe lived in Rotterdam.\n\n61\n00:03:26.927 --> 00:03:30.027\nHe lived in Rotterdam.\n\n62\n00:03:30.087 --> 00:03:34.007\nWhy is 'woonte' wrong?\n\n63\n00:03:34.027 --> 00:03:38.587\nBecause 'woon' ends in N!\n\n64\n00:03:38.827 --> 00:03:42.047\nN is not in 't Kofschip.\n\n65\n00:03:42.067 --> 00:03:44.607\nThe correct version is:\n\n66\n00:03:44.687 --> 00:03:48.767\nHe lived in Rotterdam.\n\n67\n00:03:48.807 --> 00:03:52.168\nHe lived in Rotterdam.\n\n68\n00:03:52.208 --> 00:03:55.808\nHere is another common mistake:\n\n69\n00:03:55.848 --> 00:04:00.248\nWe worked together yesterday.\n\n70\n00:04:00.268 --> 00:04:03.728\nWe worked together yesterday.\n\n71\n00:04:03.768 --> 00:04:07.768\nWhy is 'werkte' wrong here?\n\n72\n00:04:07.788 --> 00:04:11.708\nBecause 'wij' is plural!\n\n73\n00:04:11.728 --> 00:04:16.548\nPlural always needs -TEN or -DEN.\n\n74\n00:04:16.568 --> 00:04:19.088\nThe correct version is:\n\n75\n00:04:19.128 --> 00:04:23.809\nWe worked together yesterday.\n\n76\n00:04:23.829 --> 00:04:27.489\nWe worked together yesterday.\n\n77\n00:04:27.509 --> 00:04:29.729\nMemory anchor time!\n\n78\n00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:33.189\nCheck the stem in 't Kofschip!\n\n79\n00:04:33.229 --> 00:04:39.069\nT-E for Kofschip, D-E for rest!\n\n80\n00:04:39.209 --> 00:04:42.449\nAdd -N for plural!\n\n81\n00:04:42.489 --> 00:04:46.009\nLet's recap what we learned today.\n\n82\n00:04:46.049 --> 00:04:49.929\nToday we learned the past tense.\n\n83\n00:04:49.969 --> 00:04:54.030\nToday we learned the past tense.\n\n84\n00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:59.590\nI worked and I lived.\n\n85\n00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:03.990\nI worked and I lived.\n\n86\n00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:06.690\nGreat job today! See you next time!\n
grammar_imperfect_vs_perfect	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:05.040\nImagine talking about yesterday.\n\n2\n00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:08.841\nDid you work or have you worked?\n\n3\n00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:13.041\nIn Dutch, we have two past tenses.\n\n4\n00:00:13.061 --> 00:00:18.442\nThe perfect tense is called VTT.\n\n5\n00:00:18.502 --> 00:00:23.142\nVTT is very common in spoken Dutch.\n\n6\n00:00:23.162 --> 00:00:28.583\nThe simple past is called OVT.\n\n7\n00:00:28.663 --> 00:00:32.943\nOVT is mostly used for stories.\n\n8\n00:00:33.023 --> 00:00:35.363\nLaten we beginnen!\n\n9\n00:00:35.483 --> 00:00:37.664\nLet's begin!\n\n10\n00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:42.044\nFirst, let's look at VTT.\n\n11\n00:00:42.104 --> 00:00:46.144\nIk heb gisteren gewerkt.\n\n12\n00:00:46.244 --> 00:00:49.305\nI have worked yesterday.\n\n13\n00:00:49.325 --> 00:00:54.645\nNotice the structure: heb plus gewerkt.\n\n14\n00:00:54.685 --> 00:00:58.326\nNow, let's look at OVT.\n\n15\n00:00:58.386 --> 00:01:01.466\nIk werkte gisteren.\n\n16\n00:01:01.586 --> 00:01:04.306\nI worked yesterday.\n\n17\n00:01:04.346 --> 00:01:07.887\nBoth sentences talk about the past.\n\n18\n00:01:07.947 --> 00:01:12.587\nIn daily speech, use VTT more!\n\n19\n00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:16.707\nLet's practice some more VTT sentences.\n\n20\n00:01:16.767 --> 00:01:19.988\nHij heeft een appel gegeten.\n\n21\n00:01:20.048 --> 00:01:23.448\nHe has eaten an apple.\n\n22\n00:01:23.488 --> 00:01:29.589\nWij hebben de auto gewassen.\n\n23\n00:01:29.629 --> 00:01:32.129\nWe have washed the car.\n\n24\n00:01:32.169 --> 00:01:34.429\nCan you guess how to say:\n\n25\n00:01:34.449 --> 00:01:37.429\n'I have called my mother'?\n\n26\n00:01:37.469 --> 00:01:39.930\nHere is the answer:\n\n27\n00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:45.650\nIk heb mijn moeder gebeld.\n\n28\n00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:48.391\nI have called my mother.\n\n29\n00:01:48.411 --> 00:01:50.391\nGreat job!\n\n30\n00:01:50.431 --> 00:01:54.171\nNow let's look at OVT examples.\n\n31\n00:01:54.351 --> 00:01:58.752\nUse OVT for conditions and states.\n\n32\n00:01:58.832 --> 00:02:02.972\nHet weer was heel mooi.\n\n33\n00:02:02.992 --> 00:02:06.272\nThe weather was very nice.\n\n34\n00:02:06.332 --> 00:02:10.313\nZij woonden in een stad.\n\n35\n00:02:10.333 --> 00:02:13.513\nThey lived in a city.\n\n36\n00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:16.473\nTime for our Error Clinic!\n\n37\n00:02:16.513 --> 00:02:21.614\nMistake one: mixing OVT and VTT.\n\n38\n00:02:21.654 --> 00:02:24.254\nNever say this wrong sentence:\n\n39\n00:02:24.314 --> 00:02:27.554\nIk heb gisteren werkte.\n\n40\n00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:31.615\nI have worked yesterday (wrong).\n\n41\n00:02:31.635 --> 00:02:36.235\nDo not combine heb with OVT!\n\n42\n00:02:36.295 --> 00:02:38.796\nSay this correct version:\n\n43\n00:02:38.856 --> 00:02:41.916\nIk heb gisteren gewerkt.\n\n44\n00:02:42.076 --> 00:02:45.596\nI have worked yesterday.\n\n45\n00:02:45.616 --> 00:02:50.137\nMistake two: wrong auxiliary verb.\n\n46\n00:02:50.177 --> 00:02:52.057\nDon't say this:\n\n47\n00:02:52.117 --> 00:02:55.037\nIk heb naar huis gegaan.\n\n48\n00:02:55.197 --> 00:02:58.817\nI have gone home (wrong).\n\n49\n00:02:58.857 --> 00:03:02.598\nVerbs of movement use zijn!\n\n50\n00:03:02.658 --> 00:03:05.158\nSay this correct version:\n\n51\n00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:08.078\nIk ben naar huis gegaan.\n\n52\n00:03:08.258 --> 00:03:10.839\nI went home.\n\n53\n00:03:10.879 --> 00:03:13.799\nHere is your quick memory tip!\n\n54\n00:03:13.819 --> 00:03:18.579\nWhen speaking Dutch, default to VTT!\n\n55\n00:03:18.639 --> 00:03:22.200\nVandaag leerden we het verleden.\n\n56\n00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:24.520\nToday we learned the past.\n
grammar_imperfect_vs_perfect	en	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:05.040\nImagine talking about yesterday.\n\n2\n00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:08.841\nDid you work or have you worked?\n\n3\n00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:13.041\nIn Dutch, we have two past tenses.\n\n4\n00:00:13.061 --> 00:00:18.442\nThe perfect tense is called VTT.\n\n5\n00:00:18.502 --> 00:00:23.142\nVTT is very common in spoken Dutch.\n\n6\n00:00:23.162 --> 00:00:28.583\nThe simple past is called OVT.\n\n7\n00:00:28.663 --> 00:00:32.943\nOVT is mostly used for stories.\n\n8\n00:00:33.023 --> 00:00:35.363\nLet's begin!\n\n9\n00:00:35.483 --> 00:00:37.664\nLet's begin!\n\n10\n00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:42.044\nFirst, let's look at VTT.\n\n11\n00:00:42.104 --> 00:00:46.144\nI have worked yesterday.\n\n12\n00:00:46.244 --> 00:00:49.305\nI have worked yesterday.\n\n13\n00:00:49.325 --> 00:00:54.645\nNotice the structure: heb plus gewerkt.\n\n14\n00:00:54.685 --> 00:00:58.326\nNow, let's look at OVT.\n\n15\n00:00:58.386 --> 00:01:01.466\nI worked yesterday.\n\n16\n00:01:01.586 --> 00:01:04.306\nI worked yesterday.\n\n17\n00:01:04.346 --> 00:01:07.887\nBoth sentences talk about the past.\n\n18\n00:01:07.947 --> 00:01:12.587\nIn daily speech, use VTT more!\n\n19\n00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:16.707\nLet's practice some more VTT sentences.\n\n20\n00:01:16.767 --> 00:01:19.988\nHe has eaten an apple.\n\n21\n00:01:20.048 --> 00:01:23.448\nHe has eaten an apple.\n\n22\n00:01:23.488 --> 00:01:29.589\nWe have washed the car.\n\n23\n00:01:29.629 --> 00:01:32.129\nWe have washed the car.\n\n24\n00:01:32.169 --> 00:01:34.429\nCan you guess how to say:\n\n25\n00:01:34.449 --> 00:01:37.429\n'I have called my mother'?\n\n26\n00:01:37.469 --> 00:01:39.930\nHere is the answer:\n\n27\n00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:45.650\nI have called my mother.\n\n28\n00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:48.391\nI have called my mother.\n\n29\n00:01:48.411 --> 00:01:50.391\nGreat job!\n\n30\n00:01:50.431 --> 00:01:54.171\nNow let's look at OVT examples.\n\n31\n00:01:54.351 --> 00:01:58.752\nUse OVT for conditions and states.\n\n32\n00:01:58.832 --> 00:02:02.972\nThe weather was very nice.\n\n33\n00:02:02.992 --> 00:02:06.272\nThe weather was very nice.\n\n34\n00:02:06.332 --> 00:02:10.313\nThey lived in a city.\n\n35\n00:02:10.333 --> 00:02:13.513\nThey lived in a city.\n\n36\n00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:16.473\nTime for our Error Clinic!\n\n37\n00:02:16.513 --> 00:02:21.614\nMistake one: mixing OVT and VTT.\n\n38\n00:02:21.654 --> 00:02:24.254\nNever say this wrong sentence:\n\n39\n00:02:24.314 --> 00:02:27.554\nI have worked yesterday (wrong).\n\n40\n00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:31.615\nI have worked yesterday (wrong).\n\n41\n00:02:31.635 --> 00:02:36.235\nDo not combine heb with OVT!\n\n42\n00:02:36.295 --> 00:02:38.796\nSay this correct version:\n\n43\n00:02:38.856 --> 00:02:41.916\nI have worked yesterday.\n\n44\n00:02:42.076 --> 00:02:45.596\nI have worked yesterday.\n\n45\n00:02:45.616 --> 00:02:50.137\nMistake two: wrong auxiliary verb.\n\n46\n00:02:50.177 --> 00:02:52.057\nDon't say this:\n\n47\n00:02:52.117 --> 00:02:55.037\nI have gone home (wrong).\n\n48\n00:02:55.197 --> 00:02:58.817\nI have gone home (wrong).\n\n49\n00:02:58.857 --> 00:03:02.598\nVerbs of movement use zijn!\n\n50\n00:03:02.658 --> 00:03:05.158\nSay this correct version:\n\n51\n00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:08.078\nI went home.\n\n52\n00:03:08.258 --> 00:03:10.839\nI went home.\n\n53\n00:03:10.879 --> 00:03:13.799\nHere is your quick memory tip!\n\n54\n00:03:13.819 --> 00:03:18.579\nWhen speaking Dutch, default to VTT!\n\n55\n00:03:18.639 --> 00:03:22.200\nToday we learned the past.\n\n56\n00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:24.520\nToday we learned the past.\n
grammar_object_pronouns	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:05.720\nImagine someone gives you a present!\n\n2\n00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:10.381\nYou say: He gives me a gift.\n\n3\n00:00:10.441 --> 00:00:14.901\nIn Dutch, me is mij.\n\n4\n00:00:14.941 --> 00:00:19.161\nToday we learn Dutch object pronouns!\n\n5\n00:00:19.201 --> 00:00:22.881\nWe beginnen nu!\n\n6\n00:00:22.921 --> 00:00:25.042\nWe start now!\n\n7\n00:00:25.102 --> 00:00:29.062\nObject pronouns receive the action.\n\n8\n00:00:29.142 --> 00:00:33.062\nIn English, we say: Look at me!\n\n9\n00:00:33.122 --> 00:00:36.022\nIn Dutch, we say the same!\n\n10\n00:00:36.062 --> 00:00:40.082\nKijk naar mij!\n\n11\n00:00:40.222 --> 00:00:41.983\nLook at me!\n\n12\n00:00:42.043 --> 00:00:45.503\nMij means me.\n\n13\n00:00:45.543 --> 00:00:48.503\nYou can also use me.\n\n14\n00:00:48.543 --> 00:00:52.123\nHij ziet me.\n\n15\n00:00:52.143 --> 00:00:54.083\nHe sees me.\n\n16\n00:00:54.163 --> 00:00:57.804\nJou means you.\n\n17\n00:00:57.884 --> 00:01:01.784\nIk zie jou.\n\n18\n00:01:01.884 --> 00:01:03.524\nI see you.\n\n19\n00:01:03.584 --> 00:01:07.344\nHem means him.\n\n20\n00:01:07.404 --> 00:01:11.804\nWij bellen hem.\n\n21\n00:01:11.824 --> 00:01:13.365\nWe call him.\n\n22\n00:01:13.405 --> 00:01:17.145\nHaar means her.\n\n23\n00:01:17.205 --> 00:01:21.465\nHij helpt haar.\n\n24\n00:01:21.545 --> 00:01:24.405\nHe helps her.\n\n25\n00:01:24.485 --> 00:01:28.585\nOns means us.\n\n26\n00:01:28.645 --> 00:01:33.126\nZij groet ons.\n\n27\n00:01:33.206 --> 00:01:36.566\nShe greets us.\n\n28\n00:01:36.626 --> 00:01:40.726\nJullie means you all.\n\n29\n00:01:40.806 --> 00:01:44.967\nIk zie jullie.\n\n30\n00:01:45.247 --> 00:01:48.307\nI see you all.\n\n31\n00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:52.247\nHen means them.\n\n32\n00:01:52.327 --> 00:01:56.447\nIk zie hen.\n\n33\n00:01:56.707 --> 00:01:59.107\nI see them.\n\n34\n00:01:59.167 --> 00:02:01.888\nLet's pause and try a question!\n\n35\n00:02:01.928 --> 00:02:05.468\nHow do you say: He sees us?\n\n36\n00:02:05.508 --> 00:02:07.988\nCan you guess the Dutch sentence?\n\n37\n00:02:08.008 --> 00:02:14.228\nThe answer is: Hij ziet ons.\n\n38\n00:02:14.268 --> 00:02:18.489\nHij ziet ons.\n\n39\n00:02:18.529 --> 00:02:20.109\nHe sees us.\n\n40\n00:02:20.129 --> 00:02:22.889\nGreat job! Let's do another!\n\n41\n00:02:22.929 --> 00:02:26.449\nHow do you say: I hear her?\n\n42\n00:02:26.489 --> 00:02:29.109\nThink about the word for her.\n\n43\n00:02:29.189 --> 00:02:33.050\nThe answer is: haar!\n\n44\n00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:36.610\nIk hoor haar.\n\n45\n00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:39.810\nI hear her.\n\n46\n00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:44.230\nLet's practice with a pattern drill!\n\n47\n00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:47.730\nJan kent mij.\n\n48\n00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:50.731\nJan knows me.\n\n49\n00:02:50.791 --> 00:02:54.451\nJan kent jou.\n\n50\n00:02:54.511 --> 00:02:57.411\nJan knows you.\n\n51\n00:02:57.471 --> 00:03:00.951\nJan kent hem.\n\n52\n00:03:01.031 --> 00:03:03.891\nJan knows him.\n\n53\n00:03:03.971 --> 00:03:07.592\nJan kent haar.\n\n54\n00:03:07.672 --> 00:03:10.592\nJan knows her.\n\n55\n00:03:10.672 --> 00:03:14.352\nJan kent ons.\n\n56\n00:03:14.412 --> 00:03:17.352\nJan knows us.\n\n57\n00:03:17.432 --> 00:03:21.133\nJan kent jullie.\n\n58\n00:03:21.193 --> 00:03:24.353\nJan knows you all.\n\n59\n00:03:24.433 --> 00:03:28.073\nJan kent hen.\n\n60\n00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:30.673\nJan knows them.\n\n61\n00:03:30.693 --> 00:03:33.593\nTime for our error clinic!\n\n62\n00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:37.794\nMistake 1: using subject pronouns.\n\n63\n00:03:37.814 --> 00:03:41.854\nBeginners say: Hij ziet ik.\n\n64\n00:03:41.894 --> 00:03:44.674\nHij ziet ik.\n\n65\n00:03:44.734 --> 00:03:46.814\nHe sees I.\n\n66\n00:03:46.834 --> 00:03:48.554\nThat is wrong!\n\n67\n00:03:48.614 --> 00:03:51.194\nIk is a subject pronoun.\n\n68\n00:03:51.374 --> 00:03:55.235\nUse mij or me for objects!\n\n69\n00:03:55.275 --> 00:03:57.655\nHij ziet mij.\n\n70\n00:03:57.715 --> 00:03:59.815\nHe sees me.\n\n71\n00:03:59.855 --> 00:04:04.755\nMistake 2: confusing zij and haar.\n\n72\n00:04:04.815 --> 00:04:08.255\nDon't say: Ik help zij.\n\n73\n00:04:08.315 --> 00:04:10.716\nIk help zij.\n\n74\n00:04:10.916 --> 00:04:12.856\nI help she.\n\n75\n00:04:12.876 --> 00:04:15.556\nThe correct word is haar.\n\n76\n00:04:15.616 --> 00:04:17.916\nIk help haar.\n\n77\n00:04:18.136 --> 00:04:20.336\nI help her.\n\n78\n00:04:20.376 --> 00:04:25.597\nMistake 3: confusing wij and ons.\n\n79\n00:04:25.657 --> 00:04:29.697\nNever say: Zij bellen wij.\n\n80\n00:04:29.757 --> 00:04:32.497\nZij bellen wij.\n\n81\n00:04:32.557 --> 00:04:33.117\nThey call we.\n\n82\n00:04:33.137 --> 00:04:36.897\nThe correct object form is ons.\n\n83\n00:04:36.957 --> 00:04:39.997\nZij bellen ons.\n\n84\n00:04:40.037 --> 00:04:42.398\nThey call us.\n\n85\n00:04:42.478 --> 00:04:45.038\nHere is a quick memory tip!\n\n86\n00:04:45.098 --> 00:04:49.198\nObjects receive the sentence action.\n\n87\n00:04:49.218 --> 00:04:52.138\nNow let's recap today's lesson.\n\n88\n00:04:52.178 --> 00:04:55.298\nVandaag leerden we dit.\n\n89\n00:04:55.318 --> 00:04:58.299\nToday we learned this.\n\n90\n00:04:58.339 --> 00:05:05.739\nMij, jou, hem, haar, ons.\n\n91\n00:05:05.779 --> 00:05:12.560\nMe, you, him, her, us.\n\n92\n00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.120\nGreat work today!\n\n93\n00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:16.860\nKeep practicing every day!\n\n94\n00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:19.000\nTot de volgende keer!\n\n95\n00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:20.260\nUntil next time!\n
