us?\n\n36\n00:02:05.508 --> 00:02:07.988\nCan you guess the Dutch sentence?\n\n37\n00:02:08.008 --> 00:02:14.228\nThe answer is: Hij ziet ons.\n\n38\n00:02:14.268 --> 00:02:18.489\nHe sees us.\n\n39\n00:02:18.529 --> 00:02:20.109\nHe sees us.\n\n40\n00:02:20.129 --> 00:02:22.889\nGreat job! Let's do another!\n\n41\n00:02:22.929 --> 00:02:26.449\nHow do you say: I hear her?\n\n42\n00:02:26.489 --> 00:02:29.109\nThink about the word for her.\n\n43\n00:02:29.189 --> 00:02:33.050\nThe answer is: haar!\n\n44\n00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:36.610\nI hear her.\n\n45\n00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:39.810\nI hear her.\n\n46\n00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:44.230\nLet's practice with a pattern drill!\n\n47\n00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:47.730\nJan knows me.\n\n48\n00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:50.731\nJan knows me.\n\n49\n00:02:50.791 --> 00:02:54.451\nJan knows you.\n\n50\n00:02:54.511 --> 00:02:57.411\nJan knows you.\n\n51\n00:02:57.471 --> 00:03:00.951\nJan knows him.\n\n52\n00:03:01.031 --> 00:03:03.891\nJan knows him.\n\n53\n00:03:03.971 --> 00:03:07.592\nJan knows her.\n\n54\n00:03:07.672 --> 00:03:10.592\nJan knows her.\n\n55\n00:03:10.672 --> 00:03:14.352\nJan knows us.\n\n56\n00:03:14.412 --> 00:03:17.352\nJan knows us.\n\n57\n00:03:17.432 --> 00:03:21.133\nJan knows you all.\n\n58\n00:03:21.193 --> 00:03:24.353\nJan knows you all.\n\n59\n00:03:24.433 --> 00:03:28.073\nJan knows them.\n\n60\n00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:30.673\nJan knows them.\n\n61\n00:03:30.693 --> 00:03:33.593\nTime for our error clinic!\n\n62\n00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:37.794\nMistake 1: using subject pronouns.\n\n63\n00:03:37.814 --> 00:03:41.854\nBeginners say: Hij ziet ik.\n\n64\n00:03:41.894 --> 00:03:44.674\nHe sees I.\n\n65\n00:03:44.734 --> 00:03:46.814\nHe sees I.\n\n66\n00:03:46.834 --> 00:03:48.554\nThat is wrong!\n\n67\n00:03:48.614 --> 00:03:51.194\nIk is a subject pronoun.\n\n68\n00:03:51.374 --> 00:03:55.235\nUse mij or me for objects!\n\n69\n00:03:55.275 --> 00:03:57.655\nHe sees me.\n\n70\n00:03:57.715 --> 00:03:59.815\nHe sees me.\n\n71\n00:03:59.855 --> 00:04:04.755\nMistake 2: confusing zij and haar.\n\n72\n00:04:04.815 --> 00:04:08.255\nDon't say: Ik help zij.\n\n73\n00:04:08.315 --> 00:04:10.716\nI help she.\n\n74\n00:04:10.916 --> 00:04:12.856\nI help she.\n\n75\n00:04:12.876 --> 00:04:15.556\nThe correct word is haar.\n\n76\n00:04:15.616 --> 00:04:17.916\nI help her.\n\n77\n00:04:18.136 --> 00:04:20.336\nI help her.\n\n78\n00:04:20.376 --> 00:04:25.597\nMistake 3: confusing wij and ons.\n\n79\n00:04:25.657 --> 00:04:29.697\nNever say: Zij bellen wij.\n\n80\n00:04:29.757 --> 00:04:32.497\nThey call we.\n\n81\n00:04:32.557 --> 00:04:33.117\nThey call we.\n\n82\n00:04:33.137 --> 00:04:36.897\nThe correct object form is ons.\n\n83\n00:04:36.957 --> 00:04:39.997\nThey call us.\n\n84\n00:04:40.037 --> 00:04:42.398\nThey call us.\n\n85\n00:04:42.478 --> 00:04:45.038\nHere is a quick memory tip!\n\n86\n00:04:45.098 --> 00:04:49.198\nObjects receive the sentence action.\n\n87\n00:04:49.218 --> 00:04:52.138\nNow let's recap today's lesson.\n\n88\n00:04:52.178 --> 00:04:55.298\nToday we learned this.\n\n89\n00:04:55.318 --> 00:04:58.299\nToday we learned this.\n\n90\n00:04:58.339 --> 00:05:05.739\nMe, you, him, her, us.\n\n91\n00:05:05.779 --> 00:05:12.560\nMe, you, him, her, us.\n\n92\n00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.120\nGreat work today!\n\n93\n00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:16.860\nKeep practicing every day!\n\n94\n00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:19.000\nUntil next time!\n\n95\n00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:20.260\nUntil next time!\n
grammar_om_te	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:05.560\nImagine you are at a cozy café.\n\n2\n00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:08.440\nYou want to give a reason.\n\n3\n00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:10.421\nWhy are you there?\n\n4\n00:00:10.441 --> 00:00:12.761\nTo drink a coffee!\n\n5\n00:00:12.821 --> 00:00:17.781\nIn Dutch, we use: om... te.\n\n6\n00:00:17.861 --> 00:00:20.821\nIt means: in order to.\n\n7\n00:00:20.901 --> 00:00:24.381\nOr simply: to do something.\n\n8\n00:00:24.541 --> 00:00:27.042\nLaten we beginnen!\n\n9\n00:00:27.122 --> 00:00:29.422\nLet's get started!\n\n10\n00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:32.982\nHere is a short Dutch sentence.\n\n11\n00:00:33.062 --> 00:00:37.222\nIk ben hier om te leren.\n\n12\n00:00:37.382 --> 00:00:41.282\nI am here in order to learn.\n\n13\n00:00:41.302 --> 00:00:45.183\nNotice the word OM at the start.\n\n14\n00:00:45.223 --> 00:00:49.603\nNotice the word TE before the verb.\n\n15\n00:00:49.663 --> 00:00:53.603\nThe main verb goes at the end!\n\n16\n00:00:53.683 --> 00:00:56.723\nIn English: to learn.\n\n17\n00:00:56.783 --> 00:01:00.804\nIn Dutch: om te leren.\n\n18\n00:01:00.924 --> 00:01:04.164\nLet's try another simple sentence.\n\n19\n00:01:04.224 --> 00:01:07.464\nHij gaat naar bed.\n\n20\n00:01:07.524 --> 00:01:09.424\nHe goes to bed.\n\n21\n00:01:09.504 --> 00:01:12.564\nWhy is he going to bed?\n\n22\n00:01:12.624 --> 00:01:16.365\nHij gaat om te slapen.\n\n23\n00:01:16.405 --> 00:01:20.085\nHe goes in order to sleep.\n\n24\n00:01:20.105 --> 00:01:23.785\nCan we combine these two ideas?\n\n25\n00:01:23.845 --> 00:01:28.205\nHij gaat naar bed om te slapen.\n\n26\n00:01:28.245 --> 00:01:31.725\nHe goes to bed to sleep.\n\n27\n00:01:31.745 --> 00:01:33.346\nPerfect!\n\n28\n00:01:33.486 --> 00:01:37.866\nNow, let's build a longer sentence.\n\n29\n00:01:37.946 --> 00:01:40.826\nIk eet een appel.\n\n30\n00:01:40.986 --> 00:01:43.466\nI eat an apple.\n\n31\n00:01:43.526 --> 00:01:46.246\nWhy do you eat an apple?\n\n32\n00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:49.087\nOm gezond te blijven.\n\n33\n00:01:49.147 --> 00:01:52.367\nIn order to stay healthy.\n\n34\n00:01:52.447 --> 00:01:54.987\nNow let me ask you something.\n\n35\n00:01:55.047 --> 00:01:58.287\nHow do you say: to sleep?\n\n36\n00:01:58.327 --> 00:02:00.747\nThink about the pattern.\n\n37\n00:02:00.767 --> 00:02:05.008\nThe answer is: om te slapen.\n\n38\n00:02:05.048 --> 00:02:07.488\nHet is tijd om te slapen.\n\n39\n00:02:07.568 --> 00:02:11.908\nIt is time to sleep.\n\n40\n00:02:12.028 --> 00:02:16.588\nNow, how about: to study?\n\n41\n00:02:16.608 --> 00:02:22.189\nThe Dutch verb is studeren.\n\n42\n00:02:22.249 --> 00:02:27.169\nHow would you say: to study?\n\n43\n00:02:27.189 --> 00:02:33.669\nThat is right: om te studeren.\n\n44\n00:02:33.769 --> 00:02:40.730\nIk studeer om te leren.\n\n45\n00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:45.890\nI study in order to learn.\n\n46\n00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:49.590\nPattern drill time!\n\n47\n00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:54.751\nLet's repeat with different actions.\n\n48\n00:02:54.791 --> 00:02:59.871\nFirst action: buying bread.\n\n49\n00:02:59.971 --> 00:03:06.891\nIk ga om brood te kopen.\n\n50\n00:03:07.011 --> 00:03:12.052\nI go to buy bread.\n\n51\n00:03:12.132 --> 00:03:17.052\nSecond action: making tea.\n\n52\n00:03:17.132 --> 00:03:23.972\nIk ben hier om thee te maken.\n\n53\n00:03:24.132 --> 00:03:29.153\nI am here to make tea.\n\n54\n00:03:29.193 --> 00:03:33.813\nThird action: helping you.\n\n55\n00:03:33.873 --> 00:03:39.993\nIk kom om je te helpen.\n\n56\n00:03:40.133 --> 00:03:43.193\nI come to help you.\n\n57\n00:03:43.213 --> 00:03:46.294\nGreat job on these sentences!\n\n58\n00:03:46.414 --> 00:03:50.754\nNow, let's visit the Error Clinic!\n\n59\n00:03:50.814 --> 00:03:54.094\nHere is a common beginner mistake.\n\n60\n00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:57.574\nSome people forget the word TE.\n\n61\n00:03:57.594 --> 00:04:00.815\nThey say this incorrect sentence:\n\n62\n00:04:00.875 --> 00:04:03.615\nIk ben hier om leren.\n\n63\n00:04:03.755 --> 00:04:05.955\nI am here to learn.\n\n64\n00:04:05.995 --> 00:04:07.895\nWhat is wrong here?\n\n65\n00:04:07.935 --> 00:04:11.995\nThe word TE is missing before leren!\n\n66\n00:04:12.015 --> 00:04:14.235\nThe correct sentence is:\n\n67\n00:04:14.315 --> 00:04:17.416\nIk ben hier om te leren.\n\n68\n00:04:17.536 --> 00:04:19.796\nI am here to learn.\n\n69\n00:04:19.896 --> 00:04:23.416\nAnother mistake is wrong word order.\n\n70\n00:04:23.456 --> 00:04:27.276\nBeginners put TE in wrong places.\n\n71\n00:04:27.296 --> 00:04:28.716\nThey say:\n\n72\n00:04:28.796 --> 00:04:30.916\nIk ga om te eten een appel.\n\n73\n00:04:30.936 --> 00:04:32.416\nI go to eat an apple.\n\n74\n00:04:32.436 --> 00:04:34.237\nThat is wrong!\n\n75\n00:04:34.257 --> 00:04:38.917\nPut extra words inside om... te!\n\n76\n00:04:38.977 --> 00:04:41.437\nHere is the correct sentence:\n\n77\n00:04:41.517 --> 00:04:45.317\nIk ga om een appel te eten.\n\n78\n00:04:45.437 --> 00:04:48.277\nI am going to eat an apple.\n\n79\n00:04:48.337 --> 00:04:51.138\nRemember this simple rule:\n\n80\n00:04:51.218 --> 00:04:54.598\nOM starts the reason structure.\n\n81\n00:04:54.638 --> 00:04:57.878\nTE goes right before the verb.\n\n82\n00:04:57.938 --> 00:05:01.078\nAnd the verb ends the phrase!\n\n83\n00:05:01.138 --> 00:05:06.859\nMemory tip: OM... TE split the reason!\n\n84\n00:05:06.879 --> 00:05:09.859\nTime for our final summary!\n\n85\n00:05:09.919 --> 00:05:12.739\nVandaag leerden we:\n\n86\n00:05:12.799 --> 00:05:17.239\nGebruik om te met een werkwoord.\n\n87\n00:05:17.279 --> 00:05:20.979\nUse om te with a verb.\n\n88\n00:05:21.039 --> 00:05:24.600\nHet werkwoord komt aan het einde.\n\n89\n00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:27.640\nThe verb comes at the end.\n\n90\n00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.940\nFantastic work today!\n\n91\n00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:31.080\nSee you next time!\n
