292 --> 00:03:56.872\nWe travel in the summer.\n\n61\n00:03:57.012 --> 00:04:01.513\nFrom two to three I rest.\n\n62\n00:04:01.553 --> 00:04:04.733\nFrom two to three I rest.\n\n63\n00:04:04.853 --> 00:04:08.233\nThey call in an hour.\n\n64\n00:04:08.293 --> 00:04:10.473\nThey call in an hour.\n\n65\n00:04:10.533 --> 00:04:15.093\nNow let's visit the error clinic.\n\n66\n00:04:15.153 --> 00:04:18.694\nBeginner mistake number one:\n\n67\n00:04:18.774 --> 00:04:23.774\nSaying IN for time on clocks.\n\n68\n00:04:23.814 --> 00:04:28.174\nIncorrect: IN negen uur.\n\n69\n00:04:28.214 --> 00:04:30.474\nWhy is this wrong?\n\n70\n00:04:30.494 --> 00:04:35.895\nClock times always take OM, not IN!\n\n71\n00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:39.855\nI come at nine o'clock.\n\n72\n00:04:39.955 --> 00:04:43.215\nI come at nine o'clock.\n\n73\n00:04:43.255 --> 00:04:46.715\nBeginner mistake number two:\n\n74\n00:04:46.895 --> 00:04:51.135\nUsing IN for days of the week.\n\n75\n00:04:51.195 --> 00:04:55.576\nIncorrect: IN maandag.\n\n76\n00:04:55.616 --> 00:04:58.576\nDays of the week take OP!\n\n77\n00:04:58.656 --> 00:05:02.316\nI work on Monday.\n\n78\n00:05:02.436 --> 00:05:04.836\nI work on Monday.\n\n79\n00:05:04.996 --> 00:05:08.236\nBeginner mistake number three:\n\n80\n00:05:08.376 --> 00:05:12.536\nUsing IN for future minutes.\n\n81\n00:05:12.616 --> 00:05:16.837\nIncorrect: IN tien minuten.\n\n82\n00:05:16.957 --> 00:05:21.037\nUse OVER for future time intervals!\n\n83\n00:05:21.097 --> 00:05:24.917\nIt starts in ten minutes.\n\n84\n00:05:25.017 --> 00:05:27.957\nIt starts in ten minutes.\n\n85\n00:05:27.997 --> 00:05:30.337\nHere is your memory anchor.\n\n86\n00:05:30.417 --> 00:05:34.258\nOM for clocks, OP for days.\n\n87\n00:05:34.338 --> 00:05:38.798\nIN for months, OVER for later.\n\n88\n00:05:38.978 --> 00:05:42.698\nVAN and TOT for start and end!\n\n89\n00:05:42.758 --> 00:05:44.518\nGreat job today!\n\n90\n00:05:44.558 --> 00:05:47.458\nLet's do a quick spoken recap.\n\n91\n00:05:47.518 --> 00:05:51.658\nToday we learned the prepositions.\n\n92\n00:05:51.698 --> 00:05:55.039\nToday we learned the prepositions.\n\n93\n00:05:55.139 --> 00:05:58.439\nOm for clock times.\n\n94\n00:05:58.539 --> 00:06:00.939\nOm for clock times.\n\n95\n00:06:01.019 --> 00:06:04.259\nOp for days of the week.\n\n96\n00:06:04.359 --> 00:06:06.759\nOp for days of the week.\n\n97\n00:06:06.839 --> 00:06:10.199\nIn for months and seasons.\n\n98\n00:06:10.299 --> 00:06:12.900\nIn for months and seasons.\n\n99\n00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:15.860\nAnd over for the future.\n\n100\n00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:18.560\nAnd over for the future.\n\n101\n00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:20.140\nSee you in the next lesson!\n
grammar_reflexive_verbs	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:04.500\nImagine telling someone how you feel.\n\n2\n00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:07.161\nOr saying that you are mistaken.\n\n3\n00:00:07.221 --> 00:00:10.661\nIn Dutch, we use reflexive verbs.\n\n4\n00:00:10.721 --> 00:00:13.561\nThese verbs need a special pronoun.\n\n5\n00:00:13.601 --> 00:00:16.642\nIn English, you say 'myself'.\n\n6\n00:00:16.682 --> 00:00:21.102\nIn Dutch, we say 'me' or 'zich'.\n\n7\n00:00:21.142 --> 00:00:22.962\nLaten we beginnen!\n\n8\n00:00:23.002 --> 00:00:24.502\nLet us begin!\n\n9\n00:00:24.582 --> 00:00:27.623\nLet's look at 'zich wassen'.\n\n10\n00:00:27.663 --> 00:00:30.323\nThat means 'to wash oneself'.\n\n11\n00:00:30.383 --> 00:00:32.203\nIk was me.\n\n12\n00:00:32.283 --> 00:00:34.063\nI wash myself.\n\n13\n00:00:34.143 --> 00:00:36.623\nNow let's add more detail.\n\n14\n00:00:36.683 --> 00:00:39.444\nIk was me met water.\n\n15\n00:00:39.544 --> 00:00:42.184\nI wash myself with water.\n\n16\n00:00:42.204 --> 00:00:43.984\nWhat about 'you'?\n\n17\n00:00:44.024 --> 00:00:47.304\nFor 'jij', we use 'je'.\n\n18\n00:00:47.385 --> 00:00:49.405\nJij wast je.\n\n19\n00:00:49.465 --> 00:00:51.405\nYou wash yourself.\n\n20\n00:00:51.485 --> 00:00:54.725\nJij wast je elke ochtend.\n\n21\n00:00:54.805 --> 00:00:57.966\nYou wash yourself every morning.\n\n22\n00:00:57.986 --> 00:01:00.526\nCan you guess for 'he'?\n\n23\n00:01:00.546 --> 00:01:04.346\nFor 'hij', we use 'zich'.\n\n24\n00:01:04.386 --> 00:01:07.486\nHij wast zich.\n\n25\n00:01:07.526 --> 00:01:09.467\nHe washes himself.\n\n26\n00:01:09.527 --> 00:01:13.027\nHij wast zich snel.\n\n27\n00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:15.407\nHe washes himself quickly.\n\n28\n00:01:15.527 --> 00:01:19.168\nNow let's try 'zich voelen'.\n\n29\n00:01:19.208 --> 00:01:21.468\nIt means 'to feel'.\n\n30\n00:01:21.528 --> 00:01:24.308\nIk voel me goed.\n\n31\n00:01:24.468 --> 00:01:25.968\nI feel good.\n\n32\n00:01:26.048 --> 00:01:29.329\nJij voelt je goed.\n\n33\n00:01:29.369 --> 00:01:30.829\nYou feel good.\n\n34\n00:01:30.889 --> 00:01:34.429\nHij voelt zich goed.\n\n35\n00:01:34.469 --> 00:01:35.969\nHe feels good.\n\n36\n00:01:36.009 --> 00:01:38.149\nWhat about 'we'?\n\n37\n00:01:38.209 --> 00:01:42.290\nFor 'wij', we use 'ons'!\n\n38\n00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:46.150\nWij voelen ons goed.\n\n39\n00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:47.650\nWe feel good.\n\n40\n00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:50.991\nHow would you say 'they feel good'?\n\n41\n00:01:51.011 --> 00:01:55.591\nFor 'zij' plural, use 'zich'.\n\n42\n00:01:55.651 --> 00:01:58.991\nZij voelen zich goed.\n\n43\n00:01:59.011 --> 00:02:01.112\nThey feel good.\n\n44\n00:02:01.172 --> 00:02:04.332\nLet's try 'zich vergissen'.\n\n45\n00:02:04.372 --> 00:02:06.672\nIt means 'to be mistaken'.\n\n46\n00:02:06.732 --> 00:02:08.972\nIk vergis me.\n\n47\n00:02:09.092 --> 00:02:10.613\nI am mistaken.\n\n48\n00:02:10.653 --> 00:02:13.893\nHij vergist zich vaak.\n\n49\n00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:16.093\nHe is often mistaken.\n\n50\n00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:19.413\nWij vergissen ons nooit.\n\n51\n00:02:19.453 --> 00:02:21.494\nWe are never mistaken.\n\n52\n00:02:21.514 --> 00:02:24.274\nTime for our error clinic!\n\n53\n00:02:24.314 --> 00:02:27.694\nMistake one: forgetting the pronoun.\n\n54\n00:02:27.754 --> 00:02:29.994\nIk voel goed.\n\n55\n00:02:30.014 --> 00:02:31.995\nThis is wrong in Dutch!\n\n56\n00:02:32.035 --> 00:02:34.495\nYou must include 'me'.\n\n57\n00:02:34.555 --> 00:02:37.335\nIk voel me goed.\n\n58\n00:02:37.415 --> 00:02:38.995\nI feel good.\n\n59\n00:02:39.015 --> 00:02:43.276\nMistake two: wrong pronoun for 'hij'.\n\n60\n00:02:43.316 --> 00:02:47.456\nDon't say 'hij voelt hem'.\n\n61\n00:02:47.516 --> 00:02:50.696\nUse 'zich' for 'hij'!\n\n62\n00:02:50.716 --> 00:02:55.217\nHij voelt zich goed.\n\n63\n00:02:55.257 --> 00:02:57.617\nHe feels good.\n\n64\n00:02:57.657 --> 00:03:00.437\nRemember this quick tip:\n\n65\n00:03:00.457 --> 00:03:06.298\n'Ik' gets 'me', 'jij' gets 'je'.\n\n66\n00:03:06.338 --> 00:03:10.638\n'Hij' and 'zij' get 'zich'.\n\n67\n00:03:10.658 --> 00:03:14.259\n'Wij' always gets 'ons'!\n\n68\n00:03:14.299 --> 00:03:19.699\nVandaag leerden we reflexieve werkwoorden.\n\n69\n00:03:19.739 --> 00:03:23.340\nToday we learned reflexive verbs.\n\n70\n00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:26.800\nGreat job! Keep practicing every day.\n
grammar_reflexive_verbs	en	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:04.500\nImagine telling someone how you feel.\n\n2\n00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:07.161\nOr saying that you are mistaken.\n\n3\n00:00:07.221 --> 00:00:10.661\nIn Dutch, we use reflexive verbs.\n\n4\n00:00:10.721 --> 00:00:13.561\nThese verbs need a special pronoun.\n\n5\n00:00:13.601 --> 00:00:16.642\nIn English, you say 'myself'.\n\n6\n00:00:16.682 --> 00:00:21.102\nIn Dutch, we say 'me' or 'zich'.\n\n7\n00:00:21.142 --> 00:00:22.962\nLet us begin!\n\n8\n00:00:23.002 --> 00:00:24.502\nLet us begin!\n\n9\n00:00:24.582 --> 00:00:27.623\nLet's look at 'zich wassen'.\n\n10\n00:00:27.663 --> 00:00:30.323\nThat means 'to wash oneself'.\n\n11\n00:00:30.383 --> 00:00:32.203\nI wash myself.\n\n12\n00:00:32.283 --> 00:00:34.063\nI wash myself.\n\n13\n00:00:34.143 --> 00:00:36.623\nNow let's add more detail.\n\n14\n00:00:36.683 --> 00:00:39.444\nI wash myself with water.\n\n15\n00:00:39.544 --> 00:00:42.184\nI wash myself with water.\n\n16\n00:00:42.204 --> 00:00:43.984\nWhat about 'you'?\n\n17\n00:00:44.024 --> 00:00:47.304\nFor 'jij', we use 'je'.\n\n18\n00:00:47.385 --> 00:00:49.405\nYou wash yourself.\n\n19\n00:00:49.465 --> 00:00:51.405\nYou wash yourself.\n\n20\n00:00:51.485 --> 00:00:54.725\nYou wash yourself every morning.\n\n21\n00:00:54.805 --> 00:00:57.966\nYou wash yourself every morning.\n\n22\n00:00:57.986 --> 00:01:00.526\nCan you guess for 'he'?\n\n23\n00:01:00.546 --> 00:01:04.346\nFor 'hij', we use 'zich'.\n\n24\n00:01:04.386 --> 00:01:07.486\nHe washes himself.\n\n25\n00:01:07.526 --> 00:01:09.467\nHe washes himself.\n\n26\n00:01:09.527 --> 00:01:13.027\nHe washes himself quickly.\n\n27\n00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:15.407\nHe washes himself quickly.\n\n28\n00:01:15.527 --> 00:01:19.168\nNow let's try 'zich voelen'.\n\n29\n00:01:19.208 --> 00:01:21.468\nIt means 'to feel'.\n\n30\n00:01:21.528 --> 00:01:24.308\nI feel good.\n\n31\n00:01:24.468 --> 00:01:25.968\nI feel good.\n\n32\n00:01:26.048 --> 00:01:29.329\nYou feel good.\n\n33\n00:01:29.369 --> 00:01:30.829\nYou feel good.\n\n34\n00:01:30.889 --> 00:01:34.429\nHe feels good.\n\n35\n00:01:34.469 --> 00:01:35.969\nHe feels good.\n\n36\n00:01:36.009 --> 00:01:38.149\nWhat about 'we'?\n\n37\n00:01:38.209 --> 00:01:42.290\nFor 'wij', we use 'ons'!\n\n38\n00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:46.150\nWe feel good.\n\n39\n00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:47.650\nWe feel good.\n\n40\n00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:50.991\nHow would you say 'they feel good'?\n\n41\n00:01:51.011 --> 00:01:55.591\nFor 'zij' plural, use 'zich'.\n\n42\n00:01:55.651 --> 00:01:58.991\nThey feel good.\n\n43\n00:01:59.011 --> 00:02:01.112\nThey feel good.\n\n44\n00:02:01.172 --> 00:02:04.332\nLet's try 'zich vergissen'.\n\n45\n00:02:04.372 --> 00:02:06.672\nIt means 'to be mistaken'.\n\n46\n00:02:06.732 --> 00:02:08.972\nI am mistaken.\n\n47\n00:02:09.092 --> 00:02:10.613\nI am mistaken.\n\n48\n00:02:10.653 --> 00:02:13.893\nHe is often mistaken.\n\n49\n00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:16.093\nHe is often mistaken.\n\n50\n00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:19.413\nWe are never mistaken.\n\n51\n00:02:19.453 --> 00:02:21.494\nWe are never mistaken.\n\n52\n00:02:21.514 --> 00:02:24.274\nTime for our error clinic!\n\n53\n00:02:24.314 --> 00:02:27.694\nMistake one: forgetting the pronoun.\n\n54\n00:02:27.754 --> 00:02:29.994\nI feel good.\n\n55\n00:02:30.014 --> 00:02:31.995\nThis is wrong in Dutch!\n\n56\n00:02:32.035 --> 00:02:34.495\nYou must include 'me'.\n\n57\n00:02:34.555 --> 00:02:37.335\nI feel good.\n\n58\n00:02:37.415 --> 00:02:38.995\nI feel good.\n\n59\n00:02:39.015 --> 00:02:43.276\nMistake two: wrong pronoun for 'hij'.\n\n60\n00:02:43.316 --> 00:02:47.456\nDon't say 'hij voelt hem'.\n\n61\n00:02:47.516 --> 00:02:50.696\nUse 'zich' for 'hij'!\n\n62\n00:02:50.716 --> 00:02:55.217\nHe feels good.\n\n63\n00:02:55.257 --> 00:02:57.617\nHe feels good.\n\n64\n00:02:57.657 --> 00:03:00.437\nRemember this quick tip:\n\n65\n00:03:00.457 --> 00:03:06.298\n'Ik' gets 'me', 'jij' gets 'je'.\n\n66\n00:03:06.338 --> 00:03:10.638\n'Hij' and 'zij' get 'zich'.\n\n67\n00:03:10.658 --> 00:03:14.259\n'Wij' always gets 'ons'!\n\n68\n00:03:14.299 --> 00:03:19.699\nToday we learned reflexive verbs.\n\n69\n00:03:19.739 --> 00:03:23.340\nToday we learned reflexive verbs.\n\n70\n00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:26.800\nGreat job! Keep practicing every day.\n
grammar_relative_clauses	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:05.960\nImagine talking about a specific book or person.\n\n2\n00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.400\nYou want to say: 'the man who'.\n\n3\n00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:13.140\nOr: 'the book that I read'.\n\n4\n00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:19.061\nIn Dutch, we use DIE and DAT.\n\n5\n00:00:19.121 --> 00:00:21.741\nLaten we beginnen!\n\n6\n00:00:21.781 --> 00:00:24.581\nLet's begin!\n\n7\n00:00:24.601 --> 00:00:27.561\nThe rule is very simple.\n\n8\n00:00:27.681 --> 00:00:32.321\nUse DIE for DE-words and plurals.\n\n9\n00:00:32.461 --> 00:00:37.221\nUse DAT for HET-words.\n\n10\n00:00:37.261 --> 00:00:42.081\nIn English, you say WHO or THAT.\n\n11\n00:00:42.141 --> 00:00:46.982\nIn Dutch, choosing depends on the noun.\n\n12\n00:00:47.042 --> 00:00:51.302\nLet's look at a DE-word first.\n\n13\n00:00:51.322 --> 00:00:54.742\nThe word is 'man'.\n\n14\n00:00:54.802 --> 00:00:59.162\nIn Dutch: DE man.\n\n15\n00:00:59.202 --> 00:01:04.062\nDe man die hier werkt.\n\n16\n00:01:04.102 --> 00:01:07.722\nThe man who works here.\n\n17\n00:01:07.762 --> 00:01:13.063\nNotice we used DIE for DE man.\n\n18\n00:01:13.083 --> 00:01:17.243\nNow, let's look at a HET-word.\n\n19\n00:01:17.263 --> 00:01:20.683\nThe word is 'boek'.\n\n20\n00:01:20.723 --> 00:01:24.863\nIn Dutch: HET boek.\n\n21\n00:01:24.943 --> 00:01:29.443\nHet boek dat ik lees.\n\n22\n00:01:29.463 --> 00:01:32.423\nThe book that I read.\n\n23\n00:01:32.463 --> 00:01:37.564\nNotice we used DAT for HET boek.\n\n24\n00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:40.644\nLet's try another example together.\n\n25\n00:01:40.704 --> 00:01:43.884\nWhat about 'vrouw'?\n\n26\n00:01:43.904 --> 00:01:47.104\n'Vrouw' is a DE-word.\n\n27\n00:01:47.124 --> 00:01:51.284\nCan you guess: DIE or DAT?\n\n28\n00:01:51.324 --> 00:01:54.764\nThat's right, we use DIE!\n\n29\n00:01:54.804 --> 00:01:58.664\nDe vrouw die daar staat.\n\n30\n00:01:58.684 --> 00:02:02.004\nThe woman who stands there.\n\n31\n00:02:02.024 --> 00:02:04.845\nWhat about plural nouns?\n\n32\n00:02:04.865 --> 00:02:08.585\nPlural nouns ALWAYS take DE!\n\n33\n00:02:08.645 --> 00:02:12.845\nSo plurals ALWAYS use DIE!\n\n34\n00:02:12.945 --> 00:02:16.225\nLet's look at 'boeken'.\n\n35\n00:02:16.265 --> 00:02:20.005\nDe boeken die hier liggen.\n\n36\n00:02:20.025 --> 00:02:23.645\nThe books that lie here.\n\n37\n00:02:23.665 --> 00:02:27.485\nNow, what about 'huis'?\n\n38\n00:02:27.505 --> 00:02:30.845\n'Huis' is a HET-word.\n\n39\n00:02:30.885 --> 00:02:34.786\nHow would you say 'that I buy'?\n\n40\n00:02:34.826 --> 00:02:38.606\nHet huis dat ik koop.\n\n41\n00:02:38.626 --> 00:02:41.986\nThe house that I buy.\n\n42\n00:02:42.026 --> 00:02:44.326\nNotice where the verb goes!\n\n43\n00:02:44.386 --> 00:02:49.626\nIn relative clauses, verbs go last!\n\n44\n00:02:49.666 --> 00:02:54.286\nDe man die snel loopt.\n\n45\n00:02:54.306 --> 00:02:58.186\nThe man who walks fast.\n\n46\n00:02:58.246 --> 00:03:02.847\nHet kind dat hier speelt.\n\n47\n00:03:02.867 --> 00:03:06.867\nThe child that plays here.\n\n48\n00:03:06.927 --> 00:03:11.187\nDe auto die ik zie.\n\n49\n00:03:11.207 --> 00:03:14.687\nThe car that I see.\n\n50\n00:03:14.707 --> 00:03:18.107\nNow for the Error Clinic!\n\n51\n00:03:18.127 --> 00:03:23.687\nMistake one: using DAT with DE-words.\n\n52\n00:03:23.727 --> 00:03:28.648\nIncorrect: De man dat werkt.\n\n53\n00:03:28.668 --> 00:03:30.808\nWhy is this wrong?\n\n54\n00:03:30.828 --> 00:03:36.208\n'Man' is a DE-word, so use DIE!\n\n55\n00:03:36.248 --> 00:03:40.408\nDe man die werkt.\n\n56\n00:03:40.428 --> 00:03:43.668\nThe man who works.\n\n57\n00:03:43.688 --> 00:03:48.768\nMistake two: using DIE with HET-words.\n\n58\n00:03:48.808 --> 00:03:54.208\nIncorrect: Het boek die ik lees.\n\n59\n00:03:54.228 --> 00:03:56.609\nCorrect version:\n\n60\n00:03:56.649 --> 00:04:00.329\nHet boek dat ik lees.\n\n61\n00:04:00.349 --> 00:04:03.029\nThe book that I read.\n\n62\n00:04:03.069 --> 00:04:05.889\nHere is your memory anchor!\n\n63\n00:04:05.929 --> 00:04:09.329\nDE matches DIE.\n\n64\n00:04:09.389 --> 00:04:12.709\nHET matches DAT.\n\n65\n00:04:12.749 --> 00:04:15.829\nBoth end with similar sounds!\n\n66\n00:04:15.889 --> 00:04:20.189\nVandaag leerden we relatieve voornaamwoorden.\n\n67\n00:04:20.229 --> 00:04:23.970\nToday we learned relative pronouns.\n\n68\n00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:28.070\nGebruik die voor de-woorden.\n\n69\n00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:29.170\nUse die for de-words.\n\n70\n00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:32.630\nGebruik dat voor het-woorden.\n\n71\n00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:33.530\nUse dat for het-words.\n\n72\n00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:35.490\nGreat job today! Tot ziens!\n
grammar_relative_clauses	en	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:05.960\nImagine talking about a specific book or person.\n\n2\n00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.400\nYou want to say: 'the man who'.\n\n3\n00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:13.140\nOr: 'the book that I read'.\n\n4\n00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:19.061\nIn Dutch, we use DIE and DAT.\n\n5\n00:00:19.121 --> 00:00:21.741\nLet's begin!\n\n6\n00:00:21.781 --> 00:00:24.581\nLet's begin!\n\n7\n00:00:24.601 --> 00:00:27.561\nThe rule is very simple.\n\n8\n00:00:27.681 --> 00:00:32.321\nUse DIE for DE-words and plurals.\n\n9\n00:00:32.461 --> 00:00:37.221\nUse DAT for HET-words.\n\n10\n00:00:37.261 --> 00:00:42.081\nIn English, you say WHO or THAT.\n\n11\n00:00:42.141 --> 00:00:46.982\nIn Dutch, choosing depends on the noun.\n\n12\n00:00:47.042 --> 00:00:51.302\nLet's look at a DE-word first.\n\n13\n00:00:51.322 --> 00:00:54.742\nThe word is 'man'.\n\n14\n00:00:54.802 --> 00:00:59.162\nIn Dutch: DE man.\n\n15\n00:00:59.202 --> 00:01:04.062\nThe man who works here.\n\n16\n00:01:04.102 --> 00:01:07.722\nThe man who works here.\n\n17\n00:01:07.762 --> 00:01:13.063\nNotice we used DIE for DE man.\n\n18\n00:01:13.083 --> 00:01:17.243\nNow, let's look at a HET-word.\n\n19\n00:01:17.263 --> 00:01:20.683\nThe word is 'boek'.\n\n20\n00:01:20.723 --> 00:01:24.863\nIn Dutch: HET boek.\n\n21\n00:01:24.943 --> 00:01:29.443\nThe book that I read.\n\n22\n00:01:29.463 --> 00:01:32.423\nThe book that I read.\n\n23\n00:01:32.463 --> 00:01:37.564\nNotice we used DAT for HET boek.\n\n24\n00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:40.644\nLet's try another example together.\n\n25\n00:01:40.704 --> 00:01:43.884\nWhat about 'vrouw'?\n\n26\n00:01:43.904 --> 00:01:47.104\n'Vrouw' is a DE-word.\n\n27\n00:01:47.124 --> 00:01:51.284\nCan you guess: DIE or DAT?\n\n28\n00:01:51.324 --> 00:01:54.764\nThat's right, we use DIE!\n\n29\n00:01:54.804 --> 00:01:58.664\nThe woman who stands there.\n\n30\n00:01:58.684 --> 00:02:02.004\nThe woman who stands there.\n\n31\n00:02:02.024 --> 00:02:04.845\nWhat about plural nouns?\n\n32\n00:02:04.865 --> 00:02:08.585\nPlural nouns ALWAYS take DE!\n\n33\n00:02:08.645 --> 00:02:12.845\nSo plurals ALWAYS use DIE!\n\n34\n00:02:12.945 --> 00:02:16.225\nLet's look at 'boeken'.\n\n35\n00:02:16.265 --> 00:02:20.005\nThe books that lie here.\n\n36\n00:02:20.025 --> 00:02:23.645\nThe books that lie here.\n\n37\n00:02:23.665 --> 00:02:27.485\nNow, what about 'huis'?\n\n38\n00:02:27.505 --> 00:02:30.845\n'Huis' is a HET-word.\n\n39\n00:02:30.885 --> 00:02:34.786\nHow would you say 'that I buy'?\n\n40\n00:02:34.826 --> 00:02:38.606\nThe house that I buy.\n\n41\n00:02:38.626 --> 00:02:41.986\nThe house that I buy.\n\n42\n00:02:42.026 --> 00:02:44.326\nNotice where the verb goes!\n\n43\n00:02:44.386 --> 00:02:49.626\nIn relative clauses, verbs go last!\n\n44\n00:02:49.666 --> 00:02:54.286\nThe man who walks fast.\n\n45\n00:02:54.306 --> 00:02:58.186\nThe man who walks fast.\n\n46\n00:02:58.246 --> 00:03:02.847\nThe child that plays here.\n\n47\n00:03:02.867 --> 00:03:06.867\nThe child that plays here.\n\n48\n00:03:06.927 --> 00:03:11.187\nThe car that I see.\n\n49\n00:03:11.207 --> 00:03:14.687\nThe car that I see.\n\n50\n00:03:14.707 --> 00:03:18.107\nNow for the Error Clinic!\n\n51\n00:03:18.127 --> 00:03:23.687\nMistake one: using DAT with DE-words.\n\n52\n00:03:23.727 --> 00:03:28.648\nIncorrect: De man dat werkt.\n\n53\n00:03:28.668 --> 00:03:30.808\nWhy is this wrong?\n\n54\n00:03:30.828 --> 00:03:36.208\n'Man' is a DE-word, so use DIE!\n\n55\n00:03:36.248 --> 00:03:40.408\nThe man who works.\n\n56\n00:03:40.428 --> 00:03:43.668\nThe man who works.\n\n57\n00:03:43.688 --> 00:03:48.768\nMistake two: using DIE with HET-words.\n\n58\n00:03:48.808 --> 00:03:54.208\nIncorrect: Het boek die ik lees.\n\n59\n00:03:54.228 --> 00:03:56.609\nCorrect version:\n\n60\n00:03:56.649 --> 00:04:00.329\nThe book that I read.\n\n61\n00:04:00.349 --> 00:04:03.029\nThe book that I read.\n\n62\n00:04:03.069 --> 00:04:05.889\nHere is your memory anchor!\n\n63\n00:04:05.929 --> 00:04:09.329\nDE matches DIE.\n\n64\n00:04:09.389 --> 00:04:12.709\nHET matches DAT.\n\n65\n00:04:12.749 --> 00:04:15.829\nBoth end with similar sounds!\n\n66\n00:04:15.889 --> 00:04:20.189\nToday we learned relative pronouns.\n\n67\n00:04:20.229 --> 00:04:23.970\nToday we learned relative pronouns.\n\n68\n00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:28.070\nUse die for de-words.\n\n69\n00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:29.170\nUse die for de-words.\n\n70\n00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:32.630\nUse dat for het-words.\n\n71\n00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:33.530\nUse dat for het-words.\n\n72\n00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:35.490\nGreat job today! See you!\n
grammar_separable_verbs	en	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:05.020\nImagine calling a friend in Dutch.\n\n2\n00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:08.640\nYou want to say: I call you.\n\n3\n00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:13.300\nIn Dutch, the verb splits apart!\n\n4\n00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:15.240\nLet's begin!\n\n5\n00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:16.961\nLet's begin!\n\n6\n00:00:17.001 --> 00:00:21.021\nToday we learn about separable verbs.\n\n7\n00:00:21.061 --> 00:00:26.401\nWords like opbellen, meenemen, and afwassen.\n\n8\n00:00:26.461 --> 00:00:30.881\nIn main sentences, prefix splits off!\n\n9\n00:00:30.961 --> 00:00:33.681\nIt goes to the very end.\n\n10\n00:00:33.721 --> 00:00:37.361\nThink of English: I turn it on.\n\n11\n00:00:37.381 --> 00:00:40.421\nThe word on moves to end.\n\n12\n00:00:40.461 --> 00:00:43.301\nDutch does this with action verbs.\n\n13\n00:00:43.341 --> 00:00:45.702\nLet's look at our first verb.\n\n14\n00:00:45.742 --> 00:00:49.642\nThe verb is opbellen, to call.\n\n15\n00:00:49.722 --> 00:00:52.022\nI call your mother.\n\n16\n00:00:52.142 --> 00:00:54.122\nI call your mother.\n\n17\n00:00:54.162 --> 00:00:57.162\nNotice how op went to end!\n\n18\n00:00:57.202 --> 00:01:00.082\nBel stays in position two.\n\n19\n00:01:00.182 --> 00:01:02.562\nLet me show you another sentence.\n\n20\n00:01:02.602 --> 00:01:04.922\nHe calls his friend.\n\n21\n00:01:04.942 --> 00:01:09.082\nHe calls his friend.\n\n22\n00:01:09.122 --> 00:01:13.162\nNow let's look at meenemen.\n\n23\n00:01:13.202 --> 00:01:17.903\nMeenemen means to take along.\n\n24\n00:01:18.003 --> 00:01:21.783\nI take an apple along.\n\n25\n00:01:21.963 --> 00:01:26.343\nI take an apple along.\n\n26\n00:01:26.383 --> 00:01:29.703\nLet's make it a bit longer.\n\n27\n00:01:29.763 --> 00:01:33.743\nWe take the dog along.\n\n28\n00:01:33.783 --> 00:01:37.843\nWe take the dog along.\n\n29\n00:01:37.883 --> 00:01:41.223\nCan you guess the next sentence?\n\n30\n00:01:41.283 --> 00:01:45.344\nHow do you say: She takes tea?\n\n31\n00:01:45.384 --> 00:01:49.284\nThink where mee should go!\n\n32\n00:01:49.344 --> 00:01:52.564\nHere is the correct sentence.\n\n33\n00:01:52.604 --> 00:01:57.024\nShe takes warm tea along.\n\n34\n00:01:57.104 --> 00:02:01.524\nShe takes warm tea along.\n\n35\n00:02:01.564 --> 00:02:03.824\nGreat job!\n\n36\n00:02:03.844 --> 00:02:07.544\nNow, let's look at afwassen.\n\n37\n00:02:07.604 --> 00:02:11.924\nAfwassen means to wash dishes.\n\n38\n00:02:11.984 --> 00:02:16.005\nI wash the plates.\n\n39\n00:02:16.185 --> 00:02:18.905\nI wash the plates.\n\n40\n00:02:18.965 --> 00:02:21.965\nHow would you say: You wash?\n\n41\n00:02:22.025 --> 00:02:25.445\nHow do you say: You wash cups?\n\n42\n00:02:25.565 --> 00:02:27.505\nLet's see if you got it!\n\n43\n00:02:27.565 --> 00:02:32.245\nYou wash the cups.\n\n44\n00:02:32.305 --> 00:02:34.445\nYou wash the cups.\n\n45\n00:02:34.485 --> 00:02:37.085\nTime for a quick pattern drill!\n\n46\n00:02:37.105 --> 00:02:38.805\nRepeat after me.\n\n47\n00:02:38.865 --> 00:02:43.425\nHe washes the pans.\n\n48\n00:02:43.505 --> 00:02:45.826\nHe washes the pans.\n\n49\n00:02:45.866 --> 00:02:50.526\nWe wash the glass.\n\n50\n00:02:50.586 --> 00:02:52.926\nWe wash the glass.\n\n51\n00:02:52.986 --> 00:02:57.566\nThey call the doctor.\n\n52\n00:02:57.606 --> 00:02:59.606\nThey call the doctor.\n\n53\n00:02:59.666 --> 00:03:04.146\nJan takes the money along.\n\n54\n00:03:04.206 --> 00:03:06.506\nJan takes the money along.\n\n55\n00:03:06.546 --> 00:03:11.066\nMaria takes a book along.\n\n56\n00:03:11.086 --> 00:03:13.427\nMaria takes a book along.\n\n57\n00:03:13.467 --> 00:03:16.727\nWelcome to our Error Clinic!\n\n58\n00:03:16.747 --> 00:03:20.707\nBeginners often make these mistakes.\n\n59\n00:03:20.727 --> 00:03:23.667\nMistake number one:\n\n60\n00:03:23.707 --> 00:03:28.827\nDon't say: Ik opbel mijn vader.\n\n61\n00:03:28.867 --> 00:03:31.067\nWhy is this wrong?\n\n62\n00:03:31.107 --> 00:03:34.507\nDo not keep the verb together!\n\n63\n00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:37.027\nThe correct version is:\n\n64\n00:03:37.087 --> 00:03:41.427\nI call my father.\n\n65\n00:03:41.547 --> 00:03:43.768\nI call my father.\n\n66\n00:03:43.808 --> 00:03:46.168\nMistake number two:\n\n67\n00:03:46.228 --> 00:03:51.388\nDon't say: Hij neemt mee brood.\n\n68\n00:03:51.428 --> 00:03:53.508\nWhat went wrong here?\n\n69\n00:03:53.548 --> 00:03:57.068\nThe prefix must go to end!\n\n70\n00:03:57.088 --> 00:03:59.548\nThe correct version is:\n\n71\n00:03:59.628 --> 00:04:04.208\nHe takes the bread along.\n\n72\n00:04:04.248 --> 00:04:06.668\nHe takes the bread along.\n\n73\n00:04:06.688 --> 00:04:09.148\nMistake number three:\n\n74\n00:04:09.188 --> 00:04:13.789\nDon't say: Wij afwassen de borden.\n\n75\n00:04:13.889 --> 00:04:16.969\nRemember to split the verb!\n\n76\n00:04:17.009 --> 00:04:19.289\nThe correct version is:\n\n77\n00:04:19.449 --> 00:04:23.909\nWe wash the dishes.\n\n78\n00:04:23.929 --> 00:04:26.389\nWe wash the dishes.\n\n79\n00:04:26.449 --> 00:04:29.049\nHere is your memory anchor:\n\n80\n00:04:29.109 --> 00:04:33.789\nVerb in position two, prefix end!\n\n81\n00:04:33.829 --> 00:04:37.769\nTime for our final recap.\n\n82\n00:04:37.829 --> 00:04:43.750\nToday we learned separable verbs.\n\n83\n00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:48.330\nToday we learned separable verbs.\n\n84\n00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:51.790\nKeep splitting those verbs!\n\n85\n00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:55.270\nUntil next time!\n\n86\n00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:56.530\nUntil next time!\n
grammar_want_omdat	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:03.740\nImagine you are late for work.\n\n2\n00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:07.461\nYou must explain why.\n\n3\n00:00:07.521 --> 00:00:11.221\nYou need the word 'because'.\n\n4\n00:00:11.261 --> 00:00:14.901\nIn Dutch, we have two words.\n\n5\n00:00:14.921 --> 00:00:20.461\nThey are: want and omdat.\n\n6\n00:00:20.482 --> 00:00:24.042\nThey both mean because.\n\n7\n00:00:24.062 --> 00:00:26.482\nBut they change the word order.\n\n8\n00:00:26.682 --> 00:00:29.202\nLaten we beginnen!\n\n9\n00:00:29.342 --> 00:00:31.102\nLet us begin!\n\n10\n00:00:31.162 --> 00:00:35.123\nFirst, we look at want.\n\n11\n00:00:35.163 --> 00:00:38.603\nWant keeps the normal order.\n\n12\n00:00:38.683 --> 00:00:41.443\nLet us see an example.\n\n13\n00:00:41.503 --> 00:00:46.763\nIk eet want ik heb honger.\n\n14\n00:00:46.883 --> 00:00:50.864\nI eat because I am hungry.\n\n15\n00:00:50.904 --> 00:00:55.464\nNotice the verb heb is second.\n\n16\n00:00:55.504 --> 00:00:59.664\nNow, let's look at omdat.\n\n17\n00:00:59.724 --> 00:01:03.985\nOmdat sends the verb to the end.\n\n18\n00:01:04.005 --> 00:01:06.985\nLet us see the same sentence.\n\n19\n00:01:07.065 --> 00:01:12.125\nIk eet omdat ik honger heb.\n\n20\n00:01:12.225 --> 00:01:15.266\nI eat because I am hungry.\n\n21\n00:01:15.306 --> 00:01:17.846\nDid you hear the verb heb?\n\n22\n00:01:17.926 --> 00:01:20.486\nIt is at the very end!\n\n23\n00:01:20.566 --> 00:01:23.666\nLet us practice with another sentence.\n\n24\n00:01:23.706 --> 00:01:27.026\nWe want to say: He drinks.\n\n25\n00:01:27.046 --> 00:01:29.807\nBecause he is thirsty.\n\n26\n00:01:29.867 --> 00:01:33.027\nWith want, it is normal.\n\n27\n00:01:33.127 --> 00:01:38.007\nHij drinkt want hij heeft dorst.\n\n28\n00:01:38.047 --> 00:01:41.447\nHe drinks because he is thirsty.\n\n29\n00:01:41.527 --> 00:01:44.488\nNow, let's use omdat.\n\n30\n00:01:44.588 --> 00:01:46.588\nWhere does the verb go?\n\n31\n00:01:46.688 --> 00:01:49.588\nYes, to the very end!\n\n32\n00:01:49.668 --> 00:01:54.108\nHij drinkt omdat hij dorst heeft.\n\n33\n00:01:54.148 --> 00:01:57.489\nHe drinks because he is thirsty.\n\n34\n00:01:57.569 --> 00:01:59.849\nLet's try another one.\n\n35\n00:01:59.889 --> 00:02:03.269\nWe want to say: She sleeps.\n\n36\n00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:05.929\nBecause she is tired.\n\n37\n00:02:05.969 --> 00:02:07.949\nWith want:\n\n38\n00:02:08.029 --> 00:02:12.670\nZij slaapt want zij is moe.\n\n39\n00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:16.310\nShe sleeps because she is tired.\n\n40\n00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:19.330\nNow with omdat:\n\n41\n00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:23.551\nZij slaapt omdat zij moe is.\n\n42\n00:02:23.591 --> 00:02:27.651\nShe sleeps because she is tired.\n\n43\n00:02:27.671 --> 00:02:30.711\nCan you guess the next one?\n\n44\n00:02:30.771 --> 00:02:32.311\nHow do we say:\n\n45\n00:02:32.371 --> 00:02:36.571\nWe stay home because it is cold.\n\n46\n00:02:36.671 --> 00:02:39.192\nUsing want:\n\n47\n00:02:39.232 --> 00:02:44.232\nWe blijven thuis want het is koud.\n\n48\n00:02:44.252 --> 00:02:48.312\nWe stay home because it is cold.\n\n49\n00:02:48.352 --> 00:02:52.473\nNow, how about with omdat?\n\n50\n00:02:52.513 --> 00:02:56.213\nThink about the verb is.\n\n51\n00:02:56.233 --> 00:03:01.453\nWe blijven thuis omdat het koud is.\n\n52\n00:03:01.533 --> 00:03:05.774\nWe stay home because it is cold.\n\n53\n00:03:05.814 --> 00:03:08.334\nLet us look at some errors.\n\n54\n00:03:08.374 --> 00:03:10.834\nBeginners often say:\n\n55\n00:03:10.914 --> 00:03:15.254\nIk ben thuis omdat ik ben ziek.\n\n56\n00:03:15.354 --> 00:03:18.875\nI am home because I am sick.\n\n57\n00:03:18.895 --> 00:03:20.855\nThis is wrong!\n\n58\n00:03:20.935 --> 00:03:25.175\nOmdat must send ben to the end.\n\n59\n00:03:25.215 --> 00:03:27.195\nThe correct sentence is:\n\n60\n00:03:27.255 --> 00:03:31.455\nIk ben thuis omdat ik ziek ben.\n\n61\n00:03:31.616 --> 00:03:34.996\nI am home because I am sick.\n\n62\n00:03:35.056 --> 00:03:37.176\nAnother common mistake:\n\n63\n00:03:37.216 --> 00:03:40.976\nUsing want with verb at the end.\n\n64\n00:03:41.056 --> 00:03:44.296\nIk eet want ik honger heb.\n\n65\n00:03:44.416 --> 00:03:47.377\nI eat because I am hungry.\n\n66\n00:03:47.397 --> 00:03:49.737\nThis is also incorrect.\n\n67\n00:03:49.917 --> 00:03:52.857\nWant needs the normal order.\n\n68\n00:03:52.917 --> 00:03:54.177\nSo we say:\n\n69\n00:03:54.237 --> 00:03:57.517\nIk eet want ik heb honger.\n\n70\n00:03:57.617 --> 00:04:00.618\nI eat because I am hungry.\n\n71\n00:04:00.738 --> 00:04:03.078\nRemember this simple rule:\n\n72\n00:04:03.138 --> 00:04:05.458\nWant is normal.\n\n73\n00:04:05.518 --> 00:04:08.578\nOmdat kicks the verb away.\n\n74\n00:04:08.678 --> 00:04:10.958\nLet us do a quick recap.\n\n75\n00:04:10.998 --> 00:04:12.779\nToday we learned:\n\n76\n00:04:12.839 --> 00:04:17.159\nVandaag leerden we want en omdat.\n\n77\n00:04:17.199 --> 00:04:20.979\nToday we learned want and omdat.\n\n78\n00:04:20.999 --> 00:04:24.419\nUse want for normal order.\n\n79\n00:04:24.599 --> 00:04:28.700\nUse omdat for verb at the end.\n\n80\n00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:31.520\nTot de volgende keer!\n\n81\n00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:32.940\nUntil next time!\n
