0\nRemember: TUNNEL = tunnel.\n\n33\n00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:21.651\nOur fifth word is KRUISPUNT.\n\n34\n00:02:21.691 --> 00:02:27.991\nKruispunt means intersection in English.\n\n35\n00:02:28.031 --> 00:02:32.392\nThis is an intersection.\n\n36\n00:02:32.472 --> 00:02:36.452\nThis is an intersection.\n\n37\n00:02:36.532 --> 00:02:40.852\nStop at the intersection.\n\n38\n00:02:40.912 --> 00:02:43.293\nStop at the intersection.\n\n39\n00:02:43.333 --> 00:02:48.393\nRemember: KRUISPUNT = intersection.\n\n40\n00:02:48.453 --> 00:02:52.713\nOur sixth word is STOPLICHT.\n\n41\n00:02:52.793 --> 00:02:56.414\nStoplicht means traffic light in English.\n\n42\n00:02:56.454 --> 00:03:02.214\nThe traffic light is red.\n\n43\n00:03:02.234 --> 00:03:04.974\nThe traffic light is red.\n\n44\n00:03:05.014 --> 00:03:10.555\nThe traffic light is green.\n\n45\n00:03:10.595 --> 00:03:13.315\nThe traffic light is green.\n\n46\n00:03:13.355 --> 00:03:18.355\nRemember: STOPLICHT = traffic light.\n\n47\n00:03:18.435 --> 00:03:23.136\nOur final word is OVERSTEKEN.\n\n48\n00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:27.156\nOversteken means to cross in English.\n\n49\n00:03:27.196 --> 00:03:32.476\nWe cross over.\n\n50\n00:03:32.516 --> 00:03:34.436\nWe cross over.\n\n51\n00:03:34.516 --> 00:03:40.677\nCrossing safely is important.\n\n52\n00:03:40.717 --> 00:03:44.077\nCrossing safely is important.\n\n53\n00:03:44.117 --> 00:03:46.557\nLet's recap today's words.\n\n54\n00:03:46.637 --> 00:03:50.998\none. STRAAT = street.\n\n55\n00:03:51.038 --> 00:03:55.338\ntwo. PLEIN = square.\n\n56\n00:03:55.398 --> 00:03:59.598\nthree. BRUG = bridge.\n\n57\n00:03:59.658 --> 00:04:03.659\nfour. TUNNEL = tunnel.\n\n58\n00:04:03.699 --> 00:04:08.639\nfive. KRUISPUNT = intersection.\n\n59\n00:04:08.679 --> 00:04:13.479\nsix. STOPLICHT = traffic light.\n\n60\n00:04:13.539 --> 00:04:18.560\nseven. OVERSTEKEN = to cross.\n\n61\n00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:19.600\nGreat work today!\n
vocab_clothing_shopping	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:05.500\nWelcome to today's Dutch vocabulary lesson!\n\n2\n00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:10.201\nToday we learn words about clothing shopping.\n\n3\n00:00:10.241 --> 00:00:12.361\nLaten we beginnen!\n\n4\n00:00:12.421 --> 00:00:16.242\nShopping for clothes is fun and useful.\n\n5\n00:00:16.302 --> 00:00:19.542\nOur first word is MAAT.\n\n6\n00:00:19.582 --> 00:00:23.242\nMaat means size in English.\n\n7\n00:00:23.282 --> 00:00:25.983\nWelke maat zoekt u?\n\n8\n00:00:26.023 --> 00:00:28.723\nWhich size are you looking for?\n\n9\n00:00:28.783 --> 00:00:31.583\nIk zoek een kleine maat.\n\n10\n00:00:31.703 --> 00:00:34.423\nI am looking for a small size.\n\n11\n00:00:34.503 --> 00:00:37.684\nOur second word is PASSEN.\n\n12\n00:00:37.744 --> 00:00:41.584\nPassen means to try on in English.\n\n13\n00:00:41.624 --> 00:00:44.744\nMag ik deze broek passen?\n\n14\n00:00:44.764 --> 00:00:47.505\nMay I try on these trousers?\n\n15\n00:00:47.645 --> 00:00:50.125\nU kunt hier passen.\n\n16\n00:00:50.185 --> 00:00:52.485\nYou can try on here.\n\n17\n00:00:52.565 --> 00:00:55.445\nOur third word is KASSA.\n\n18\n00:00:55.485 --> 00:01:00.006\nKassa means cash register in English.\n\n19\n00:01:00.066 --> 00:01:03.026\nWaar is de kassa?\n\n20\n00:01:03.066 --> 00:01:05.747\nWhere is the cash register?\n\n21\n00:01:05.787 --> 00:01:09.147\nDe kassa is daar.\n\n22\n00:01:09.187 --> 00:01:11.867\nThe cash register is over there.\n\n23\n00:01:11.947 --> 00:01:16.048\nOur fourth word is KORTINGSBON.\n\n24\n00:01:16.088 --> 00:01:20.608\nKortingsbon means discount coupon in English.\n\n25\n00:01:20.668 --> 00:01:24.108\nIk heb een kortingsbon.\n\n26\n00:01:24.348 --> 00:01:27.189\nI have a discount coupon.\n\n27\n00:01:27.289 --> 00:01:31.529\nGebruik de kortingsbon hier.\n\n28\n00:01:31.729 --> 00:01:34.949\nUse the discount coupon here.\n\n29\n00:01:35.009 --> 00:01:38.690\nOur fifth word is RUILEN.\n\n30\n00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:42.850\nRuilen means to exchange in English.\n\n31\n00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:47.131\nKan ik dit shirt ruilen?\n\n32\n00:01:47.151 --> 00:01:49.631\nCan I exchange this shirt?\n\n33\n00:01:49.771 --> 00:01:53.991\nU kunt dit shirt ruilen.\n\n34\n00:01:54.051 --> 00:01:56.932\nYou can exchange this shirt.\n\n35\n00:01:57.032 --> 00:02:01.652\nOur sixth phrase is TE GROOT.\n\n36\n00:02:01.692 --> 00:02:06.193\nTe groot means too big in English.\n\n37\n00:02:06.253 --> 00:02:09.593\nDeze jas is te groot.\n\n38\n00:02:09.633 --> 00:02:12.293\nThis jacket is too big.\n\n39\n00:02:12.333 --> 00:02:15.434\nHet hemd is te groot.\n\n40\n00:02:15.454 --> 00:02:17.954\nThe shirt is too big.\n\n41\n00:02:18.034 --> 00:02:22.154\nOur seventh phrase is TE KLEIN.\n\n42\n00:02:22.194 --> 00:02:26.755\nTe klein means too small in English.\n\n43\n00:02:26.815 --> 00:02:30.255\nDeze schoenen zijn te klein.\n\n44\n00:02:30.295 --> 00:02:33.115\nThese shoes are too small.\n\n45\n00:02:33.135 --> 00:02:36.056\nDe broek is te klein.\n\n46\n00:02:36.076 --> 00:02:38.776\nThe trousers are too small.\n\n47\n00:02:38.876 --> 00:02:41.496\nLet's recap today's words.\n\n48\n00:02:41.596 --> 00:02:46.437\néén. MAAT = size.\n\n49\n00:02:46.477 --> 00:02:51.877\ntwee. PASSEN = to try on.\n\n50\n00:02:51.937 --> 00:02:57.198\ndrie. KASSA = cash register.\n\n51\n00:02:57.278 --> 00:03:03.198\nvier. KORTINGSBON = discount coupon.\n\n52\n00:03:03.258 --> 00:03:08.619\nvijf. RUILEN = to exchange.\n\n53\n00:03:08.739 --> 00:03:13.479\nzes. TE GROOT = too big.\n\n54\n00:03:13.519 --> 00:03:18.200\nzeven. TE KLEIN = too small.\n\n55\n00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:19.200\nGreat work today!\n
