vocab_cooking	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:05.540\nWelcome to today's Dutch vocabulary lesson!\n\n2\n00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:09.141\nToday we learn words about cooking.\n\n3\n00:00:09.161 --> 00:00:12.401\nCooking in the kitchen is fun!\n\n4\n00:00:12.561 --> 00:00:15.161\nLet's begin with our lesson.\n\n5\n00:00:15.241 --> 00:00:17.821\nLaten we beginnen!\n\n6\n00:00:17.961 --> 00:00:19.621\nLet's start!\n\n7\n00:00:19.701 --> 00:00:23.502\nOur first word is KOKEN.\n\n8\n00:00:23.542 --> 00:00:26.442\nKoken means to cook.\n\n9\n00:00:26.522 --> 00:00:29.902\nIk ga vandaag koken.\n\n10\n00:00:30.122 --> 00:00:33.182\nI am going to cook today.\n\n11\n00:00:33.222 --> 00:00:37.443\nWij koken in de keuken.\n\n12\n00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:40.023\nWe cook in the kitchen.\n\n13\n00:00:40.183 --> 00:00:43.883\nOur second word is BAKKEN.\n\n14\n00:00:43.923 --> 00:00:47.523\nBakken means to bake or fry.\n\n15\n00:00:47.583 --> 00:00:51.504\nIk bak een lekker brood.\n\n16\n00:00:51.664 --> 00:00:54.684\nI bake a delicious bread.\n\n17\n00:00:54.744 --> 00:00:58.044\nHij bakt een eitje.\n\n18\n00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:00.484\nHe fries an egg.\n\n19\n00:01:00.504 --> 00:01:04.084\nNext, we have SNIJDEN.\n\n20\n00:01:04.184 --> 00:01:07.545\nSnijden means to cut.\n\n21\n00:01:07.605 --> 00:01:10.865\nIk snijd de groenten.\n\n22\n00:01:11.005 --> 00:01:13.945\nI cut the vegetables.\n\n23\n00:01:14.025 --> 00:01:17.905\nZij snijdt het verse brood.\n\n24\n00:01:17.945 --> 00:01:21.286\nShe cuts the fresh bread.\n\n25\n00:01:21.306 --> 00:01:24.726\nNow let's learn kitchen tools.\n\n26\n00:01:24.786 --> 00:01:28.626\nOur fourth word is PAN.\n\n27\n00:01:28.666 --> 00:01:32.006\nPan means pan.\n\n28\n00:01:32.066 --> 00:01:36.047\nDe pan staat op het vuur.\n\n29\n00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:39.367\nThe pan is on the stove.\n\n30\n00:01:39.427 --> 00:01:42.627\nSoep zit in de pan.\n\n31\n00:01:42.707 --> 00:01:46.287\nSoup is in the pan.\n\n32\n00:01:46.307 --> 00:01:50.328\nThe fifth word is POT.\n\n33\n00:01:50.348 --> 00:01:54.668\nPot means pot or jar.\n\n34\n00:01:54.728 --> 00:01:58.348\nDe pot is erg groot.\n\n35\n00:01:58.368 --> 00:02:01.729\nThe pot is very big.\n\n36\n00:02:01.809 --> 00:02:05.649\nEr zit suiker in de pot.\n\n37\n00:02:05.749 --> 00:02:10.269\nThere is sugar in the pot.\n\n38\n00:02:10.349 --> 00:02:13.929\nOur sixth word is MES.\n\n39\n00:02:13.969 --> 00:02:16.930\nMes means knife.\n\n40\n00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:20.910\nHet mes is heel scherp.\n\n41\n00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:24.050\nThe knife is very sharp.\n\n42\n00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:28.130\nIk gebruik een scherp mes.\n\n43\n00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:31.411\nI use a sharp knife.\n\n44\n00:02:31.431 --> 00:02:35.151\nThe seventh word is BORD.\n\n45\n00:02:35.191 --> 00:02:38.251\nBord means plate.\n\n46\n00:02:38.311 --> 00:02:42.571\nHet eten staat op het bord.\n\n47\n00:02:42.591 --> 00:02:45.932\nThe food is on the plate.\n\n48\n00:02:45.992 --> 00:02:49.132\nDit bord is schoon.\n\n49\n00:02:49.152 --> 00:02:52.052\nThis plate is clean.\n\n50\n00:02:52.112 --> 00:02:55.532\nNext is the word VORK.\n\n51\n00:02:55.632 --> 00:02:58.613\nVork means fork.\n\n52\n00:02:58.673 --> 00:03:01.973\nIk eet met een vork.\n\n53\n00:03:02.153 --> 00:03:05.293\nI eat with a fork.\n\n54\n00:03:05.333 --> 00:03:08.833\nDe vork liegt op tafel.\n\n55\n00:03:08.873 --> 00:03:12.114\nThe fork lies on the table.\n\n56\n00:03:12.174 --> 00:03:15.714\nThe ninth word is LEPEL.\n\n57\n00:03:15.774 --> 00:03:18.694\nLepel means spoon.\n\n58\n00:03:18.754 --> 00:03:22.274\nIk gebruik een kleine lepel.\n\n59\n00:03:22.454 --> 00:03:25.094\nI use a small spoon.\n\n60\n00:03:25.134 --> 00:03:28.475\nDe soep vraagt om een lepel.\n\n61\n00:03:28.515 --> 00:03:31.095\nThe soup needs a spoon.\n\n62\n00:03:31.175 --> 00:03:34.595\nOur last word is RECEPT.\n\n63\n00:03:34.675 --> 00:03:37.755\nRecept means recipe.\n\n64\n00:03:37.815 --> 00:03:40.996\nIk lees een goed recept.\n\n65\n00:03:41.016 --> 00:03:42.196\nI read a good recipe.\n\n66\n00:03:42.216 --> 00:03:44.516\nDit recept is heel makkelijk.\n\n67\n00:03:44.556 --> 00:03:47.376\nThis recipe is very easy.\n\n68\n00:03:47.456 --> 00:03:49.916\nLet's recap today's words.\n\n69\n00:03:50.016 --> 00:03:53.456\néén. KOKEN = to cook.\n\n70\n00:03:53.496 --> 00:03:57.237\ntwee. BAKKEN = to bake.\n\n71\n00:03:57.257 --> 00:04:00.957\ndrie. SNIJDEN = to cut.\n\n72\n00:04:01.017 --> 00:04:04.457\nvier. PAN = pan.\n\n73\n00:04:04.497 --> 00:04:07.937\nvijf. POT = pot.\n\n74\n00:04:07.997 --> 00:04:13.678\nzes. MES = knife.\n\n75\n00:04:13.738 --> 00:04:19.698\nzeven. BORD = plate.\n\n76\n00:04:19.798 --> 00:04:26.039\nacht. VORK = fork.\n\n77\n00:04:26.079 --> 00:04:32.659\nnegen. LEPEL = spoon.\n\n78\n00:04:32.699 --> 00:04:39.140\ntien. RECEPT = recipe.\n\n79\n00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:42.240\nGreat work learning Dutch cooking words!\n\n80\n00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:43.380\nSee you next time!\n
vocab_cooking	en	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:05.540\nWelcome to today's Dutch vocabulary lesson!\n\n2\n00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:09.141\nToday we learn words about cooking.\n\n3\n00:00:09.161 --> 00:00:12.401\nCooking in the kitchen is fun!\n\n4\n00:00:12.561 --> 00:00:15.161\nLet's begin with our lesson.\n\n5\n00:00:15.241 --> 00:00:17.821\nLet's start!\n\n6\n00:00:17.961 --> 00:00:19.621\nLet's start!\n\n7\n00:00:19.701 --> 00:00:23.502\nOur first word is KOKEN.\n\n8\n00:00:23.542 --> 00:00:26.442\nKoken means to cook.\n\n9\n00:00:26.522 --> 00:00:29.902\nI am going to cook today.\n\n10\n00:00:30.122 --> 00:00:33.182\nI am going to cook today.\n\n11\n00:00:33.222 --> 00:00:37.443\nWe cook in the kitchen.\n\n12\n00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:40.023\nWe cook in the kitchen.\n\n13\n00:00:40.183 --> 00:00:43.883\nOur second word is BAKKEN.\n\n14\n00:00:43.923 --> 00:00:47.523\nBakken means to bake or fry.\n\n15\n00:00:47.583 --> 00:00:51.504\nI bake a delicious bread.\n\n16\n00:00:51.664 --> 00:00:54.684\nI bake a delicious bread.\n\n17\n00:00:54.744 --> 00:00:58.044\nHe fries an egg.\n\n18\n00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:00.484\nHe fries an egg.\n\n19\n00:01:00.504 --> 00:01:04.084\nNext, we have SNIJDEN.\n\n20\n00:01:04.184 --> 00:01:07.545\nSnijden means to cut.\n\n21\n00:01:07.605 --> 00:01:10.865\nI cut the vegetables.\n\n22\n00:01:11.005 --> 00:01:13.945\nI cut the vegetables.\n\n23\n00:01:14.025 --> 00:01:17.905\nShe cuts the fresh bread.\n\n24\n00:01:17.945 --> 00:01:21.286\nShe cuts the fresh bread.\n\n25\n00:01:21.306 --> 00:01:24.726\nNow let's learn kitchen tools.\n\n26\n00:01:24.786 --> 00:01:28.626\nOur fourth word is PAN.\n\n27\n00:01:28.666 --> 00:01:32.006\nPan means pan.\n\n28\n00:01:32.066 --> 00:01:36.047\nThe pan is on the stove.\n\n29\n00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:39.367\nThe pan is on the stove.\n\n30\n00:01:39.427 --> 00:01:42.627\nSoup is in the pan.\n\n31\n00:01:42.707 --> 00:01:46.287\nSoup is in the pan.\n\n32\n00:01:46.307 --> 00:01:50.328\nThe fifth word is POT.\n\n33\n00:01:50.348 --> 00:01:54.668\nPot means pot or jar.\n\n34\n00:01:54.728 --> 00:01:58.348\nThe pot is very big.\n\n35\n00:01:58.368 --> 00:02:01.729\nThe pot is very big.\n\n36\n00:02:01.809 --> 00:02:05.649\nThere is sugar in the pot.\n\n37\n00:02:05.749 --> 00:02:10.269\nThere is sugar in the pot.\n\n38\n00:02:10.349 --> 00:02:13.929\nOur sixth word is MES.\n\n39\n00:02:13.969 --> 00:02:16.930\nMes means knife.\n\n40\n00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:20.910\nThe knife is very sharp.\n\n41\n00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:24.050\nThe knife is very sharp.\n\n42\n00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:28.130\nI use a sharp knife.\n\n43\n00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:31.411\nI use a sharp knife.\n\n44\n00:02:31.431 --> 00:02:35.151\nThe seventh word is BORD.\n\n45\n00:02:35.191 --> 00:02:38.251\nBord means plate.\n\n46\n00:02:38.311 --> 00:02:42.571\nThe food is on the plate.\n\n47\n00:02:42.591 --> 00:02:45.932\nThe food is on the plate.\n\n48\n00:02:45.992 --> 00:02:49.132\nThis plate is clean.\n\n49\n00:02:49.152 --> 00:02:52.052\nThis plate is clean.\n\n50\n00:02:52.112 --> 00:02:55.532\nNext is the word VORK.\n\n51\n00:02:55.632 --> 00:02:58.613\nVork means fork.\n\n52\n00:02:58.673 --> 00:03:01.973\nI eat with a fork.\n\n53\n00:03:02.153 --> 00:03:05.293\nI eat with a fork.\n\n54\n00:03:05.333 --> 00:03:08.833\nThe fork lies on the table.\n\n55\n00:03:08.873 --> 00:03:12.114\nThe fork lies on the table.\n\n56\n00:03:12.174 --> 00:03:15.714\nThe ninth word is LEPEL.\n\n57\n00:03:15.774 --> 00:03:18.694\nLepel means spoon.\n\n58\n00:03:18.754 --> 00:03:22.274\nI use a small spoon.\n\n59\n00:03:22.454 --> 00:03:25.094\nI use a small spoon.\n\n60\n00:03:25.134 --> 00:03:28.475\nThe soup needs a spoon.\n\n61\n00:03:28.515 --> 00:03:31.095\nThe soup needs a spoon.\n\n62\n00:03:31.175 --> 00:03:34.595\nOur last word is RECEPT.\n\n63\n00:03:34.675 --> 00:03:37.755\nRecept means recipe.\n\n64\n00:03:37.815 --> 00:03:40.996\nI read a good recipe.\n\n65\n00:03:41.016 --> 00:03:42.196\nI read a good recipe.\n\n66\n00:03:42.216 --> 00:03:44.516\nThis recipe is very easy.\n\n67\n00:03:44.556 --> 00:03:47.376\nThis recipe is very easy.\n\n68\n00:03:47.456 --> 00:03:49.916\nLet's recap today's words.\n\n69\n00:03:50.016 --> 00:03:53.456\none. KOKEN = to cook.\n\n70\n00:03:53.496 --> 00:03:57.237\ntwo. BAKKEN = to bake.\n\n71\n00:03:57.257 --> 00:04:00.957\nthree. SNIJDEN = to cut.\n\n72\n00:04:01.017 --> 00:04:04.457\nfour. PAN = pan.\n\n73\n00:04:04.497 --> 00:04:07.937\nfive. POT = pot.\n\n74\n00:04:07.997 --> 00:04:13.678\nsix. MES = knife.\n\n75\n00:04:13.738 --> 00:04:19.698\nseven. BORD = plate.\n\n76\n00:04:19.798 --> 00:04:26.039\neight. VORK = fork.\n\n77\n00:04:26.079 --> 00:04:32.659\nnine. LEPEL = spoon.\n\n78\n00:04:32.699 --> 00:04:39.140\nten. RECEPT = recipe.\n\n79\n00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:42.240\nGreat work learning Dutch cooking words!\n\n80\n00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:43.380\nSee you next time!\n
vocab_digital_daily	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:03.460\nHello everyone!\n\n2\n00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.360\nWelcome to Dutch class!\n\n3\n00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.941\nToday we learn digital words.\n\n4\n00:00:10.001 --> 00:00:11.821\nAre you ready?\n\n5\n00:00:11.881 --> 00:00:14.361\nLaten we beginnen!\n\n6\n00:00:14.461 --> 00:00:16.601\nLet's begin!\n\n7\n00:00:16.661 --> 00:00:20.841\nWord number one is TELEFOON.\n\n8\n00:00:20.861 --> 00:00:25.042\nTelefoon means phone in English.\n\n9\n00:00:25.102 --> 00:00:27.762\nLet's hear an example.\n\n10\n00:00:27.862 --> 00:00:31.442\nIk gebruik mijn telefoon.\n\n11\n00:00:31.602 --> 00:00:34.342\nI use my phone.\n\n12\n00:00:34.362 --> 00:00:37.982\nMijn telefoon is nieuw.\n\n13\n00:00:38.022 --> 00:00:40.523\nMy phone is new.\n\n14\n00:00:40.563 --> 00:00:44.643\nWord number two is INTERNET.\n\n15\n00:00:44.723 --> 00:00:48.703\nInternet means internet in English.\n\n16\n00:00:48.763 --> 00:00:51.763\nHere is the first sentence.\n\n17\n00:00:51.823 --> 00:00:55.904\nHet internet is erg snel.\n\n18\n00:00:55.924 --> 00:00:59.544\nThe internet is very fast.\n\n19\n00:00:59.604 --> 00:01:02.824\nIk zit op het internet.\n\n20\n00:01:02.964 --> 00:01:05.464\nI am on the internet.\n\n21\n00:01:05.504 --> 00:01:08.304\nWord number three is APP.\n\n22\n00:01:08.504 --> 00:01:11.865\nApp means app in English.\n\n23\n00:01:11.965 --> 00:01:14.625\nLet's see a sentence.\n\n24\n00:01:14.705 --> 00:01:19.485\nIk open een nieuwe app.\n\n25\n00:01:19.605 --> 00:01:23.105\nI open a new app.\n\n26\n00:01:23.145 --> 00:01:27.266\nDeze app is erg handig.\n\n27\n00:01:27.326 --> 00:01:31.246\nThis app is very useful.\n\n28\n00:01:31.306 --> 00:01:35.506\nWord number four is BERICHT.\n\n29\n00:01:35.546 --> 00:01:40.486\nBericht means message in English.\n\n30\n00:01:40.606 --> 00:01:43.527\nListen to this sentence.\n\n31\n00:01:43.607 --> 00:01:48.367\nIk stuur een kort bericht.\n\n32\n00:01:48.467 --> 00:01:52.347\nI send a short message.\n\n33\n00:01:52.407 --> 00:01:56.967\nHij leest het bericht nu.\n\n34\n00:01:57.007 --> 00:02:00.788\nHe reads the message now.\n\n35\n00:02:00.848 --> 00:02:05.148\nWord number five is E-MAIL.\n\n36\n00:02:05.248 --> 00:02:10.128\nE-mail means email in English.\n\n37\n00:02:10.168 --> 00:02:12.988\nHere is an example.\n\n38\n00:02:13.088 --> 00:02:17.269\nIk schrijf een e-mail.\n\n39\n00:02:17.389 --> 00:02:19.509\nI write an email.\n\n40\n00:02:19.529 --> 00:02:24.329\nDe e-mail is erg belangrijk.\n\n41\n00:02:24.369 --> 00:02:28.849\nThe email is very important.\n\n42\n00:02:28.869 --> 00:02:34.310\nWord number six is OPLADEN.\n\n43\n00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:38.910\nOpladen means to charge.\n\n44\n00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:42.150\nLet's practice a sentence.\n\n45\n00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:46.951\nIk moet mijn telefoon opladen.\n\n46\n00:02:47.091 --> 00:02:50.811\nI must charge my phone.\n\n47\n00:02:50.851 --> 00:02:55.471\nDe batterij laadt nu op.\n\n48\n00:02:55.511 --> 00:02:59.571\nThe battery charges now.\n\n49\n00:02:59.611 --> 00:03:04.412\nWord number seven is WIFI.\n\n50\n00:03:04.472 --> 00:03:09.512\nWifi means wifi in English.\n\n51\n00:03:09.572 --> 00:03:12.452\nListen carefully now.\n\n52\n00:03:12.532 --> 00:03:17.013\nIs er hier snelle wifi?\n\n53\n00:03:17.093 --> 00:03:21.073\nIs there fast wifi here?\n\n54\n00:03:21.113 --> 00:03:25.853\nDe wifi werkt heel goed.\n\n55\n00:03:25.873 --> 00:03:30.253\nThe wifi works very well.\n\n56\n00:03:30.273 --> 00:03:35.554\nWord number eight is WACHTWOORD.\n\n57\n00:03:35.594 --> 00:03:39.254\nWachtwoord means password in English.\n\n58\n00:03:39.294 --> 00:03:43.934\nHere is our last sentence.\n\n59\n00:03:43.994 --> 00:03:51.194\nMijn wachtwoord is geheim.\n\n60\n00:03:53.595 --> 00:03:57.635\nMy password is secret.\n\n61\n00:03:57.735 --> 00:04:06.735\nVul het juiste wachtwoord in.\n\n62\n00:04:07.776 --> 00:04:11.796\nEnter the correct password.\n\n63\n00:04:11.896 --> 00:04:15.736\nLet's recap today's words.\n\n64\n00:04:15.856 --> 00:04:22.697\néén. TELEFOON = phone.\n\n65\n00:04:22.737 --> 00:04:29.657\ntwee. INTERNET = internet.\n\n66\n00:04:29.717 --> 00:04:35.898\ndrie. APP = app.\n\n67\n00:04:35.978 --> 00:04:42.978\nvier. BERICHT = message.\n\n68\n00:04:43.038 --> 00:04:49.939\nvijf. E-MAIL = email.\n\n69\n00:04:50.019 --> 00:04:57.319\nzes. OPLADEN = to charge.\n\n70\n00:04:57.379 --> 00:05:04.139\nzeven. WIFI = wifi.\n\n71\n00:05:04.239 --> 00:05:11.220\nacht. WACHTWOORD = password.\n\n72\n00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:12.800\nGreat work today!\n
