2.407 --> 00:01:56.967\nHe reads the message now.\n\n34\n00:01:57.007 --> 00:02:00.788\nHe reads the message now.\n\n35\n00:02:00.848 --> 00:02:05.148\nWord number five is E-MAIL.\n\n36\n00:02:05.248 --> 00:02:10.128\nE-mail means email in English.\n\n37\n00:02:10.168 --> 00:02:12.988\nHere is an example.\n\n38\n00:02:13.088 --> 00:02:17.269\nI write an email.\n\n39\n00:02:17.389 --> 00:02:19.509\nI write an email.\n\n40\n00:02:19.529 --> 00:02:24.329\nThe email is very important.\n\n41\n00:02:24.369 --> 00:02:28.849\nThe email is very important.\n\n42\n00:02:28.869 --> 00:02:34.310\nWord number six is OPLADEN.\n\n43\n00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:38.910\nOpladen means to charge.\n\n44\n00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:42.150\nLet's practice a sentence.\n\n45\n00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:46.951\nI must charge my phone.\n\n46\n00:02:47.091 --> 00:02:50.811\nI must charge my phone.\n\n47\n00:02:50.851 --> 00:02:55.471\nThe battery charges now.\n\n48\n00:02:55.511 --> 00:02:59.571\nThe battery charges now.\n\n49\n00:02:59.611 --> 00:03:04.412\nWord number seven is WIFI.\n\n50\n00:03:04.472 --> 00:03:09.512\nWifi means wifi in English.\n\n51\n00:03:09.572 --> 00:03:12.452\nListen carefully now.\n\n52\n00:03:12.532 --> 00:03:17.013\nIs there fast wifi here?\n\n53\n00:03:17.093 --> 00:03:21.073\nIs there fast wifi here?\n\n54\n00:03:21.113 --> 00:03:25.853\nThe wifi works very well.\n\n55\n00:03:25.873 --> 00:03:30.253\nThe wifi works very well.\n\n56\n00:03:30.273 --> 00:03:35.554\nWord number eight is WACHTWOORD.\n\n57\n00:03:35.594 --> 00:03:39.254\nWachtwoord means password in English.\n\n58\n00:03:39.294 --> 00:03:43.934\nHere is our last sentence.\n\n59\n00:03:43.994 --> 00:03:51.194\nMy password is secret.\n\n60\n00:03:53.595 --> 00:03:57.635\nMy password is secret.\n\n61\n00:03:57.735 --> 00:04:06.735\nEnter the correct password.\n\n62\n00:04:07.776 --> 00:04:11.796\nEnter the correct password.\n\n63\n00:04:11.896 --> 00:04:15.736\nLet's recap today's words.\n\n64\n00:04:15.856 --> 00:04:22.697\none. TELEFOON = phone.\n\n65\n00:04:22.737 --> 00:04:29.657\ntwo. INTERNET = internet.\n\n66\n00:04:29.717 --> 00:04:35.898\nthree. APP = app.\n\n67\n00:04:35.978 --> 00:04:42.978\nfour. BERICHT = message.\n\n68\n00:04:43.038 --> 00:04:49.939\nfive. E-MAIL = email.\n\n69\n00:04:50.019 --> 00:04:57.319\nsix. OPLADEN = to charge.\n\n70\n00:04:57.379 --> 00:05:04.139\nseven. WIFI = wifi.\n\n71\n00:05:04.239 --> 00:05:11.220\neight. WACHTWOORD = password.\n\n72\n00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:12.800\nGreat work today!\n
vocab_health_body	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:04.680\nWelcome to today's Dutch lesson.\n\n2\n00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:08.441\nToday we learn health vocabulary.\n\n3\n00:00:08.501 --> 00:00:11.401\nHealth is very important.\n\n4\n00:00:11.501 --> 00:00:14.761\nLet's start with our lesson.\n\n5\n00:00:14.901 --> 00:00:17.701\nLaten we beginnen!\n\n6\n00:00:17.781 --> 00:00:19.682\nLet's begin!\n\n7\n00:00:19.742 --> 00:00:22.862\nOur first word is ZIEK.\n\n8\n00:00:22.962 --> 00:00:26.402\nZiek means sick in English.\n\n9\n00:00:26.462 --> 00:00:29.122\nLet's hear it in a sentence.\n\n10\n00:00:29.182 --> 00:00:32.663\nIk ben vandaag ziek.\n\n11\n00:00:32.823 --> 00:00:35.643\nI am sick today.\n\n12\n00:00:35.683 --> 00:00:38.403\nBen jij ook ziek?\n\n13\n00:00:38.483 --> 00:00:40.783\nAre you sick too?\n\n14\n00:00:40.863 --> 00:00:43.844\nOur second word is PIJN.\n\n15\n00:00:43.864 --> 00:00:47.484\nPijn means pain in English.\n\n16\n00:00:47.524 --> 00:00:50.464\nLet's hear an example sentence.\n\n17\n00:00:50.524 --> 00:00:53.784\nIk heb veel pijn.\n\n18\n00:00:53.924 --> 00:00:56.825\nI have much pain.\n\n19\n00:00:56.885 --> 00:00:59.705\nWaar heb je pijn?\n\n20\n00:00:59.745 --> 00:01:01.765\nWhere do you have pain?\n\n21\n00:01:01.845 --> 00:01:06.426\nOur third word is KOORTS.\n\n22\n00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:10.686\nKoorts means fever in English.\n\n23\n00:01:10.726 --> 00:01:15.666\nHere is a sentence with koorts.\n\n24\n00:01:15.726 --> 00:01:21.047\nHet kind heeft koorts.\n\n25\n00:01:21.107 --> 00:01:25.687\nThe child has a fever.\n\n26\n00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:31.608\nHij heeft hoge koorts.\n\n27\n00:01:31.648 --> 00:01:35.768\nHe has a high fever.\n\n28\n00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:40.948\nOur fourth word is HOESTEN.\n\n29\n00:01:41.008 --> 00:01:46.009\nHoesten means to cough in English.\n\n30\n00:01:46.089 --> 00:01:49.969\nLet's use it in a sentence.\n\n31\n00:01:50.049 --> 00:01:55.590\nIk moet veel hoesten.\n\n32\n00:01:55.770 --> 00:02:00.010\nI have to cough a lot.\n\n33\n00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:05.070\nWaarom moet je hoesten?\n\n34\n00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:08.891\nWhy must you cough?\n\n35\n00:02:08.991 --> 00:02:13.751\nOur fifth word is PILLEN.\n\n36\n00:02:13.791 --> 00:02:18.192\nPillen means pills in English.\n\n37\n00:02:18.292 --> 00:02:22.392\nListen to the next sentence.\n\n38\n00:02:22.452 --> 00:02:28.172\nIk neem twee pillen.\n\n39\n00:02:28.352 --> 00:02:31.153\nI take two pills.\n\n40\n00:02:31.213 --> 00:02:34.353\nDe pillen helpen goed.\n\n41\n00:02:34.373 --> 00:02:36.733\nThe pills help well.\n\n42\n00:02:36.813 --> 00:02:40.353\nOur sixth word is RECEPT.\n\n43\n00:02:40.473 --> 00:02:44.234\nRecept means prescription in English.\n\n44\n00:02:44.314 --> 00:02:46.414\nLet's practice this word.\n\n45\n00:02:46.494 --> 00:02:49.334\nIk heb een recept.\n\n46\n00:02:49.474 --> 00:02:51.614\nI have a prescription.\n\n47\n00:02:51.654 --> 00:02:55.235\nDe dokter geeft een recept.\n\n48\n00:02:55.255 --> 00:02:58.095\nThe doctor gives a prescription.\n\n49\n00:02:58.175 --> 00:03:01.855\nOur seventh word is APOTHEKER.\n\n50\n00:03:01.935 --> 00:03:05.656\nApotheker means pharmacist in English.\n\n51\n00:03:05.696 --> 00:03:08.316\nHere is our last sentence.\n\n52\n00:03:08.396 --> 00:03:11.796\nDe apotheker helpt mij.\n\n53\n00:03:11.816 --> 00:03:14.096\nThe pharmacist helps me.\n\n54\n00:03:14.176 --> 00:03:17.417\nIk spreek de apotheker.\n\n55\n00:03:17.517 --> 00:03:19.737\nI speak to the pharmacist.\n\n56\n00:03:19.797 --> 00:03:22.197\nLet's recap today's words.\n\n57\n00:03:22.237 --> 00:03:26.737\néén. ZIEK = sick.\n\n58\n00:03:26.777 --> 00:03:31.178\ntwee. PIJN = pain.\n\n59\n00:03:31.278 --> 00:03:35.958\ndrie. KOORTS = fever.\n\n60\n00:03:36.058 --> 00:03:41.179\nvier. HOESTEN = to cough.\n\n61\n00:03:41.239 --> 00:03:46.119\nvijf. PILLEN = pills.\n\n62\n00:03:46.179 --> 00:03:51.619\nzes. RECEPT = prescription.\n\n63\n00:03:51.699 --> 00:03:57.180\nzeven. APOTHEKER = pharmacist.\n\n64\n00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:58.580\nGreat work today!\n
