 to cough a lot.\n\n33\n00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:05.070\nWhy must you cough?\n\n34\n00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:08.891\nWhy must you cough?\n\n35\n00:02:08.991 --> 00:02:13.751\nOur fifth word is PILLEN.\n\n36\n00:02:13.791 --> 00:02:18.192\nPillen means pills in English.\n\n37\n00:02:18.292 --> 00:02:22.392\nListen to the next sentence.\n\n38\n00:02:22.452 --> 00:02:28.172\nI take two pills.\n\n39\n00:02:28.352 --> 00:02:31.153\nI take two pills.\n\n40\n00:02:31.213 --> 00:02:34.353\nThe pills help well.\n\n41\n00:02:34.373 --> 00:02:36.733\nThe pills help well.\n\n42\n00:02:36.813 --> 00:02:40.353\nOur sixth word is RECEPT.\n\n43\n00:02:40.473 --> 00:02:44.234\nRecept means prescription in English.\n\n44\n00:02:44.314 --> 00:02:46.414\nLet's practice this word.\n\n45\n00:02:46.494 --> 00:02:49.334\nI have a prescription.\n\n46\n00:02:49.474 --> 00:02:51.614\nI have a prescription.\n\n47\n00:02:51.654 --> 00:02:55.235\nThe doctor gives a prescription.\n\n48\n00:02:55.255 --> 00:02:58.095\nThe doctor gives a prescription.\n\n49\n00:02:58.175 --> 00:03:01.855\nOur seventh word is APOTHEKER.\n\n50\n00:03:01.935 --> 00:03:05.656\nApotheker means pharmacist in English.\n\n51\n00:03:05.696 --> 00:03:08.316\nHere is our last sentence.\n\n52\n00:03:08.396 --> 00:03:11.796\nThe pharmacist helps me.\n\n53\n00:03:11.816 --> 00:03:14.096\nThe pharmacist helps me.\n\n54\n00:03:14.176 --> 00:03:17.417\nI speak to the pharmacist.\n\n55\n00:03:17.517 --> 00:03:19.737\nI speak to the pharmacist.\n\n56\n00:03:19.797 --> 00:03:22.197\nLet's recap today's words.\n\n57\n00:03:22.237 --> 00:03:26.737\none. ZIEK = sick.\n\n58\n00:03:26.777 --> 00:03:31.178\ntwo. PIJN = pain.\n\n59\n00:03:31.278 --> 00:03:35.958\nthree. KOORTS = fever.\n\n60\n00:03:36.058 --> 00:03:41.179\nfour. HOESTEN = to cough.\n\n61\n00:03:41.239 --> 00:03:46.119\nfive. PILLEN = pills.\n\n62\n00:03:46.179 --> 00:03:51.619\nsix. RECEPT = prescription.\n\n63\n00:03:51.699 --> 00:03:57.180\nseven. APOTHEKER = pharmacist.\n\n64\n00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:58.580\nGreat work today!\n
vocab_nature_outdoor	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:05.240\nWelcome to today's Dutch lesson.\n\n2\n00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:10.800\nToday we explore nature and outdoors.\n\n3\n00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:14.981\nDutch nature is very beautiful.\n\n4\n00:00:15.021 --> 00:00:19.281\nLet's learn seven words together.\n\n5\n00:00:19.341 --> 00:00:23.061\nLaten we nu beginnen!\n\n6\n00:00:23.141 --> 00:00:25.781\nLet's get started now!\n\n7\n00:00:25.861 --> 00:00:30.561\nOur first word is NATUUR.\n\n8\n00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:35.721\nNatuur means nature in English.\n\n9\n00:00:35.761 --> 00:00:39.361\nListen to this example sentence.\n\n10\n00:00:39.421 --> 00:00:44.862\nDe natuur is hier heel mooi.\n\n11\n00:00:44.902 --> 00:00:48.962\nNature is very beautiful here.\n\n12\n00:00:49.002 --> 00:00:52.522\nIk hou van de natuur.\n\n13\n00:00:52.682 --> 00:00:56.302\nI love nature very much.\n\n14\n00:00:56.382 --> 00:01:00.702\nOur second word is BOS.\n\n15\n00:01:00.762 --> 00:01:05.502\nBos means forest in English.\n\n16\n00:01:05.542 --> 00:01:08.503\nLet me show you a sentence.\n\n17\n00:01:08.583 --> 00:01:13.043\nHet bos is erg groot.\n\n18\n00:01:13.063 --> 00:01:16.783\nThe forest is very big.\n\n19\n00:01:16.823 --> 00:01:19.543\nWij lopen in het bos.\n\n20\n00:01:19.563 --> 00:01:22.803\nWe are walking in the forest.\n\n21\n00:01:22.883 --> 00:01:27.463\nOur third word is STRAND.\n\n22\n00:01:27.523 --> 00:01:31.963\nStrand means beach in English.\n\n23\n00:01:32.003 --> 00:01:35.584\nLet's try a new sentence.\n\n24\n00:01:35.644 --> 00:01:40.424\nHet strand is erg mooi.\n\n25\n00:01:40.444 --> 00:01:44.904\nThe beach is very beautiful.\n\n26\n00:01:44.964 --> 00:01:49.144\nIk ben op het strand.\n\n27\n00:01:49.424 --> 00:01:53.104\nI am on the beach now.\n\n28\n00:01:53.204 --> 00:01:57.804\nOur fourth word is DUIN.\n\n29\n00:01:57.864 --> 00:02:02.224\nDuin means dune in English.\n\n30\n00:02:02.284 --> 00:02:06.625\nYou find dunes near the beach.\n\n31\n00:02:06.685 --> 00:02:11.145\nDat is een hoog duin.\n\n32\n00:02:11.185 --> 00:02:15.365\nThat is a high dune.\n\n33\n00:02:15.405 --> 00:02:20.005\nWe klimmen op het duin.\n\n34\n00:02:20.045 --> 00:02:24.125\nWe climb up the dune together.\n\n35\n00:02:24.385 --> 00:02:28.925\nOur fifth word is POLDER.\n\n36\n00:02:28.965 --> 00:02:33.186\nPolder means reclaimed land in English.\n\n37\n00:02:33.206 --> 00:02:36.966\nHere is a useful Dutch sentence.\n\n38\n00:02:36.986 --> 00:02:40.706\nDe polder is heel plat.\n\n39\n00:02:40.726 --> 00:02:44.206\nThe polder is very flat.\n\n40\n00:02:44.266 --> 00:02:47.526\nIk zie de mooie polder.\n\n41\n00:02:47.706 --> 00:02:51.066\nI see the beautiful polder.\n\n42\n00:02:51.166 --> 00:02:55.306\nOur sixth word is WANDELEN.\n\n43\n00:02:55.366 --> 00:02:59.767\nWandelen means to walk in English.\n\n44\n00:02:59.807 --> 00:03:02.767\nLet's practice a sentence together.\n\n45\n00:03:02.827 --> 00:03:06.627\nWij wandelen in het park.\n\n46\n00:03:06.647 --> 00:03:09.607\nWe walk in the park.\n\n47\n00:03:09.667 --> 00:03:12.887\nIk wil graag wandelen.\n\n48\n00:03:13.047 --> 00:03:15.607\nI would like to walk.\n\n49\n00:03:15.687 --> 00:03:19.787\nOur seventh word is VOGELS.\n\n50\n00:03:19.827 --> 00:03:24.108\nVogels means birds in English.\n\n51\n00:03:24.148 --> 00:03:27.548\nHere is our last example sentence.\n\n52\n00:03:27.648 --> 00:03:31.488\nEr vliegen veel vogels.\n\n53\n00:03:31.508 --> 00:03:34.128\nMany birds are flying.\n\n54\n00:03:34.188 --> 00:03:37.628\nZie jij de vogels daar?\n\n55\n00:03:37.688 --> 00:03:40.608\nDo you see the birds there?\n\n56\n00:03:40.668 --> 00:03:44.028\nLet's recap today's words.\n\n57\n00:03:44.128 --> 00:03:49.428\néén. NATUUR = nature.\n\n58\n00:03:49.448 --> 00:03:55.149\ntwee. BOS = forest.\n\n59\n00:03:55.169 --> 00:04:01.169\ndrie. STRAND = beach.\n\n60\n00:04:01.229 --> 00:04:06.869\nvier. DUIN = dune.\n\n61\n00:04:06.909 --> 00:04:12.869\nvijf. POLDER = polder.\n\n62\n00:04:12.929 --> 00:04:19.290\nzes. WANDELEN = to walk.\n\n63\n00:04:19.330 --> 00:04:26.010\nzeven. VOGELS = birds.\n\n64\n00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:29.170\nGreat work learning nature words today!\n\n65\n00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:30.770\nSee you in the next lesson!\n
