 beach.\n\n31\n00:02:06.685 --> 00:02:11.145\nThat is a high dune.\n\n32\n00:02:11.185 --> 00:02:15.365\nThat is a high dune.\n\n33\n00:02:15.405 --> 00:02:20.005\nWe climb up the dune together.\n\n34\n00:02:20.045 --> 00:02:24.125\nWe climb up the dune together.\n\n35\n00:02:24.385 --> 00:02:28.925\nOur fifth word is POLDER.\n\n36\n00:02:28.965 --> 00:02:33.186\nPolder means reclaimed land in English.\n\n37\n00:02:33.206 --> 00:02:36.966\nHere is a useful Dutch sentence.\n\n38\n00:02:36.986 --> 00:02:40.706\nThe polder is very flat.\n\n39\n00:02:40.726 --> 00:02:44.206\nThe polder is very flat.\n\n40\n00:02:44.266 --> 00:02:47.526\nI see the beautiful polder.\n\n41\n00:02:47.706 --> 00:02:51.066\nI see the beautiful polder.\n\n42\n00:02:51.166 --> 00:02:55.306\nOur sixth word is WANDELEN.\n\n43\n00:02:55.366 --> 00:02:59.767\nWandelen means to walk in English.\n\n44\n00:02:59.807 --> 00:03:02.767\nLet's practice a sentence together.\n\n45\n00:03:02.827 --> 00:03:06.627\nWe walk in the park.\n\n46\n00:03:06.647 --> 00:03:09.607\nWe walk in the park.\n\n47\n00:03:09.667 --> 00:03:12.887\nI would like to walk.\n\n48\n00:03:13.047 --> 00:03:15.607\nI would like to walk.\n\n49\n00:03:15.687 --> 00:03:19.787\nOur seventh word is VOGELS.\n\n50\n00:03:19.827 --> 00:03:24.108\nVogels means birds in English.\n\n51\n00:03:24.148 --> 00:03:27.548\nHere is our last example sentence.\n\n52\n00:03:27.648 --> 00:03:31.488\nMany birds are flying.\n\n53\n00:03:31.508 --> 00:03:34.128\nMany birds are flying.\n\n54\n00:03:34.188 --> 00:03:37.628\nDo you see the birds there?\n\n55\n00:03:37.688 --> 00:03:40.608\nDo you see the birds there?\n\n56\n00:03:40.668 --> 00:03:44.028\nLet's recap today's words.\n\n57\n00:03:44.128 --> 00:03:49.428\none. NATUUR = nature.\n\n58\n00:03:49.448 --> 00:03:55.149\ntwo. BOS = forest.\n\n59\n00:03:55.169 --> 00:04:01.169\nthree. STRAND = beach.\n\n60\n00:04:01.229 --> 00:04:06.869\nfour. DUIN = dune.\n\n61\n00:04:06.909 --> 00:04:12.869\nfive. POLDER = polder.\n\n62\n00:04:12.929 --> 00:04:19.290\nsix. WANDELEN = to walk.\n\n63\n00:04:19.330 --> 00:04:26.010\nseven. VOGELS = birds.\n\n64\n00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:29.170\nGreat work learning nature words today!\n\n65\n00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:30.770\nSee you in the next lesson!\n
vocab_polite_expressions	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:05.560\nWelcome to our Dutch lesson.\n\n2\n00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:10.340\nToday we learn polite words.\n\n3\n00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:14.121\nLaten we nu beginnen!\n\n4\n00:00:14.221 --> 00:00:19.341\nOur first word is DANK JE WEL.\n\n5\n00:00:19.381 --> 00:00:23.921\nThis is informal for thank you.\n\n6\n00:00:24.021 --> 00:00:27.461\nLet us hear an example.\n\n7\n00:00:27.521 --> 00:00:31.521\nDank je wel voor de hulp.\n\n8\n00:00:31.581 --> 00:00:35.542\nIk zeg dank je wel.\n\n9\n00:00:35.562 --> 00:00:39.922\nNow, let's learn the formal version.\n\n10\n00:00:39.962 --> 00:00:45.122\nThe formal version is DANK U WEL.\n\n11\n00:00:45.142 --> 00:00:49.722\nUse this with teachers or strangers.\n\n12\n00:00:49.782 --> 00:00:53.962\nDank u wel, meneer Bakker.\n\n13\n00:00:54.002 --> 00:00:58.003\nWij zeggen dank u wel.\n\n14\n00:00:58.103 --> 00:01:03.023\nOur next word is ALSJEBLIEFT.\n\n15\n00:01:03.043 --> 00:01:07.943\nThis means please or here you go.\n\n16\n00:01:07.963 --> 00:01:12.643\nIt is used in informal situations.\n\n17\n00:01:12.703 --> 00:01:17.443\nEen appel voor jou, alsjeblieft.\n\n18\n00:01:17.503 --> 00:01:20.084\nHelp mij, alsjeblieft.\n\n19\n00:01:20.124 --> 00:01:24.824\nNow, the formal version is ALSTUBLIEFT.\n\n20\n00:01:24.864 --> 00:01:28.124\nUse this with people you respect.\n\n21\n00:01:28.144 --> 00:01:31.944\nKoffie voor u, alstublieft.\n\n22\n00:01:31.984 --> 00:01:35.904\nSpreekt u langzaam, alstublieft.\n\n23\n00:01:35.964 --> 00:01:40.484\nExcellent. Our next word is GRAAG.\n\n24\n00:01:40.564 --> 00:01:45.005\nGraag means gladly or with pleasure.\n\n25\n00:01:45.045 --> 00:01:47.985\nIt is used to accept offers.\n\n26\n00:01:48.045 --> 00:01:50.645\nIk wil graag een thee.\n\n27\n00:01:50.805 --> 00:01:53.665\nJa, ik doe dat graag.\n\n28\n00:01:53.705 --> 00:01:57.105\nNow we look at GRAAG GEDAAN.\n\n29\n00:01:57.165 --> 00:01:59.825\nIt means you are welcome.\n\n30\n00:01:59.905 --> 00:02:02.765\nGraag gedaan, tot ziens!\n\n31\n00:02:02.806 --> 00:02:06.106\nNext, we have the word SORRY.\n\n32\n00:02:06.186 --> 00:02:10.066\nSorry means sorry in Dutch too.\n\n33\n00:02:10.146 --> 00:02:12.646\nSorry, ik ben te laat.\n\n34\n00:02:12.706 --> 00:02:15.566\nHet spijt me, sorry hoor.\n\n35\n00:02:15.606 --> 00:02:19.226\nAnother polite word is EXCUSEER.\n\n36\n00:02:19.306 --> 00:02:22.486\nExcuseer means excuse me.\n\n37\n00:02:22.646 --> 00:02:25.167\nUse it to get someone's attention.\n\n38\n00:02:25.247 --> 00:02:28.587\nExcuseer, waar is de trein?\n\n39\n00:02:28.647 --> 00:02:32.107\nExcuseer mij, mag ik erlangs?\n\n40\n00:02:32.167 --> 00:02:35.967\nOur last phrase is GEEN DANK.\n\n41\n00:02:36.027 --> 00:02:39.567\nGeen dank means no thanks needed.\n\n42\n00:02:39.607 --> 00:02:42.447\nIt is another way to say welcome.\n\n43\n00:02:42.547 --> 00:02:44.747\nGeen dank, mijn vriend.\n\n44\n00:02:44.827 --> 00:02:48.008\nGeen dank, graag gedaan hoor.\n\n45\n00:02:48.068 --> 00:02:50.668\nYou are doing very well.\n\n46\n00:02:50.688 --> 00:02:53.248\nLet's recap today's words.\n\n47\n00:02:53.288 --> 00:02:54.748\nNummer één.\n\n48\n00:02:54.808 --> 00:02:57.588\nALSJEBLIEFT = please.\n\n49\n00:02:57.628 --> 00:02:59.088\nNummer twee.\n\n50\n00:02:59.148 --> 00:03:02.968\nALSTUBLIEFT = please (formal).\n\n51\n00:03:02.988 --> 00:03:04.488\nNummer drie.\n\n52\n00:03:04.528 --> 00:03:07.368\nDANK JE WEL = thank you.\n\n53\n00:03:07.408 --> 00:03:08.948\nNummer vier.\n\n54\n00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:12.909\nDANK U WEL = thank you (formal).\n\n55\n00:03:12.929 --> 00:03:14.469\nNummer vijf.\n\n56\n00:03:14.529 --> 00:03:17.129\nGRAAG = gladly.\n\n57\n00:03:17.169 --> 00:03:18.549\nNummer zes.\n\n58\n00:03:18.609 --> 00:03:22.709\nGRAAG GEDAAN = you are welcome.\n\n59\n00:03:22.749 --> 00:03:24.629\nNummer zeven.\n\n60\n00:03:24.709 --> 00:03:28.249\nSORRY = sorry.\n\n61\n00:03:28.309 --> 00:03:30.009\nNummer acht.\n\n62\n00:03:30.069 --> 00:03:34.550\nEXCUSEER = excuse me.\n\n63\n00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:36.410\nNummer negen.\n\n64\n00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:40.950\nGEEN DANK = you are welcome.\n\n65\n00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:42.430\nGreat work today!\n
vocab_polite_expressions	en	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:05.560\nWelcome to our Dutch lesson.\n\n2\n00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:10.340\nToday we learn polite words.\n\n3\n00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:14.121\nLet us start now!\n\n4\n00:00:14.221 --> 00:00:19.341\nOur first word is DANK JE WEL.\n\n5\n00:00:19.381 --> 00:00:23.921\nThis is informal for thank you.\n\n6\n00:00:24.021 --> 00:00:27.461\nLet us hear an example.\n\n7\n00:00:27.521 --> 00:00:31.521\nThank you for the help.\n\n8\n00:00:31.581 --> 00:00:35.542\nI say thank you.\n\n9\n00:00:35.562 --> 00:00:39.922\nNow, let's learn the formal version.\n\n10\n00:00:39.962 --> 00:00:45.122\nThe formal version is DANK U WEL.\n\n11\n00:00:45.142 --> 00:00:49.722\nUse this with teachers or strangers.\n\n12\n00:00:49.782 --> 00:00:53.962\nThank you, Mr. Bakker.\n\n13\n00:00:54.002 --> 00:00:58.003\nWe say thank you.\n\n14\n00:00:58.103 --> 00:01:03.023\nOur next word is ALSJEBLIEFT.\n\n15\n00:01:03.043 --> 00:01:07.943\nThis means please or here you go.\n\n16\n00:01:07.963 --> 00:01:12.643\nIt is used in informal situations.\n\n17\n00:01:12.703 --> 00:01:17.443\nAn apple for you, here you go.\n\n18\n00:01:17.503 --> 00:01:20.084\nHelp me, please.\n\n19\n00:01:20.124 --> 00:01:24.824\nNow, the formal version is ALSTUBLIEFT.\n\n20\n00:01:24.864 --> 00:01:28.124\nUse this with people you respect.\n\n21\n00:01:28.144 --> 00:01:31.944\nCoffee for you, here you go.\n\n22\n00:01:31.984 --> 00:01:35.904\nSpeak slowly, please.\n\n23\n00:01:35.964 --> 00:01:40.484\nExcellent. Our next word is GRAAG.\n\n24\n00:01:40.564 --> 00:01:45.005\nGraag means gladly or with pleasure.\n\n25\n00:01:45.045 --> 00:01:47.985\nIt is used to accept offers.\n\n26\n00:01:48.045 --> 00:01:50.645\nI would gladly like a tea.\n\n27\n00:01:50.805 --> 00:01:53.665\nYes, I gladly do that.\n\n28\n00:01:53.705 --> 00:01:57.105\nNow we look at GRAAG GEDAAN.\n\n29\n00:01:57.165 --> 00:01:59.825\nIt means you are welcome.\n\n30\n00:01:59.905 --> 00:02:02.765\nYou are welcome, goodbye!\n\n31\n00:02:02.806 --> 00:02:06.106\nNext, we have the word SORRY.\n\n32\n00:02:06.186 --> 00:02:10.066\nSorry means sorry in Dutch too.\n\n33\n00:02:10.146 --> 00:02:12.646\nSorry, I am too late.\n\n34\n00:02:12.706 --> 00:02:15.566\nI am sorry, sorry indeed.\n\n35\n00:02:15.606 --> 00:02:19.226\nAnother polite word is EXCUSEER.\n\n36\n00:02:19.306 --> 00:02:22.486\nExcuseer means excuse me.\n\n37\n00:02:22.646 --> 00:02:25.167\nUse it to get someone's attention.\n\n38\n00:02:25.247 --> 00:02:28.587\nExcuse me, where is the train?\n\n39\n00:02:28.647 --> 00:02:32.107\nExcuse me, may I pass?\n\n40\n00:02:32.167 --> 00:02:35.967\nOur last phrase is GEEN DANK.\n\n41\n00:02:36.027 --> 00:02:39.567\nGeen dank means no thanks needed.\n\n42\n00:02:39.607 --> 00:02:42.447\nIt is another way to say welcome.\n\n43\n00:02:42.547 --> 00:02:44.747\nYou are welcome, my friend.\n\n44\n00:02:44.827 --> 00:02:48.008\nYou are welcome, gladly done indeed.\n\n45\n00:02:48.068 --> 00:02:50.668\nYou are doing very well.\n\n46\n00:02:50.688 --> 00:02:53.248\nLet's recap today's words.\n\n47\n00:02:53.288 --> 00:02:54.748\nNumber one.\n\n48\n00:02:54.808 --> 00:02:57.588\nALSJEBLIEFT = please.\n\n49\n00:02:57.628 --> 00:02:59.088\nNumber two.\n\n50\n00:02:59.148 --> 00:03:02.968\nALSTUBLIEFT = please (formal).\n\n51\n00:03:02.988 --> 00:03:04.488\nNumber three.\n\n52\n00:03:04.528 --> 00:03:07.368\nDANK JE WEL = thank you.\n\n53\n00:03:07.408 --> 00:03:08.948\nNumber four.\n\n54\n00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:12.909\nDANK U WEL = thank you (formal).\n\n55\n00:03:12.929 --> 00:03:14.469\nNumber five.\n\n56\n00:03:14.529 --> 00:03:17.129\nGRAAG = gladly.\n\n57\n00:03:17.169 --> 00:03:18.549\nNumber six.\n\n58\n00:03:18.609 --> 00:03:22.709\nGRAAG GEDAAN = you are welcome.\n\n59\n00:03:22.749 --> 00:03:24.629\nNumber seven.\n\n60\n00:03:24.709 --> 00:03:28.249\nSORRY = sorry.\n\n61\n00:03:28.309 --> 00:03:30.009\nNumber eight.\n\n62\n00:03:30.069 --> 00:03:34.550\nEXCUSEER = excuse me.\n\n63\n00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:36.410\nNumber nine.\n\n64\n00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:40.950\nGEEN DANK = you are welcome.\n\n65\n00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:42.430\nGreat work today!\n
