tasty soup.\n\n33\n00:02:18.286 --> 00:02:22.746\nRemember: KOKEN = cooking.\n\n34\n00:02:22.846 --> 00:02:26.686\nOur sixth word is MUZIEK.\n\n35\n00:02:26.726 --> 00:02:30.166\nMuziek means music.\n\n36\n00:02:30.266 --> 00:02:34.227\nI listen to music.\n\n37\n00:02:34.267 --> 00:02:37.707\nThe music is very beautiful.\n\n38\n00:02:37.787 --> 00:02:42.627\nRemember: MUZIEK = music.\n\n39\n00:02:42.727 --> 00:02:46.787\nOur seventh word is SCHILDEREN.\n\n40\n00:02:46.847 --> 00:02:50.387\nSchilderen means painting.\n\n41\n00:02:50.447 --> 00:02:53.987\nShe can paint beautifully.\n\n42\n00:02:54.067 --> 00:02:58.128\nI paint a big house.\n\n43\n00:02:58.188 --> 00:03:03.248\nRemember: SCHILDEREN = painting.\n\n44\n00:03:03.288 --> 00:03:06.788\nLet's recap today's words.\n\n45\n00:03:06.888 --> 00:03:11.368\none. VOETBAL = football.\n\n46\n00:03:11.408 --> 00:03:17.228\ntwo. ZWEMMEN = swimming.\n\n47\n00:03:17.308 --> 00:03:24.249\nthree. FIETSEN = cycling.\n\n48\n00:03:24.349 --> 00:03:31.409\nfour. LEZEN = reading.\n\n49\n00:03:31.469 --> 00:03:37.949\nfive. KOKEN = cooking.\n\n50\n00:03:38.029 --> 00:03:44.730\nsix. MUZIEK = music.\n\n51\n00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:51.730\nseven. SCHILDEREN = painting.\n\n52\n00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:54.930\nGreat work today!\n\n53\n00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:55.650\nSee you next time!\n
vocab_vegetables_fruit	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:04.580\nWelcome to our Dutch classroom!\n\n2\n00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.661\nToday we learn about fresh food.\n\n3\n00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:12.101\nWe look at vegetables and fruit.\n\n4\n00:00:12.181 --> 00:00:14.581\nIn Dutch, we say:\n\n5\n00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:18.081\nGroenten en fruit.\n\n6\n00:00:18.141 --> 00:00:21.221\nLet us start our lesson.\n\n7\n00:00:21.281 --> 00:00:24.042\nLaten we beginnen!\n\n8\n00:00:24.102 --> 00:00:27.722\nOur first word is APPEL.\n\n9\n00:00:27.782 --> 00:00:31.442\nAppel means apple in English.\n\n10\n00:00:31.542 --> 00:00:34.302\nListen to this sentence.\n\n11\n00:00:34.362 --> 00:00:37.763\nDe appel is rood.\n\n12\n00:00:37.843 --> 00:00:39.863\nLet's hear another one.\n\n13\n00:00:39.903 --> 00:00:42.923\nIk eet een appel.\n\n14\n00:00:42.963 --> 00:00:45.743\nThat is very simple, right?\n\n15\n00:00:45.823 --> 00:00:49.683\nOur second word is BANAAN.\n\n16\n00:00:49.723 --> 00:00:52.724\nBanaan means banana.\n\n17\n00:00:52.764 --> 00:00:55.784\nHere is our first sentence.\n\n18\n00:00:55.844 --> 00:00:59.144\nDe banaan is geel.\n\n19\n00:00:59.264 --> 00:01:01.324\nAnd another sentence.\n\n20\n00:01:01.364 --> 00:01:04.504\nHij eet een banaan.\n\n21\n00:01:04.524 --> 00:01:07.765\nNow let us look at TOMAAT.\n\n22\n00:01:07.805 --> 00:01:10.805\nTomaat means tomato.\n\n23\n00:01:10.865 --> 00:01:13.465\nLet's practice with a sentence.\n\n24\n00:01:13.485 --> 00:01:16.805\nDe tomaat is rood.\n\n25\n00:01:16.825 --> 00:01:19.625\nHere is one more.\n\n26\n00:01:19.705 --> 00:01:22.866\nZij snijdt de tomaat.\n\n27\n00:01:22.906 --> 00:01:25.846\nFantastic progress!\n\n28\n00:01:25.906 --> 00:01:29.726\nNext we have the AARDAPPEL.\n\n29\n00:01:29.906 --> 00:01:32.966\nAardappel means potato.\n\n30\n00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:35.687\nLet's hear a sentence.\n\n31\n00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:39.587\nIk kook de aardappel.\n\n32\n00:01:39.627 --> 00:01:42.187\nLet's do another one.\n\n33\n00:01:42.227 --> 00:01:45.607\nDe aardappel is warm.\n\n34\n00:01:45.647 --> 00:01:48.667\nGreat, you are doing well.\n\n35\n00:01:48.707 --> 00:01:52.348\nNext is the word WORTEL.\n\n36\n00:01:52.388 --> 00:01:56.188\nWortel means carrot in English.\n\n37\n00:01:56.228 --> 00:01:59.248\nLet's listen to a sentence.\n\n38\n00:01:59.268 --> 00:02:02.988\nDe wortel is oranje.\n\n39\n00:02:03.048 --> 00:02:06.089\nAnd another sentence.\n\n40\n00:02:06.129 --> 00:02:09.549\nDe wortel is gezond.\n\n41\n00:02:09.569 --> 00:02:11.369\nPerfect.\n\n42\n00:02:11.609 --> 00:02:15.069\nNow let us learn UI.\n\n43\n00:02:15.129 --> 00:02:18.070\nUi means onion.\n\n44\n00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:21.030\nLet's hear it in a sentence.\n\n45\n00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:24.290\nIk snijd een ui.\n\n46\n00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:26.890\nLet's try another one.\n\n47\n00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:29.550\nDe ui is scherp.\n\n48\n00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:31.430\nWell done.\n\n49\n00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:35.771\nOur seventh word is SLA.\n\n50\n00:02:35.851 --> 00:02:39.871\nSla means lettuce.\n\n51\n00:02:39.951 --> 00:02:42.991\nLet's use it in a sentence.\n\n52\n00:02:43.031 --> 00:02:46.712\nDe sla is groen.\n\n53\n00:02:46.752 --> 00:02:49.532\nHere is another sentence.\n\n54\n00:02:49.572 --> 00:02:53.912\nWij eten verse sla.\n\n55\n00:02:53.972 --> 00:02:56.752\nYou are learning fast!\n\n56\n00:02:56.792 --> 00:03:01.633\nNext we have the word DRUIVEN.\n\n57\n00:03:01.693 --> 00:03:05.833\nDruiven means grapes.\n\n58\n00:03:05.873 --> 00:03:09.193\nHere is our first sentence.\n\n59\n00:03:09.233 --> 00:03:13.513\nDe druiven zijn zoet.\n\n60\n00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:16.174\nAnd the second sentence.\n\n61\n00:03:16.254 --> 00:03:20.834\nIk koop blauwe druiven.\n\n62\n00:03:20.894 --> 00:03:26.234\nOur final word for today is PEER.\n\n63\n00:03:26.274 --> 00:03:30.155\nPeer means pear.\n\n64\n00:03:30.195 --> 00:03:32.935\nLet's hear a sentence.\n\n65\n00:03:32.975 --> 00:03:37.335\nDe peer is sappig.\n\n66\n00:03:37.395 --> 00:03:40.815\nLet's practice one more sentence.\n\n67\n00:03:40.895 --> 00:03:45.336\nIk eet een peer.\n\n68\n00:03:45.396 --> 00:03:48.356\nLet's recap today's words.\n\n69\n00:03:48.456 --> 00:03:54.076\néén. APPEL = apple.\n\n70\n00:03:54.136 --> 00:04:00.417\ntwee. BANAAN = banana.\n\n71\n00:04:00.457 --> 00:04:06.557\ndrie. TOMAAT = tomato.\n\n72\n00:04:06.677 --> 00:04:12.518\nvier. AARDAPPEL = potato.\n\n73\n00:04:12.598 --> 00:04:19.018\nvijf. WORTEL = carrot.\n\n74\n00:04:19.078 --> 00:04:25.158\nzes. UI = onion.\n\n75\n00:04:25.238 --> 00:04:32.179\nzeven. SLA = lettuce.\n\n76\n00:04:32.239 --> 00:04:39.439\nacht. DRUIVEN = grapes.\n\n77\n00:04:39.839 --> 00:04:47.039\nnegen. PEER = pear.\n\n78\n00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:48.380\nGreat work today!\n
