\n00:01:42.227 --> 00:01:45.607\nThe potato is warm.\n\n34\n00:01:45.647 --> 00:01:48.667\nGreat, you are doing well.\n\n35\n00:01:48.707 --> 00:01:52.348\nNext is the word WORTEL.\n\n36\n00:01:52.388 --> 00:01:56.188\nWortel means carrot in English.\n\n37\n00:01:56.228 --> 00:01:59.248\nLet's listen to a sentence.\n\n38\n00:01:59.268 --> 00:02:02.988\nThe carrot is orange.\n\n39\n00:02:03.048 --> 00:02:06.089\nAnd another sentence.\n\n40\n00:02:06.129 --> 00:02:09.549\nThe carrot is healthy.\n\n41\n00:02:09.569 --> 00:02:11.369\nPerfect.\n\n42\n00:02:11.609 --> 00:02:15.069\nNow let us learn UI.\n\n43\n00:02:15.129 --> 00:02:18.070\nUi means onion.\n\n44\n00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:21.030\nLet's hear it in a sentence.\n\n45\n00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:24.290\nI cut an onion.\n\n46\n00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:26.890\nLet's try another one.\n\n47\n00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:29.550\nThe onion is sharp.\n\n48\n00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:31.430\nWell done.\n\n49\n00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:35.771\nOur seventh word is SLA.\n\n50\n00:02:35.851 --> 00:02:39.871\nSla means lettuce.\n\n51\n00:02:39.951 --> 00:02:42.991\nLet's use it in a sentence.\n\n52\n00:02:43.031 --> 00:02:46.712\nThe lettuce is green.\n\n53\n00:02:46.752 --> 00:02:49.532\nHere is another sentence.\n\n54\n00:02:49.572 --> 00:02:53.912\nWe eat fresh lettuce.\n\n55\n00:02:53.972 --> 00:02:56.752\nYou are learning fast!\n\n56\n00:02:56.792 --> 00:03:01.633\nNext we have the word DRUIVEN.\n\n57\n00:03:01.693 --> 00:03:05.833\nDruiven means grapes.\n\n58\n00:03:05.873 --> 00:03:09.193\nHere is our first sentence.\n\n59\n00:03:09.233 --> 00:03:13.513\nThe grapes are sweet.\n\n60\n00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:16.174\nAnd the second sentence.\n\n61\n00:03:16.254 --> 00:03:20.834\nI buy blue grapes.\n\n62\n00:03:20.894 --> 00:03:26.234\nOur final word for today is PEER.\n\n63\n00:03:26.274 --> 00:03:30.155\nPeer means pear.\n\n64\n00:03:30.195 --> 00:03:32.935\nLet's hear a sentence.\n\n65\n00:03:32.975 --> 00:03:37.335\nThe pear is juicy.\n\n66\n00:03:37.395 --> 00:03:40.815\nLet's practice one more sentence.\n\n67\n00:03:40.895 --> 00:03:45.336\nI eat a pear.\n\n68\n00:03:45.396 --> 00:03:48.356\nLet's recap today's words.\n\n69\n00:03:48.456 --> 00:03:54.076\none. APPEL = apple.\n\n70\n00:03:54.136 --> 00:04:00.417\ntwo. BANAAN = banana.\n\n71\n00:04:00.457 --> 00:04:06.557\nthree. TOMAAT = tomato.\n\n72\n00:04:06.677 --> 00:04:12.518\nfour. AARDAPPEL = potato.\n\n73\n00:04:12.598 --> 00:04:19.018\nfive. WORTEL = carrot.\n\n74\n00:04:19.078 --> 00:04:25.158\nsix. UI = onion.\n\n75\n00:04:25.238 --> 00:04:32.179\nseven. SLA = lettuce.\n\n76\n00:04:32.239 --> 00:04:39.439\neight. DRUIVEN = grapes.\n\n77\n00:04:39.839 --> 00:04:47.039\nnine. PEER = pear.\n\n78\n00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:48.380\nGreat work today!\n
vocab_work_office	nl	WEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:05.580\nWelcome to today's Dutch vocabulary lesson.\n\n2\n00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.141\nToday we learn words about work.\n\n3\n00:00:09.181 --> 00:00:12.001\nWe will talk about the office.\n\n4\n00:00:12.161 --> 00:00:14.161\nLaten we beginnen!\n\n5\n00:00:14.281 --> 00:00:15.581\nLet's begin!\n\n6\n00:00:15.661 --> 00:00:18.701\nOur first word is WERKEN.\n\n7\n00:00:18.781 --> 00:00:21.322\nWerken means to work.\n\n8\n00:00:21.402 --> 00:00:23.422\nListen to this sentence.\n\n9\n00:00:23.482 --> 00:00:26.302\nIk wil vandaag werken.\n\n10\n00:00:26.482 --> 00:00:28.702\nI want to work today.\n\n11\n00:00:28.742 --> 00:00:31.703\nWij werken elke dag.\n\n12\n00:00:31.823 --> 00:00:34.223\nWe work every day.\n\n13\n00:00:34.303 --> 00:00:37.363\nOur second word is KANTOOR.\n\n14\n00:00:37.423 --> 00:00:40.043\nKantoor means office.\n\n15\n00:00:40.143 --> 00:00:42.583\nLet's use it in sentences.\n\n16\n00:00:42.643 --> 00:00:45.404\nHet kantoor is groot.\n\n17\n00:00:45.424 --> 00:00:47.624\nThe office is big.\n\n18\n00:00:47.704 --> 00:00:50.124\nIk ben op kantoor.\n\n19\n00:00:50.304 --> 00:00:52.324\nI am at the office.\n\n20\n00:00:52.404 --> 00:00:55.764\nOur third word is COLLEGA.\n\n21\n00:00:55.804 --> 00:00:59.625\nCollega means colleague.\n\n22\n00:00:59.665 --> 00:01:03.545\nHere are two example sentences.\n\n23\n00:01:03.585 --> 00:01:07.885\nMijn collega is aardig.\n\n24\n00:01:07.905 --> 00:01:11.386\nMy colleague is nice.\n\n25\n00:01:11.466 --> 00:01:15.286\nIk help mijn collega.\n\n26\n00:01:15.366 --> 00:01:18.486\nI help my colleague.\n\n27\n00:01:18.566 --> 00:01:22.927\nOur fourth word is BAAS.\n\n28\n00:01:22.967 --> 00:01:26.947\nBaas means boss.\n\n29\n00:01:27.027 --> 00:01:30.827\nLet me show you two examples.\n\n30\n00:01:30.867 --> 00:01:35.208\nDe baas is vriendelijk.\n\n31\n00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:38.508\nThe boss is friendly.\n\n32\n00:01:38.608 --> 00:01:42.828\nOnze baas spreekt nu.\n\n33\n00:01:42.928 --> 00:01:46.529\nOur boss is speaking now.\n\n34\n00:01:46.629 --> 00:01:51.489\nOur fifth word is VERGADERING.\n\n35\n00:01:51.529 --> 00:01:55.909\nVergadering means meeting.\n\n36\n00:01:55.989 --> 00:01:59.830\nListen carefully to this sentence.\n\n37\n00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:04.530\nDe vergadering begint zo.\n\n38\n00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:07.990\nThe meeting starts soon.\n\n39\n00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:10.871\nWij hebben een vergadering.\n\n40\n00:02:10.931 --> 00:02:14.291\nWe have a meeting.\n\n41\n00:02:14.371 --> 00:02:19.171\nOur sixth word is SALARIS.\n\n42\n00:02:19.231 --> 00:02:23.372\nSalaris means salary.\n\n43\n00:02:23.412 --> 00:02:26.572\nHere are the examples.\n\n44\n00:02:26.632 --> 00:02:31.712\nHet salaris is goed.\n\n45\n00:02:31.732 --> 00:02:35.213\nThe salary is good.\n\n46\n00:02:35.293 --> 00:02:40.313\nHij krijgt zijn salaris.\n\n47\n00:02:40.373 --> 00:02:44.473\nHe gets his salary.\n\n48\n00:02:44.573 --> 00:02:49.454\nOur seventh word is SOLLICITATIE.\n\n49\n00:02:49.514 --> 00:02:54.254\nSollicitatie means job application.\n\n50\n00:02:54.314 --> 00:02:58.054\nLet's hear two sentences.\n\n51\n00:02:58.114 --> 00:03:03.555\nDe sollicitatie ging goed.\n\n52\n00:03:03.575 --> 00:03:07.595\nThe job application went well.\n\n53\n00:03:07.675 --> 00:03:12.976\nIk schrijf een sollicitatie.\n\n54\n00:03:13.156 --> 00:03:17.056\nI write a job application.\n\n55\n00:03:17.116 --> 00:03:20.896\nLet's recap today's words.\n\n56\n00:03:21.016 --> 00:03:26.937\néén. WERKEN = to work.\n\n57\n00:03:26.977 --> 00:03:33.177\ntwee. KANTOOR = office.\n\n58\n00:03:33.237 --> 00:03:39.178\ndrie. COLLEGA = colleague.\n\n59\n00:03:39.258 --> 00:03:45.318\nvier. BAAS = boss.\n\n60\n00:03:45.398 --> 00:03:51.779\nvijf. VERGADERING = meeting.\n\n61\n00:03:51.859 --> 00:03:57.099\nzes. SALARIS = salary.\n\n62\n00:03:57.179 --> 00:04:03.320\nzeven. SOLLICITATIE = job application.\n\n63\n00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:05.460\nGreat work today!\n\n64\n00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:06.500\nSee you next time!\n
