cw_direction_words	A1A2:common_words	A1A2	🇳🇱 Dutch Common Words #17: Direction Words | A1 Beginners	Richtingen	Direction Words in Dutch	In this lesson we cover: Richtingen (A1-A2 - Common Words)\n\nLearn Dutch from scratch with a clear, slow narrated lesson designed for complete beginners.\n\n---\n\n🗣 Key Phrases\n• naar links\n• naar rechts\n• rechtdoor\n• om de hoek\n• dichtbij\n• ver weg\n\n---\n\n📖 Vocabulary\n• links — left\n• rechts — right\n• rechtdoor — straight ahead\n• om de hoek — around the corner\n• dichtbij — nearby\n• ver weg — far away\n• hier — here\n• daar — there\n• voor — in front of\n• achter — behind\n• naast — next to\n• bij — at / near\n• naar — to / towards\n\n---\n\n📝 Grammar Notes\n- Using Prepositions of Direction in Dutch: Direction words like 'links' and 'rechts' often combine with 'naar' when indicating movement (e.g., 'naar links' = to the left). Position words like 'voor', 'achter', and 'naast' are used directly before nouns with 'het' or 'de'.\n\nPattern Breakdown\n- Ga naar links. (Go to the left.)\n\nMini Examples\n- Ga naar links. (Go to the left.)\n- Het huis is naast de bank. (The house is next to the bank.)\n\n---\n\n#LearnDutch #Dutch #DutchForBeginners #DutchIn5Minutes #Nederlandse #DutchLesson #A1-A2Dutch\n	bLRJcUd4v_I	390	Speaker1: Hello everyone! Speaker1: Welcome to our Dutch direction lesson. Speaker1: Welkom bij de les! Speaker1: Welcome to the lesson! Speaker1: Today we learn words for giving directions. Speaker1: This helps you find your way. Speaker1: Are you ready to learn? Speaker1: Laten we nu beginnen! Speaker1: Let us start now! Speaker1: Our first word is LINKS. Speaker1: LINKS means left in English. Speaker1: Ga hier naar links. Speaker1: Go left here. Speaker1: Het museum is links. Speaker1: The museum is on the left. Speaker1: Remember that LINKS means left. Speaker1: Our second word is RECHTS. Speaker1: RECHTS means right in English. Speaker1: Sla af naar rechts. Speaker1: Turn to the right. Speaker1: De bus staat rechts. Speaker1: The bus is on the right. Speaker1: So RECHTS is right. Speaker1: Next we have RECHTDOOR. Speaker1: RECHTDOOR means straight ahead. Speaker1: Ga gewoon rechtdoor. Speaker1: Just go straight ahead. Speaker1: Loop honderd meter rechtdoor. Speaker1: Walk one hundred meters straight. Speaker1: RECHTDOOR means straight ahead. Speaker1: Our fourth phrase is OM DE HOEK. Speaker1: This phrase means around the corner. Speaker1: De bakker is om de hoek. Speaker1: The bakery is around the corner. Speaker1: Het café is om de hoek. Speaker1: The cafe is around the corner. Speaker1: OM DE HOEK is around the corner. Speaker1: Next is the word DICHTBIJ. Speaker1: DICHTBIJ means nearby or close. Speaker1: De school is dichtbij. Speaker1: The school is nearby. Speaker1: Mijn huis is heel dichtbij. Speaker1: My house is very close. Speaker1: DICHTBIJ means close or nearby. Speaker1: Now let us learn VER WEG. Speaker1: VER WEG means far away. Speaker1: Het station is ver weg. Speaker1: The station is far away. Speaker1: De stad is ver weg. Speaker1: The city is far away. Speaker1: VER WEG means far away. Speaker1: Our seventh word is HIER. Speaker1: HIER simply means here. Speaker1: Stop hier even. Speaker1: Stop here for a moment. Speaker1: Ik ben hier nu. Speaker1: I am here now. Speaker1: HIER is easy, it means here. Speaker1: Next we learn the word DAAR. Speaker1: DAAR means there in English. Speaker1: Kijk maar daar. Speaker1: Just look over there. Speaker1: De trein staat daar. Speaker1: The train is over there. Speaker1: DAAR means there. Speaker1: Now let us look at VOOR. Speaker1: VOOR means in front of. Speaker1: Ik sta voor het park. Speaker1: I stand in front of the park. Speaker1: De auto staat voor de deur. Speaker1: The car is in front of the door. Speaker1: VOOR means in front of. Speaker1: Our tenth word is ACHTER. Speaker1: ACHTER means behind. Speaker1: De tuin is achter het huis. Speaker1: The garden is behind the house. Speaker1: Hij loopt