cw_emotions	A1A2:common_words	A1A2	🇳🇱 Dutch Common Words #27: Emotions | A1 Beginners	Emoties in het Nederlands	Emotions in Dutch	In this lesson we cover: Emoties in het Nederlands (A1-A2 - Common Words)\n\nLearn Dutch from scratch with a clear, slow narrated lesson designed for complete beginners.\n\n---\n\n🗣 Key Phrases\n• Hoe voel jij je vandaag?\n• Ik ben blij.\n• Waarom ben je verdrietig?\n• Ik ben bang voor...\n\n---\n\n📖 Vocabulary\n• blij — happy\n• verdrietig — sad\n• boos — angry\n• bang — afraid\n• moe — tired\n• ziek — sick\n• gelukkig — happy / fortunate\n• nerveus — nervous\n\n---\n\n📝 Grammar Notes\n- Expressing feelings with 'zijn': In Dutch, emotion adjectives are commonly used with the verb 'zijn' (to be).\n\nPattern Breakdown\n- Ik ben blij.\n\nMini Examples\n- Ik ben blij.\n- Hij is moe.\n\n---\n\n#LearnDutch #Dutch #DutchForBeginners #DutchIn5Minutes #Nederlandse #DutchLesson #A1-A2Dutch\n	wzzGgxRi0W4	246	Speaker1: Welcome to today's Dutch lesson! Speaker1: Today we will learn common emotion words. Speaker1: Hoe voel jij je vandaag? Speaker1: How do you feel today? Speaker1: Laten we beginnen! Speaker1: Let's begin! Speaker1: Our first word is for happy: blij. Speaker1: Ik ben vandaag erg blij. Speaker1: I am very happy today. Speaker1: De kinderen zijn heel blij. Speaker1: The children are very happy. Speaker1: Great job! Let's try the next word. Speaker1: Our second word is for sad: verdrietig. Speaker1: Waarom ben je verdrietig? Speaker1: Why are you sad? Speaker1: Het kind is heel verdrietig. Speaker1: The child is very sad. Speaker1: Now, let's learn the word for angry: boos. Speaker1: De man is erg boos. Speaker1: The man is very angry. Speaker1: Hij is boos op mij. Speaker1: He is angry with me. Speaker1: Next, we have the word for afraid or scared: bang. Speaker1: Ik ben bang voor honden. Speaker1: I am afraid of dogs. Speaker1: Ben jij ook bang? Speaker1: Are you afraid too? Speaker1: You are doing wonderful! Speaker1: Now let's learn t