un. Speaker1: De zon schijnt vandaag. Speaker1: The sun shines today. Speaker1: Ik hou van de zon. Speaker1: I love the sun. Speaker1: Zon means sun. Speaker1: Our fifth word is maan. Speaker1: Maan means moon. Speaker1: De maan schijnt 's nachts. Speaker1: The moon shines at night. Speaker1: Ik zie de witte maan. Speaker1: I see the white moon. Speaker1: Maan means moon. Speaker1: Our sixth word is lucht. Speaker1: Lucht means sky or air. Speaker1: De lucht is heel blauw. Speaker1: The sky is very blue. Speaker1: Vogels vliegen in de lucht. Speaker1: Birds fly in the sky. Speaker1: Lucht means sky. Speaker1: Excellent! Speaker1: Next, let's learn about water and land. Speaker1: Our seventh word is zee. Speaker1: Zee means sea. Speaker1: De zee is erg koud. Speaker1: The sea is very cold. Speaker1: Wij zwemmen in de zee. Speaker1: We swim in the sea. Speaker1: Zee means sea. Speaker1: Our eighth word is rivier. Speaker1: Rivier means river. Speaker1: De rivier is heel lang. Speaker1: The river is very long. Speaker1: Vissen zwemmen in de rivier. Speaker1: Fish swim in the river. Speaker1: Rivier means river. Speaker1: Our ninth word is berg. Speaker1: Berg means mountain. Speaker1: De berg is heel hoog. Speaker1: The mountain is very high. Speaker1: Wij klimmen op de berg. Speaker1: We climb on the mountain. Speaker1: Berg means mountain. Speaker1: Time for a quick recap! Speaker1: Vandaag leerden we nieuwe woorden. Speaker1: Today we learned new words. Speaker1: Boom, bloem, gras, zon en maan. Speaker1: Tree, flower, grass, sun and moon. Speaker1: En ook lucht, zee, rivier, berg. Speaker1: And also sky, sea, river, mountain. Speaker1: You did a fantastic job today! Speaker1: Practice these words often. Speaker1: See you in the next lesson!	17	f	\N	2026-08-18 18:51:29.654518+00
cw_negative_indefinites	A1A2:common_words	A1A2	🇳🇱 Dutch Common Words #30: Negative Words | A1 Beginners	Negatieve Woorden	Negative Words	In this lesson we cover: Negatieve Woorden (A1-A2 - Common Words)\n\nLearn Dutch from scratch with a clear, slow narrated lesson designed for complete beginners.\n\n---\n\n🗣 Key Phrases\n• niemand in het huis\n• ik zie niets\n• nergens te vinden\n• ik kom nooit te laat\n• bijna klaar\n• nauwelijks horen\n\n---\n\n📖 Vocabulary\n• niemand — nobody / no one\n• niets — nothing\n• nergens — nowhere\n• nooit — never\n• bijna — almost\n• nauwelijks — hardly / barely\n\n---\n\n📝 Grammar Notes\n- Negative Words in Dutch: In Dutch, 'niemand', 'niets', 'nergens', and 'nooit' are absolute negative terms for people, things, places, and time. 'Bijna' and 'nauwelijks' express degree or limited amount.\n\nPattern Breakdown\n- Er is niemand. (There is nobody.)\n\nMini Examples\n- Er is niemand. (There is nobody.)\n- Ik zie niets. (I see nothing.)\n\n---\n\n#LearnDutch #Dutch #DutchForBeginners #DutchIn5Minutes #Nederlandse #DutchLesson #A1-A2Dutch\n	nXAqSIG3ByM	268	Speaker1: Welcome to today's Dutch lesson! Speaker1: Today we will learn negative words. Speaker1: Words like nobody, nothing, and never. Speaker1: These words are very useful in daily life. Speaker1: Are you ready to begin? Speaker1: Laten we beginnen! Speaker1: Let's start! Speaker1: Our first word is NIEMAND, which means nobody. Speaker1: Er is niemand in het huis. Speaker1: There is nobody in the house. Speaker1: Niemand weet het antwoord vandaag. Speaker1: Nobody knows the answer today. Speaker1: Ik zie niemand op straat. Speaker1: I see nobody in the street. Speaker1: Our next word is NIETS, which means nothing. Speaker1: Ik zie niets in het donker. Speaker1: I see nothing in the dark. Speaker1: Hij zegt niets tegen mij. Speaker1: He says nothing to me. Speaker1: Er is niets te doen hier. Speaker1: There is nothing to do here. Speaker1: Now let's learn NERGENS, which means nowhere.