grammar_want_omdat	A1A2:grammar	A1A2	🇳🇱 Dutch Grammar #19: Want & Omdat (Word Order) | A1-A2 Beginners	Want versus Omdat	Word Order with Want and Omdat	In this lesson we cover: Want versus Omdat (A1-A2 - Grammar)\n\nLearn Dutch from scratch with a clear, slow narrated lesson designed for complete beginners.\n\n---\n\n🗣 Key Phrases\n• want en omdat\n• ik heb honger\n• omdat ik ziek ben\n\n---\n\n📖 Vocabulary\n• want — because (coordinating)\n• omdat — because (subordinating)\n• honger — hunger\n• dorst — thirst\n• ziek — sick\n• thuis — home / at home\n\n---\n\n📝 Grammar Notes\n- Want vs Omdat word order: 'Want' is a coordinating conjunction, which means it joins two main clauses together. The word order in the second clause remains standard: Subject + Verb + Rest. 'Omdat' is a subordinating conjunction, which introduces a subordinate clause. This kicks the working verb to the very end of the clause.\n\nPattern Breakdown\n- Ik werk niet want ik ben ziek. (I do not work because I am sick.)\n\nMini Examples\n- Ik werk niet want ik ben ziek. (I do not work because I am sick.)\n- Ik werk niet omdat ik ziek ben. (I do not work because I am sick.)\n\n---\n\n#LearnDutch #Dutch #DutchForBeginners #DutchIn5Minutes #Nederlandse #DutchLesson #A1-A2Dutch\n	uS3UOM6dpuI	273	Speaker1: Imagine you are late for work. Speaker1: You must explain why. Speaker1: You need the word 'because'. Speaker1: In Dutch, we have two words. Speaker1: They are: want and omdat. Speaker1: They both mean because. Speaker1: But they change the word order. Speaker1: Laten we beginnen! Speaker1: Let us begin! Speaker1: First, we look at want. Speaker1: Want keeps the normal order. Speaker1: Let us see an example. Speaker1: Ik eet want ik heb honger. Speaker1: I eat because I am hungry. Speaker1: Notice the verb heb is second. Speaker1: Now, let's look at omdat. Speaker1: Omdat sends the verb to the end. Speaker1: Let us see the same sentence. Speaker1: Ik eet omdat ik honger heb. Speaker1: I eat because I 