vocab_nature_outdoor	A1A2:vocabulary	A1A2	🇳🇱 Dutch Vocabulary #17: Nature & Outdoors | A1 Beginners	Natuur en Buiten	Nature and Outdoors	In this lesson we cover: Natuur en Buiten (A1-A2 - Vocabulary)\n\nLearn Dutch from scratch with a clear, slow narrated lesson designed for complete beginners.\n\n---\n\n🗣 Key Phrases\n• in het bos\n• op het strand\n• de natuur is mooi\n• graag wandelen\n\n---\n\n📖 Vocabulary\n• natuur — nature\n• bos — forest\n• strand — beach\n• duin — dune\n• polder — polder\n• wandelen — to walk\n• vogels — birds\n\n---\n\n📝 Grammar Notes\n- Articles with Nature Nouns: In Dutch, nouns take either 'de' or 'het'. 'De' is used for 'natuur', 'polder', and plural nouns like 'vogels'. 'Het' is used for 'bos', 'strand', and 'duin'.\n\nPattern Breakdown\n- de natuur (the nature)\n\nMini Examples\n- de natuur (the nature)\n- het bos (the forest)\n\n---\n\n#LearnDutch #Dutch #DutchForBeginners #DutchIn5Minutes #Nederlandse #DutchLesson #A1-A2Dutch\n	7fMjsyOGBPA	271	Speaker1: Welcome to today's Dutch lesson. Speaker1: Today we explore nature and outdoors. Speaker1: Dutch nature is very beautiful. Speaker1: Let's learn seven words together. Speaker1: Laten we nu beginnen! Speaker1: Let's get started now! Speaker1: Our first word is NATUUR. Speaker1: Natuur means nature in English. Speaker1: Listen to this example sentence. Speaker1: De natuur is hier heel mooi. Speaker1: Nature is very beautiful here. Speaker1: Ik hou van de natuur. Speaker1: I love nature very much. Speaker1: Our second word is BOS. Speaker1: Bos means forest in English. Speaker1: Let me show you a sentence. Speaker1: Het bos is erg groot. Speaker1: The forest is very big. Speaker1: Wij lopen in het bos. Speaker1: We are walking in the forest. Speaker1: Our third word is STRAND. Speaker1: Strand means beach in English. Speaker1: Let's try a new sentence. Speaker1: Het strand is erg mooi. Speaker1: The beach is very beautiful. Speaker1: Ik ben op het strand. Speaker1: I am on the beach now.