vocab_school_items	A1A2:vocabulary	A1A2	🇳🇱 Dutch Vocabulary #11: School Items | A1 Beginners	Schoolspullen	School Items	In this lesson we cover: Schoolspullen (A1 - Vocabulary)\n\nLearn Dutch from scratch with a clear, slow narrated lesson designed for complete beginners.\n\n---\n\n🗣 Key Phrases\n• Het boek is rood.\n• Ik heb een pen.\n• Ik schrijf in het schrift.\n• Mijn tas is groot.\n\n---\n\n📖 Vocabulary\n• boek — book\n• pen — pen\n• potlood — pencil\n• schrift — notebook\n• tas — bag\n• gum — eraser\n\n---\n\n📝 Grammar Notes\n- Articles with School Items (De vs Het): In Dutch, every noun is either a 'de' word or a 'het' word. Learn each noun with its definite article.\n\nPattern Breakdown\n- het boek (the book)\n\nMini Examples\n- het boek (the book)\n- het potlood (the pencil)\n\n---\n\n#LearnDutch #Dutch #DutchForBeginners #DutchIn5Minutes #Nederlandse #DutchLesson #A1Dutch\n	TgjGJ3UF_sU	\N	Speaker1: Welcome to Dutch vocabulary class! Speaker1: Today we learn school items. Speaker1: Are you ready? Speaker1: Laten we beginnen! Speaker1: Let's start! Speaker1: School items are very useful. Speaker1: You use them every day. Speaker1: Our first word is BOEK. Speaker1: Boek means book in English. Speaker1: Het boek is rood. Speaker1: The book is red. Speaker1: Ik lees een boek. Speaker1: I read a book. Speaker1: Dit is mijn boek. Speaker1: This is my book. Speaker1: Our next word is PEN. Speaker1: Pen means pen in English. Speaker1: Ik heb een pen. Speaker1: I have a pen. Speaker1: De pen is blauw. Speaker1: The pen is blue. Speaker1: Waar is de pen? Speaker1: Where is the pen? Speaker1: Our third word is POTLOOD. Speaker1: Potlood means pencil in English. Speaker1: Ik teken met potlood. Speaker1: I draw with pencil. Speaker1: Het potlood is geel. Speaker1: The pencil is yellow. Speaker1: Het potlood is klein. Speaker1: The pencil is small. Speaker1: Our fourth word is SCHRIFT. Speaker1: Schrift means notebook in English. Speaker1: Ik schrijf in het schrift. Spea