vocab_time	A1A2:vocabulary	A1A2	🇳🇱 Dutch Vocabulary #9: Time Expressions | A1 Beginners	Woorden over Tijd	Time Expressions	In this lesson we cover: Woorden over Tijd (A1 - Vocabulary)\n\nLearn Dutch from scratch with a clear, slow narrated lesson designed for complete beginners.\n\n---\n\n🗣 Key Phrases\n• nu\n• later\n• vandaag\n• morgen\n• gisteren\n• vroeg\n• laat\n\n---\n\n📖 Vocabulary\n• nu — now\n• later — later\n• vandaag — today\n• morgen — tomorrow\n• gisteren — yesterday\n• vroeg — early\n• laat — late\n\n---\n\n📝 Grammar Notes\n- Position of Time Expressions: In Dutch sentences, time adverbs like 'vandaag', 'morgen', or 'gisteren' typically follow the main verb in basic sentence structures.\n\nPattern Breakdown\n- Ik werk vandaag niet.\n\nMini Examples\n- Ik werk vandaag niet.\n- Gisteren was ik thuis.\n\n---\n\n#LearnDutch #Dutch #DutchForBeginners #DutchIn5Minutes #Nederlandse #DutchLesson #A1Dutch\n	A9jp6K_gnrY	\N	Speaker1: Welcome to today's Dutch vocabulary lesson! Speaker1: Today we will learn about time. Speaker1: Time expressions are very useful in Dutch. Speaker1: Laten we beginnen! Speaker1: Let's get started! Speaker1: Our first word is NU. Speaker1: Nu means now in English. Speaker1: Ik kom nu naar huis. Speaker1: I am coming home now. Speaker1: Wat doe je nu? Speaker1: What are you doing now? Speaker1: Our second word is LATER. Speaker1: Later means later in English. Speaker1: Tot later mijn vriend! Speaker1: See you later my friend! Speaker1: Wij eten later vandaag. Speaker1: We eat later today. Speaker1: Our third word is VANDAAG. Speaker1: Vandaag means today in English. Speaker1: Vandaag is het mooi weer. Speaker1: Today the weather is nice. Speaker1: Ik werk vandaag niet. Speaker1: I am not working today. Speaker1: Next, we have the word MORGEN. Speaker1: Morgen means tomorrow in English. Speaker1: Zie ik je morgen? Speaker1: Do I see you tomorrow? Speaker1: Morgen is een nieuwe dag. Speaker1: Tomorrow is a new day. Speaker1: Our fifth word is GISTEREN. Speaker1: Gisteren means yesterday in English. Speaker1: Gisteren was ik thuis. Speaker1: Yesterday I was at home. Speaker1: Het regende gisteren heel hard. Speaker1: It rained very hard yesterday. Speaker1: Now, let's learn VROEG. Speaker1: Vroeg means early in English. Speaker1: Ik sta vroeg op. Speaker1: I get up early. Speaker1: De trein komt vroeg aan. Speaker1: The train arrives early. Speaker1: Our last word is LAAT. Speaker1: Laat means late in English. Speaker1: Het is al erg laat. Speaker1: It is already very late. Speaker1: Waarom ben je zo laat? Speaker1: Why are you so late? Speaker1: Let's recap today's words. Speaker1: één. NU = now. Speaker1: twee. LATER = later. Speaker1: drie. VANDAAG = today. Speaker1: vier. MORGEN = tomorrow. Speaker1: vijf. GISTEREN = yesterday. Speaker1: zes. VROEG = early. Speaker1: zeven. LAAT = late. Speaker1: Great work today!	9	f	\N	2026-08-18 18:51:29.654518+00
vocab_transport	A1A2:vocabulary	A1A2	🇳🇱 Dutch Vocabulary #10: Transport | A1 Beginners	Het Vervoer	Dutch Transport Vocabulary	In this lesson we cover: Het Vervoer (A1 - Vocabulary)\n\nLearn Dutch from scratch with a clear, slow narrated lesson designed for complete beginners.\n\n---\n\n🗣 Key Phrases\n• de trein\n• de bus\n• de fiets\n• de auto\n• het vliegtuig\n\n---\n\n📖 Vocabulary\n• trein — train\n• bus — bus\n• fiets — bicycle\n• auto — car\n• tram — tram\n• metro — metro\n• vliegtuig — airplane\n\n---\n\n📝 Grammar Notes\n- Articles for Transport Words: Most vehicles in Dutch use 'de' (de trein, de bus, de fiets, de auto, de tram, de metro). One main exception is 'het vliegtuig' (the airplane).\n- Traveling 'by' a vehicle: To express traveling by a transport mode in Dutch, use the preposition 'met' followed by the article and vehicle.\n\nPattern Breakdown\n- de trein (the train)\n- met de trein (by train)\n\nMini Examples\n- de trein (the train)\n- de fiets (the bicycle)\n- met de trein (by train)\n- met de bus (by bus)\n\n---\n\n#LearnDutch #Dutch #DutchForBeginners #DutchIn5Minutes #Nederlandse #DutchLesson #A1Dutch\n	L_Hoq51ep1A	\N	Speaker1: Welcome to today's lesson! Speaker1: Today we learn about transport. Speaker1: Transport in Dutch is vervoer. Speaker1: Laten we beginnen! Speaker1: Let's start! Speaker1: We will learn seven transport words today. Speaker1: Our first word is TREIN. Speaker1: Trein means train in English. Speaker1: De trein komt nu. Speaker1: The train is coming now. Speaker1: Ik reis met de trein. Speaker1: I travel by train. Speaker1: Our second word is BUS. Speaker1: Bus means bus in English. Speaker1: De bus is erg laat. Speaker1: The bus is very late. Speaker1: Wij nemen de bus. Speaker1: We take the bus. Speaker1: Next, we have FIETS. Speaker1: Fiets means bicycle in English. Speaker1: Ik heb een rode fiets. Speaker1: I have a red bicycle. Speaker1: Zij rijdt op de fiets. Speaker1: She rides on the bicycle. Speaker1: Our fourth word